    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-009",
      "text": "Because net asset value drives subscriptions, redemptions, performance calculations, advertising, and fees, managers who both manage and value the portfolio have both an incentive and the ability to inappropriately over-value their portfolios.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where the manager performs or controls valuation",
        "where NAV is the basis for fees and performance figures"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Given the conflicting responsibilities, managers have an incentive and the ability to inappropriately over-value their portfolios.27",
      "text_sha256": "2d1800a2a57a91a4f31c8441d437e2269a285cbf9ce3a7ebf06ac8e4c2996d24",
      "source_sha256": "6aa3a280dc6750723be2389f3af2aabf3a16c4ce20e49fcdaddd7f2ea95a67aa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-012",
      "text": "There is an adverse selection problem in independent valuation: an administrator who actually had the knowledge and understanding of complex instruments required for the task would probably be incentivized to use that expertise in a more profitable setting instead.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "economics",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "for administrators valuing highly complex instruments"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Had the administrator the required knowledge and understanding of the complexities, he or she would probably be incentivized to use that experience and understanding in a more profitable setting.",
      "text_sha256": "599b9519599dc1749d03fec447a859cec3c2dc39be3db5c163b4acde74da34e1",
      "source_sha256": "6aa3a280dc6750723be2389f3af2aabf3a16c4ce20e49fcdaddd7f2ea95a67aa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-021",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-021",
      "text": "The principal-agent problem in complex financial products is exacerbated by hierarchies in financial institutions, which create multiple layers of agency relationships between the traders using the products and the principals bearing the real economic risk.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "in banks and large institutions trading complex financial products"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-021:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The principal-agent problem is further exacerbated by hierarchies in financial institutions that often create multiple layers of agency relationships to trade and invest in complex financial products.",
      "text_sha256": "dac92a34fc90061d876e593b1c162d6e8d5790c00c8cee3d47d798ea106a9825",
      "source_sha256": "6aa3a280dc6750723be2389f3af2aabf3a16c4ce20e49fcdaddd7f2ea95a67aa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-023",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-023",
      "text": "Because rating agencies are paid by CDO issuers while the ratings' main users are buyers, the agency as agent has an incentive to issue high ratings to satisfy its issuer principal, and the buyer has no means of controlling the agency other than through its relationship with the issuer.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "under the issuer-pays model for structured finance ratings"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-023:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The rating agency as the agent would probably have an incentive to issue high ratings to satisfy the issuer of a CDO as its principal. The buyer as the beneficiary of the rating has no means of controlling the rating agencies and its ratings other than through its relationship with the issuer.",
      "text_sha256": "9a0f35d01fe49c3abd6fc8958faaced94d85486baccb71aa7b07bf8bb6b55de5",
      "source_sha256": "6aa3a280dc6750723be2389f3af2aabf3a16c4ce20e49fcdaddd7f2ea95a67aa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-024",
      "text": "The issuer-buyer relationship and the incentives inside it are unlikely to be able to adequately control the principal-agent relationship between issuer and rating agency so as to ensure accurate ratings.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "compliance",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "under the issuer-pays rating model for CDOs"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "It seems unlikely that the issuer-buyer relationship and the incentives inherent within could adequately control the principal-agent relationship between issuer and rating agency to ensure accurate ratings.",
      "text_sha256": "e89c8c9fea16c5560b7390ad01ea818cb4f96f4dfaac226965ac2fe1b7466088",
      "source_sha256": "6aa3a280dc6750723be2389f3af2aabf3a16c4ce20e49fcdaddd7f2ea95a67aa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-025",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-025",
      "text": "Qualified investors have strong incentives to accept valuation problems rather than contest them, because contesting would jeopardize their relationships with management and other industry participants and damage their own reputations.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "qualified investors with industry relationships and reputational stakes"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Even though their preference may be to obtain accurate valuation when needed, they have strong incentives to accept valuation problems in order to maintain the relationships with management and other industry participants and protect their reputations. Managers are also dependent on their",
      "text_sha256": "e30e3a2687faa0322554154cde2ae4242fa465e32e9cf9af328d8460079ba05b",
      "source_sha256": "6aa3a280dc6750723be2389f3af2aabf3a16c4ce20e49fcdaddd7f2ea95a67aa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-030",
      "text": "Unless an investor's business is primarily to invest in hard-to-value assets, that investor's sophistication cannot be assumed regardless of personal wealth.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "for investments in hard-to-value assets and complex financial instruments"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Unless the business of an investor is to primarily invest in certain hard-to-value assets, the sophistication of such investor can probably not be assumed, regardless of personal wealth. Investors who could",
      "text_sha256": "a21675269963cc913e108ccf34161d9ccd5ea488774f068591ecfcefc897aabd",
      "source_sha256": "6aa3a280dc6750723be2389f3af2aabf3a16c4ce20e49fcdaddd7f2ea95a67aa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-031",
      "text": "Raising the Regulation D numerical tests by adding an investable assets requirement would probably not address how to remedy investors' lack of understanding of hard-to-value assets.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "securities-law",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "under the SEC proposal to add a 2.5 million dollar investments requirement"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "raising the numerical tests by adding an investable assets requirement236 would probably not address the question of how the lack of understanding of certain hard-to-value assets could be addressed.",
      "text_sha256": "c3ce62985b9908babbdd66a7798af313764d102087b784c79806b6452e1b4f6e",
      "source_sha256": "6aa3a280dc6750723be2389f3af2aabf3a16c4ce20e49fcdaddd7f2ea95a67aa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-032",
      "text": "More disclosure does not always mean better governance, because the information provided may be hard to assess and evaluate.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where disclosed valuation and risk data is complex"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "More disclosure may not, however, always mean better governance if the information provided is hard to assess and evaluate.",
      "text_sha256": "4aeecb5180ae8f20bb7bb712df251d8e24f32b74ee6181a684037cb3740f6be5",
      "source_sha256": "6aa3a280dc6750723be2389f3af2aabf3a16c4ce20e49fcdaddd7f2ea95a67aa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1428387-039",
      "text": "Investor suitability standards would address the sophistication problem by requiring independent verification that investors in highly complex financial products can evaluate investment risk independently and are capable of making independent investment decisions.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "economics",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "dynamic-regulation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "for investments in highly complex financial products"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1428387-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Investor suitability standards would address these concerns by requiring independent verification that investors in highly complex financial products have the capability to evaluate investment risk independently and are capable of making independent investment decisions.",
      "text_sha256": "f1f7a8120beee7472fb0712dc827dcdd29af2fbddc0149a485358832628ffc55",
      "source_sha256": "6aa3a280dc6750723be2389f3af2aabf3a16c4ce20e49fcdaddd7f2ea95a67aa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1558614-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1558614-013",
      "text": "Limited liability lets managers and shareholders capture most of the benefits of excessive risk taking while not bearing all of its costs, which is one explanation for why bankers take excessive risk.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "corporation protected by limited liability",
        "corporation may lack assets sufficient to pay creditors"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1558614-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Accordingly, both managers and shareholders of a corporation enjoy most of the benefits of excessive 62 risk taking but do not bear all of the costs.",
      "text_sha256": "feb93c6cfecd0628de36dac683d958120caf778453fb0061f04f869043958077",
      "source_sha256": "e898211630f4116879329d6de8397523dca5b066864147421aa5cbc7429dc83b",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1558614-014",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1558614-014",
      "text": "The U.S. governance structure, built on periodic disclosure of performance data and stock price maximization, encourages risk taking because managers feel compelled to meet shareholder expectations at every reporting interval.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "disclosure",
        "corporate-governance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "governance systems that emphasize periodic performance disclosure and stock price"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1558614-014:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Risk taking in this context may be encour- aged by the perceived need to satisfy expectations of shareholders. Managers feel compelled to fulfill performance expectations whenev- er results are disclosed, be it quarterly, bi-annually, or annually.",
      "text_sha256": "15521f837ecf9c294d1826e26992b3fdd3674d2995300f6749286b3c003a9c4d",
      "source_sha256": "e898211630f4116879329d6de8397523dca5b066864147421aa5cbc7429dc83b",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1558614-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1558614-015",
      "text": "German corporate law's historical focus on conflicts between controlling and minority shareholders leaves it poorly equipped to address managerial abuse of power, including excessive risk taking by managers.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "corporate-governance",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "systems where ownership is concentrated and the central conflict is shareholder against shareholder"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1558614-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Ar- guably, a legal system that focuses on the interaction of controlling and minority shareholders is not as well equipped to deal with mana- gerial abuse of power, including excessive risk taking by managers.",
      "text_sha256": "658c6fa4e5bce137824a0865df97e514934dc03689f723cc288837ae03263498",
      "source_sha256": "e898211630f4116879329d6de8397523dca5b066864147421aa5cbc7429dc83b",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1558614-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1558614-018",
      "text": "Codetermination makes the German supervisory board's decision making more cumbersome, so a co determined Aufsichtsrat may not respond quickly enough to fast moving events such as an escalation of portfolio risk or a liquidity crisis.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "corporate-governance",
        "compliance",
        "defi",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "corporations large enough to trigger employee representation on the supervisory board",
        "employee representatives may also carry union political objectives"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
