    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1806252-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Even assuming that systemic implications arise from hedge fund investing, systemic risk is such a multifaceted issue that it could require the involvement of more than one regulator in one jurisdiction.",
      "text_sha256": "335f26a6e94030d1858133e7a72b5f882307871881e362f9b7e28f05adf8bf45",
      "source_sha256": "3343ebfe05a925c3d1a75625c4b351ccff515c50819a48d155804daacf01429d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1806252-020",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1806252-020",
      "text": "Discrimination against non-EU jurisdictions under the AIFM Directive could provoke retaliatory action, and retaliation combined with a lack of intra-European cooperation could damage the European financial services industry and the whole European economy.",
      "claim_type": "predictive",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "obstacles to EU market access for non-EU funds and managers persist"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1806252-020:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Discrimination against non-EU jurisdictions could provoke retaliatory action. As a consequence, retaliatory actions and a lack of intra-European cooperation could damage the European financial services industry and the whole European economy.",
      "text_sha256": "c7d5e007f199d553d508b3c812ddc054939c685c66c22aacb2b4826d5a0395b8",
      "source_sha256": "3343ebfe05a925c3d1a75625c4b351ccff515c50819a48d155804daacf01429d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1806252-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1806252-028",
      "text": "A standard objection to indirect regulation is that counterparty credit risk management will not work effectively unless the lending bank has an exclusive relationship with the hedge fund that lets it control the relationship.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "a hedge fund borrows from more than one bank, so no single bank sees its overall risk exposure"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1806252-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "CCRM will not work effectively unless the bank has an exclusive relationship with the hedge fund that allows it to control the relationship.",
      "text_sha256": "dd8d7d4798f0c08e596a91e2ca2a6212d697cce321ef3be670184618e95c2d2c",
      "source_sha256": "3343ebfe05a925c3d1a75625c4b351ccff515c50819a48d155804daacf01429d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1806252-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1806252-031",
      "text": "Banks' role in monitoring hedge funds is not easily comparable to the principal agent problem between securities buyers and credit rating agencies, because banks have more influence over hedge funds than securities buyers have over rating agencies and their ratings.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance",
        "systemic-risk",
        "compliance",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1806252-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Banks have perhaps more influence over hedge funds than buyers of securities over credit rating agencies and their ratings.",
      "text_sha256": "e5b3a823e36248a1a23e0b790b77eb60abdcfbf1c64cab909aaa6be5fb45d409",
      "source_sha256": "3343ebfe05a925c3d1a75625c4b351ccff515c50819a48d155804daacf01429d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1806252-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1806252-032",
      "text": "The numerical wealth requirements used to define qualified hedge fund investors fail as a regulatory device, because investors who meet the wealth thresholds do not always have the knowledge, understanding, and sophistication needed to invest in highly complex financial instruments.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "accredited investor standards under Regulation D and PFIARA"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1806252-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The policy fails to take into account investors who technically fulfill the numerical wealth requirements but lack an adequate level of financial sophistication.",
      "text_sha256": "6aa70850368b2f0f3c091335bf0d62d1fc34a4ea07cb0ba8f8815bbafc05cce5",
      "source_sha256": "3343ebfe05a925c3d1a75625c4b351ccff515c50819a48d155804daacf01429d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-006",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1908473-006",
      "text": "The second trigger, which increases voting rights before resolution, should fire on evidence that conversion into equity was unsuccessful, that conversion came too early or too late, or that the firm's financial performance keeps trending downward.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "contingent-capital",
        "governance-design",
        "systemic-risk"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Applies after the first trigger has already converted debt into equity",
        "Applies before authorities initiate resolution"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-006:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Increasing the voting rights pre-resolution could be triggered by evidence that the conversion into equity was not successful, that conversion was triggered too early or too late, or that there is an overall continuing downward trend in the financial performance of the company.",
      "text_sha256": "183a3383badada022d9ef3693d74ffd884267617387beee63f12e051fe6a0e06",
      "source_sha256": "9d578dac663357529edd1f6453fcfe69bdc59ac882408d9edfde5a4c2916befa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1908473-010",
      "text": "Contingent capital offers only limited protection against information asymmetries, principal and agent conflicts, and collective action problems, so it cannot by itself prevent economic failure.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance",
        "institutional-design",
        "contingent-capital"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Contingent capital can only limitedly protect against information asymmetries, principal/agent issues, and collective action problems.",
      "text_sha256": "e15a5caa9a8f1c20e41649ef2faf4f33b28c50e3020dc0b4d82d706bc617bc3f",
      "source_sha256": "9d578dac663357529edd1f6453fcfe69bdc59ac882408d9edfde5a4c2916befa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-011",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1908473-011",
      "text": "Existing proposals for implementing contingent capital do not explain how they would address the information asymmetries and principal and agent problems that may lie at the core of the credit crisis.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance",
        "contingent-capital"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Assumes information asymmetries and principal agent problems were central causes of the crisis"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-011:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Although contingent capital has many beneficial attributes, existing proposals for implementing contingent capital are unclear as to how they will address information asymmetries and principal/agent problems.",
      "text_sha256": "bb62b49e8b2ac2fff5cfe6a8c1f1b6d1129285630f2fcb9c8315b0b647ae8961",
      "source_sha256": "9d578dac663357529edd1f6453fcfe69bdc59ac882408d9edfde5a4c2916befa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-014",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1908473-014",
      "text": "The incentive effects of corporate governance controls may not operate in systemically important financial institutions, because managers and owners who anticipate a bailout commitment adjust their risk preferences upward.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "systemic-risk",
        "governance-design",
        "corporate-governance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Applies to institutions considered too big to fail"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-014:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "the incentives originating from corporate governance controls may not work in SIFIs. SIFIs are often considered too big to fail and may be bailed out.108 If that is the case, SIFI principals-managers-owners may anticipate a bailout commitment and adjust their risk preferences upwards.",
      "text_sha256": "d3e09218fd7bbb1c30818329724dea8e7016257b39e2062dbea623b01ecdcf30",
      "source_sha256": "9d578dac663357529edd1f6453fcfe69bdc59ac882408d9edfde5a4c2916befa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1908473-024",
      "text": "Departing from Coffee's design, super-voting rights should be allocated to contingent capital holders only if the first trigger failed to improve the institution's financial health; at the first trigger the new shareholder gets one vote per share.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "contingent-capital"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Voting rights escalate only on a continuing downward trend after the first conversion"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Although we agree with the need for increased voting rights, the proposal in this Article would allocate super-voting rights to CCS holders only if the first trigger did not result in an improvement of the financial institution's financial health.",
      "text_sha256": "140793a7dfd2d610b167695f4fced669b7d953847419d1f3a50ab75f1b58cd73",
      "source_sha256": "9d578dac663357529edd1f6453fcfe69bdc59ac882408d9edfde5a4c2916befa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-025",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1908473-025",
      "text": "To balance constituent incentives and prevent abuse, the voting rights increase should be calibrated so that contingent capital holders obtain a majority stake only in combination with the largest institutional shareholder.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Change of control limited to the case where the first trigger failed"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "To balance the constituents' incentives and avoid abuse,194 the voting rights increase could be calibrated to give CCS holders a majority stake in the company only with, for instance, the largest institutional shareholder.",
      "text_sha256": "4bb29d60a9d4e5c7a6b501e771472c59ca1ca96485b159299f47ce20832c4c76",
      "source_sha256": "9d578dac663357529edd1f6453fcfe69bdc59ac882408d9edfde5a4c2916befa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1908473-029",
      "text": "Information asymmetries between market participants and a systemically important institution's management before default can be reduced if a financial weakening after conversion of contingent capital triggers a voting rights increase.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "systemic-risk",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Requires that the weakening occur after contingent capital has converted into equity"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The information asymmetries between market participants and a SIFI's management before a SIFI defaults199 could be minimized if a financial weakening of the SIFI after conversion of CCS triggers a voting rights increase.",
      "text_sha256": "e2ebab5810ea836540c9353f8397bb42c91e0f9d39c09a63383af150cc59ee12",
      "source_sha256": "9d578dac663357529edd1f6453fcfe69bdc59ac882408d9edfde5a4c2916befa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1908473-030",
      "text": "The second trigger voting rights increase should never actually be triggered; its function is to level the playing field between constituents, incentivize negotiation, and provide an alternative to reorganization.",
      "claim_type": "normative",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "contingent-capital"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The second trigger voting rights increase should never actually be triggered. Rather, it should help level the playing field between constituents and incentivize negotiation and provide an alternative to reorganization.",
      "text_sha256": "15de611eb425dc4e8dcccb7fdf43bcca9db424d04f84820adf67569f8e6944ea",
      "source_sha256": "9d578dac663357529edd1f6453fcfe69bdc59ac882408d9edfde5a4c2916befa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1908473-031",
      "text": "German corporate law permits increases in voting rights only in very limited circumstances, such as grandfathered multiple voting shares, so the proposed voting rights increase would require statutory reform in Germany.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "law-and-legal-systems"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "H\u00f6chststimmrechte were banned for listed German corporations in 1998",
        "France and the United Kingdom by contrast permit multiple votes per share"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "German corporate law allows an increase in voting rights only in very limited circumstances, such as grandfathering provisions for shares with multiple voting rights that were created before the enactment of the Corporations Act",
      "text_sha256": "fef0955a5acf31a8952a93f53b721e53a376fdee177ba22435023949e72081db",
      "source_sha256": "9d578dac663357529edd1f6453fcfe69bdc59ac882408d9edfde5a4c2916befa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1908473-032",
      "text": "Allocating super-voting stock to contingent capital holders satisfies Delaware's legitimate business purpose requirement, because the allocation serves to avoid insolvency and dissolution of the institution.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Delaware permits alternative voting arrangements if the charter provides for them or is amended",
        "Increases are limited if inequitable or in breach of fiduciary duty"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1908473-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Allocating super-voting stock, as proposed herein, would be for the legitimate business purpose of avoiding both insolvency and dissolution.",
      "text_sha256": "7bade66fe790f0506e64729960820dba2b84f8ff6f4ce6e98e65a1f69653acc1",
      "source_sha256": "9d578dac663357529edd1f6453fcfe69bdc59ac882408d9edfde5a4c2916befa",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1998455-005",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1998455-005",
      "text": "Combined with other corporate governance mechanisms, contingent capital securities function as an internal, institution specific mechanism that could fill the void left by regulators' apparent inability to supervise financial institutions effectively.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "contingent-capital",
        "governance-design",
        "corporate-governance",
        "institutional-design",
        "systemic-risk"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where CCS are used alongside, not instead of, other corporate governance mechanisms"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1998455-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Com- bined with other corporate governance mechanisms, CCSs, as an internal institution-specific mechanism, could help fill a void left by regulators' seeming inability to supervise financial institutions effectively.",
      "text_sha256": "62bfc576d039a6c91f956530a517c9bdebf1f0678f1deabec629316d7c7c3bfa",
      "source_sha256": "1c16ff10a284469ba15fb7ba5523449b917388ee692d9b394f9e8c094544e32c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1998455-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1998455-010",
      "text": "The threat of dilution of stock holdings, combined with the threat of loss on conversion, reduces the pressure shareholders place on the management of systemically important financial institutions to take higher risks.",
