      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1998455-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1998455-032",
      "text": "A contingent capital design that increases voting rights on conversion allows systemically important institutions to lower risk taking implicitly and to achieve an indirect, institution specific form of corporate governance reform through increased checks and balances.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "contingent-capital",
        "corporate-governance",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where CCS are issued with a voting rights increase upon conversion",
        "issuance may be voluntary or mandatory"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1998455-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "With a design that increases voting rights, SI- FIs could implicitly lower risk-taking and allow for a form of in- direct and institution- specific corporate governance reform, i.e., increased checks and balances.",
      "text_sha256": "789be58dfd248447f06083ac35a4074fe99da746c183c5f588a4a867719ed206",
      "source_sha256": "1c16ff10a284469ba15fb7ba5523449b917388ee692d9b394f9e8c094544e32c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1998455-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1998455-033",
      "text": "Because the threat of a change of control leads leaders to take fewer risks in order to avoid triggering conversion, a contingent capital design with increased voting rights allows those leaders to act more in accordance with their moral convictions and conscience.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where conversion carries a credible threat of change of control",
        "where shareholders respond by allowing management more discretion over risk taking"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1998455-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "It could allow SIFI leaders to increasingly act in accordance with their moral convictions and conscience because the threat of change of control may influence SIFI leaders to take fewer risks to avoid triggering the conversion of CCS and a possible change of con- trol.",
      "text_sha256": "029bbfc17175c128b580191096e1a1b442074faff85908cea340e7c242520359",
      "source_sha256": "1c16ff10a284469ba15fb7ba5523449b917388ee692d9b394f9e8c094544e32c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1998455-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1998455-034",
      "text": "Management incentives for risk control are heightened upon conversion, especially where management knows that holders of converted contingent capital would command a majority vote, with or without institutional shareholders.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design",
        "contingent-capital",
        "corporate-governance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "depends on the volume of CCS issuance, which determines the influence of CCS holders"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1998455-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "More importantly, management incen- tives for risk control could be heightened upon conversion, espe- cially if management knows that CCS holders would have a ma- jority vote upon conversion (with or without institutional shareholders).",
      "text_sha256": "e7cf3039839e583756bfe94225960eaaf2e0758d253aff273ef00684eaeb0fee",
      "source_sha256": "1c16ff10a284469ba15fb7ba5523449b917388ee692d9b394f9e8c094544e32c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1998455-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/1998455-038",
      "text": "Rather than banning purchases by systemically important institutions of each other's contingent capital, which could be detrimental to market evolution, the design should require disclosure of the purchaser's identity and approval by the issuer.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "economics",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where the concern is competitors acquiring voting rights as equity holders upon conversion"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:1998455-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "An outright ban of SIFI CCS purchases, or at least purchases in other SIFI CCS issuances, could be detrimental for CCS mar- ket evolution. Perhaps a mechanism that requires disclosure of the identity of the purchaser for SIFIs and approval by the issuer could address these concerns.",
      "text_sha256": "48327670f03b2c93fc65b732e1b59b4527efc2a38520a5a889d4798a7d38ab75",
      "source_sha256": "1c16ff10a284469ba15fb7ba5523449b917388ee692d9b394f9e8c094544e32c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
