    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2029983-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The Netherlands is already Europe's most attractive venue to facilitate such settlements because it is the only European country that allows a collective settlement in a mass litigation to be binding on all class members who do not opt-out of the",
      "text_sha256": "2cd9293e931a793a3b25a39c7a43c57c0f4f416ae3aaf62c73fc9fa5d0fdca71",
      "source_sha256": "fde2ff611420eb283cbb49a6b681a2ae8efa2b4603ae71480e2d91483f0295f2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2029983-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2029983-029",
      "text": "The WCAM's structural limits could reduce the number of successful settlements: while the largest cases such as Shell and Fortis give plaintiffs enough leverage to force large settlements, smaller cases may not be successfully settled in Dutch courts.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
