      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2317580-017",
      "text": "A CIA raises the stakes for directors who would otherwise neglect their governance responsibilities, because the agreement puts the company effectively on parole and gives the government direct access that facilitates detection of compliance failures.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "companies operating under an executed CIA",
        "OIG inspection and site visit rights"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "A CIA increases the stakes for directors choosing to eschew their governance responsibilities. A company operating under a CIA is essentially on parole.55 CIAs give the government direct access to a health care corporation, facilitating the detection of compliance issues.",
      "text_sha256": "3b882fd4dc6bb9f61156f5a796e50f50eb862e69b4c2d8a48eeb2097e3eb2f8f",
      "source_sha256": "50973e1e820aef47a4e7ffdbdcb513d03f1845643fcf4fa5910e9528a0b7dac2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2317580-024",
      "text": "Although CIAs are not laws, they go beyond aspirational governance standards because they set forth concrete governance rules that more clearly define the duties to be informed, to exercise oversight, and to maintain effective reporting systems, thereby requiring a higher standard of care.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "corporate-governance",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "directors of companies operating under a CIA"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Although CIAs are not laws, they do go beyond aspirational governance standards. CIAs set forth concrete governance rules that expand the fiduciary duties of directors.",
      "text_sha256": "96f7fefebc62eab96cc241a997093e60fa46fe0331b6000cb748d27176ebb437",
      "source_sha256": "50973e1e820aef47a4e7ffdbdcb513d03f1845643fcf4fa5910e9528a0b7dac2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2317580-028",
      "text": "Because CIAs mandate a chief compliance officer and dictate how that officer interacts with the board, they increase the board's knowledge and monitoring of compliance, and a board possessing such knowledge should play a bigger role in ensuring that the company meets federal and state standards.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "compliance",
        "corporate-governance",
        "citation-and-knowledge"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "CIAs that mandate a CCO and prescribe CCO to board reporting"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "More specifically, because CIAs often mandate a CCO and dictate how the CCO interacts with the board, CIAs can increase boards' knowledge and monitoring of the company's compliance.",
      "text_sha256": "d73a1ded0ddeabf4622e8620836e72eda5eb332f3ad9967d73fa74974410e620",
      "source_sha256": "50973e1e820aef47a4e7ffdbdcb513d03f1845643fcf4fa5910e9528a0b7dac2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2317580-032",
      "text": "When a company operates under a CIA, the judicial distinction between the law and aspirational corporate governance becomes less clear.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "companies operating under a CIA"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, when a company is operating under a CIA, the distinction between the law and aspirational governance is less clear.",
      "text_sha256": "2af330f9a319ce80e489ed8e63363e2dd7e30c05adc45afdf23e37efadc6a867",
      "source_sha256": "50973e1e820aef47a4e7ffdbdcb513d03f1845643fcf4fa5910e9528a0b7dac2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2317580-033",
      "text": "In re Pfizer stipulates that for a company that executed a CIA the court will allow an assumption that the directors were fully informed and therefore willing participants in the corporate malfeasance, so that the CIAs themselves became the court's proof that the directors could have breached their fiduciary duties.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "corporate-governance",
        "law-and-legal-systems"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "In re Pfizer, 722 F. Supp. 2d 453 (S.D.N.Y. 2010)",
        "boards obligated by prior CIAs to monitor the very conduct alleged"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The court stipulates that in the case of a company that executed a CIA, it will allow an assumption that the directors were fully informed, and thus, willing participants in the corporate malfeasance.",
      "text_sha256": "f83a8f3d0774ef39725c7f5e1d4972131ad1932d1d57875ebd8b5b9a7ed55932",
      "source_sha256": "50973e1e820aef47a4e7ffdbdcb513d03f1845643fcf4fa5910e9528a0b7dac2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2317580-035",
      "text": "Courts assume that the boards of companies that executed a CIA have more knowledge and can exercise more control, and therefore hold those directors to a heightened fiduciary duty, rejecting directors' claims of ignorance because executing a CIA or a CIA like agreement means directors do know or should know about the noncompliance.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "corporate-governance",
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "companies that executed a CIA or a comparable agreement such as a voluntary compliance plan"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-035:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "To summarize, courts assume that the boards of companies that executed a CIA have more knowledge and can exercise more control and should thus act with a heightened fiduciary duty. Directors are held to a higher standard if the company executed a CIA.",
      "text_sha256": "76ef83a051945e52cd18cdf7e2f5cc8822ff7abc6ef61149055040a6034d50cb",
      "source_sha256": "50973e1e820aef47a4e7ffdbdcb513d03f1845643fcf4fa5910e9528a0b7dac2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2317580-038",
      "text": "Governance of health care providers is distinctively complicated because directors must balance patients, physicians, taxpayers, the government, and shareholders, and substantial government involvement and liability through Medicare and Medicaid make the taxpaying public a stakeholder.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "corporate-governance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "directors of health care corporations",
        "Medicare and Medicaid participation"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Substantial government involvement and liability through Medicare and Medicaid further complicates governance of health care providers because the taxpaying public is a stakeholder.",
      "text_sha256": "b31f4f29119dce381410c470771722e84753d675a6c3bb6e9a3600b45a73f708",
      "source_sha256": "50973e1e820aef47a4e7ffdbdcb513d03f1845643fcf4fa5910e9528a0b7dac2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2317580-039",
      "text": "As a unique hybrid category, CIAs transcend both the law of fiduciary duties and aspirational corporate governance, and courts may come to interpret CIAs and other hybrid forms such as deferred prosecution agreements as expanding the basic legal duty of care.",
      "claim_type": "predictive",
      "topics": [
        "compliance",
        "governance-design",
        "corporate-governance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "continued judicial recognition of CIAs and voluntary compliance plans"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2317580-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Given the characteristics of CIAs and courts' increasing recognition of CIAs and VCPs, courts may interpret CIAs and other hybrid forms, such as deferred prosecution agreements, as expanding the basic legal duty of care.",
      "text_sha256": "e10274e58eb4b913cef4f090b650b3e887e5cec14be16f14cb4749d51bcb4cb2",
      "source_sha256": "50973e1e820aef47a4e7ffdbdcb513d03f1845643fcf4fa5910e9528a0b7dac2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
