    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2337268-002",
      "text": "The IAA restricts the assignment of advisory contracts without client consent in order to protect investors against changes in the character or quality of the advisory services they contracted for.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "contracts between investment advisers and their clients"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Moreover, to protect investors against changes in the character or quality of advisory services, the IAA prohibits the assignment of contracts with clients unless the",
      "text_sha256": "f4bb91c69668c1e83c2aa6531c51133b20877a6447dd9c04afa1e9f75c4853bd",
      "source_sha256": "7075ce35282a8ee75b81ae3dec0e19f68631beae7f3c3a00ab2827538dc9e302",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-004",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2337268-004",
      "text": "Investment adviser status under the IAA requires that the advice concern a security; without a security in the dealings between adviser and client the statutory definition does not apply.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "private-funds",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "securities-law"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "classification of a person as an investment adviser under the IAA"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Providing investment advice and being considered an investment adviser under the IAA requires that a person renders advice with regard to a security.",
      "text_sha256": "42dac82a4761b7e43e00a95f401d528a7d3f90ec444770cb0210c40e764d6c56",
      "source_sha256": "7075ce35282a8ee75b81ae3dec0e19f68631beae7f3c3a00ab2827538dc9e302",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2337268-008",
      "text": "Proof of special compensation is a necessary condition for classifying a broker dealer as an investment adviser, and the burden of proving both special compensation and that the advice exceeded the incidental is on the plaintiff.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "broker dealers whose advisory services are solely incidental to brokerage"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "A broker-dealer cannot be classified as an investment adviser without proof of special compensation.",
      "text_sha256": "a6b685126004fb9c012cdf92fbc5f7bd5b5e568977d3c1c663d3dd46837f15ba",
      "source_sha256": "7075ce35282a8ee75b81ae3dec0e19f68631beae7f3c3a00ab2827538dc9e302",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2337268-009",
      "text": "Congress created distinct hedge fund adviser categories in Title IV of the Dodd-Frank Act because it recognized that not all hedge fund advisers pose the same systemic risks and therefore do not all require the same level of oversight.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "systemic-risk",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "hedge fund advisers under Title IV of the Dodd-Frank Act"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "When it passed the Dodd-Frank Act,17 Congress recognized that not all hedge fund advisers pose the same systemic risks and therefore require the same level of oversight. Congress therefore created different hedge fund adviser categories in Title IV of the Dodd-Frank Act.18",
      "text_sha256": "36b850b6c052ee16261a1b8a391beffe9b5e224be67112e8ba6fd62cc794d3b7",
      "source_sha256": "7075ce35282a8ee75b81ae3dec0e19f68631beae7f3c3a00ab2827538dc9e302",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2337268-010",
      "text": "Title IV and the SEC forms use assets under management as a proxy for systemic threat, so that disclosure obligations scale upward with the size of the hedge fund adviser.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "systemic-risk",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "disclosure"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "hedge fund advisers categorized by AUM under Title IV"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "forms suggest that the larger the hedge fund advisers, as measured by their assets under management (AUM), the higher the possible systemic threat the respective fund poses. Accordingly, the disclosure requirements increase with the AUM size of hedge fund advisers.",
      "text_sha256": "ab1839ea56fb5d87d2700b6e5019fd3216e78f35b18b4cf5f6694d404c9c3463",
      "source_sha256": "7075ce35282a8ee75b81ae3dec0e19f68631beae7f3c3a00ab2827538dc9e302",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2337268-012",
      "text": "Where a state does not provide sufficient regulation of mid-sized investment advisers, oversight reverts to the SEC, so state level regulatory gaps trigger a federal backstop rather than leaving advisers unsupervised.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "mid-sized investment advisers",
        "states whose regulation is deemed insufficient"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Should a particular state not provide sufficient regulation, the SEC will oversee the mid-sized investment adviser.22",
      "text_sha256": "2a995795d889ed8b025d1d71195d904833759cd047d054ca5598ac2c2586863d",
      "source_sha256": "7075ce35282a8ee75b81ae3dec0e19f68631beae7f3c3a00ab2827538dc9e302",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2337268-018",
      "text": "Registration is the gateway that makes data collection and enhanced disclosure by hedge fund managers possible, and the Dodd-Frank Act raised disclosure requirements for registered advisers specifically to address systemic risk concerns.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "securities-law",
        "disclosure",
        "systemic-risk",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "registered investment advisers after the Dodd-Frank Act"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The registration of investment advisers facilitates the collection of data and enhanced disclosure by hedge fund managers. The Dodd-Frank Act increased the disclosure requirements for registered investment advisers to address concerns over systemic risk.40",
      "text_sha256": "41dd4f0c936b18931330d6c8cd91849ddc0af25c73da95d8558724640c5f4c37",
      "source_sha256": "7075ce35282a8ee75b81ae3dec0e19f68631beae7f3c3a00ab2827538dc9e302",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2337268-032",
      "text": "The Dodd-Frank Act tightened custodial practice by requiring safeguards for client assets and verification by independent accountants, a response to concerns over theft and client exposure to Ponzi schemes.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "defi"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "investment advisers with custody of client assets after 2010"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In 2010, in an effort to address concerns over theft and to lower clients' exposure to the risks of Ponzi schemes, the Dodd-Frank Act amended the IAA, heightening custodial practices by requiring safeguards for client assets and the use of independent accountants to verify assets.96",
      "text_sha256": "61a837edfe915720ed3db43909f689488295435197ea5f2f9e81ea1081afa6a1",
      "source_sha256": "7075ce35282a8ee75b81ae3dec0e19f68631beae7f3c3a00ab2827538dc9e302",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2337268-036",
      "text": "Because investment advisers owe a duty to obtain best execution for customer orders, they ought to evaluate the executions carried out on their clients' behalf on a periodic basis.",
      "claim_type": "normative",
      "topics": [
        "corporate-governance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "advisers placing or directing client orders"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "investment advisers are subject to a duty to obtain the best execution for customer orders,103 investment advisers ought to periodically evaluate the executions on behalf of their clients.",
      "text_sha256": "7b039dce906005156d190c4d5da2e4dd17ef0479667655e80f84e02393e34333",
      "source_sha256": "7075ce35282a8ee75b81ae3dec0e19f68631beae7f3c3a00ab2827538dc9e302",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-043",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2337268-043",
      "text": "Referral fees to third parties are permitted only if the recipients are bona fide persons under securities laws, the fees are disclosed to the adviser's clients, and the fees are paid under a written agreement.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "citation-and-knowledge"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "referral fees paid by investment advisers to third parties"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2337268-043:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Advisers may pay referral fees provided the referral fee recipients are bona fide persons under securities laws, the fees have been disclosed to the investment adviser's clients, and the fees are paid in accordance with a written agreement.113",
      "text_sha256": "c8d35b7e5be16e56fe16d98d4b664bd152891e5a1856cd8e63a0db40359b434b",
      "source_sha256": "7075ce35282a8ee75b81ae3dec0e19f68631beae7f3c3a00ab2827538dc9e302",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2348463-001",
      "text": "There is a substantial overlap between the systemic risk disclosure requirements imposed on hedge fund advisers under Title IV of the Dodd-Frank Act and the disclosure requirements under the fully revised version of Bankruptcy Rule 2019.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "private-funds",
        "systemic-risk",
        "disclosure",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "hedge fund advisers subject to Title IV reporting",
        "creditors and groups covered by Revised Rule 2019 in chapter 9 and chapter 11 cases"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The author provides evidence of a substantial overlap between systemic risk disclosure requirements under Title IV and the disclosure requirements under the fully-revised version of Bankruptcy Rule 2019 (Revised Rule 2019).",
      "text_sha256": "a6ea9bc8e6a1aaa4edd42119538f9682c1320dba43c6dd99513c6765ede5e908",
      "source_sha256": "b3682f24c0b277b3307fb9f54cd17a4e0a87b48eecba34b40e189212f20c9a22",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2348463-002",
      "text": "Under the regulatory framework in place at the time of writing, the threat that hedge funds' systemic risk filings could be publicly disclosed through the bankruptcy process will affect hedge funds' tactics and their role in distressed investing only marginally.",
      "claim_type": "predictive",
      "topics": [
        "systemic-risk",
        "disclosure",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "private-funds"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "current regulatory framework as of 2013 to 2014",
        "Form PF disclosures not yet standardized by the SEC"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In the current regulatory framework, the threat of public disclosure of systemic risk filings by hedge funds via the bankruptcy process may only marginally affect hedge funds' tactics and their role in distressed investing.",
      "text_sha256": "eb10eda4eb0ee2b24740212589e3d302c6af157960f1180bc1413ba4c2b0d104",
      "source_sha256": "b3682f24c0b277b3307fb9f54cd17a4e0a87b48eecba34b40e189212f20c9a22",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2348463-007",
      "text": "The SEC has not standardized the disclosures required in Form PF, and there is evidence that Form PF requirements rest on an inconsistent use of industry terms, which can in turn produce inconsistent and contradictory data reporting.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "private-funds",
        "systemic-risk",
        "disclosure",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Form PF as promulgated and in effect at the time of writing"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The SEC has not yet standardized the required disclosures in Form PF and there is some evidence that the disclosure requirements in Form PF are based on an inconsistent use of industry terms which may in turn result in inconsistent and perhaps contradictory data reporting.",
      "text_sha256": "573d4b2270f57995f34166400b8d7d0a9779c5e7f3fe5af2debf258976477fc9",
      "source_sha256": "b3682f24c0b277b3307fb9f54cd17a4e0a87b48eecba34b40e189212f20c9a22",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2348463-010",
      "text": "Old Bankruptcy Rule 2019 was applied inconsistently in practice, with courts interpreting it with a high degree of variability both across and within jurisdictions.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "systemic-risk",
        "law-and-legal-systems"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "period before the 2011 revision of Rule 2019"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Old Rule 2019 had been applied inconsistently in practice. Courts interpreted old Rule 2019 with a high degree of variability, both across and within jurisdictions.",
      "text_sha256": "1373db9aade3372661d6d87a1605150af380720b8ce1722dee00bb0d2ad1fcc5",
      "source_sha256": "b3682f24c0b277b3307fb9f54cd17a4e0a87b48eecba34b40e189212f20c9a22",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2348463-017",
      "text": "Mandatory quarterly Form PF reporting for large hedge fund advisers is designed to give the Financial Stability Oversight Council timely data for identifying emerging systemic risk trends and to align United States practice with international trends.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "private-funds",
        "systemic-risk",
        "disclosure",
        "compliance",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "advisers with at least $1.5 billion regulatory assets under management attributable to hedge funds"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Mandatory quarterly reporting for large hedge fund advisers in the United States is intended to provide the FSOC with timely data to identify emerging trends in systemic risk and align with international trends.",
      "text_sha256": "019bb69fde41cef999f9e836cedc026f013318eb14cab6599dc6ea0fd2fe47e8",
      "source_sha256": "b3682f24c0b277b3307fb9f54cd17a4e0a87b48eecba34b40e189212f20c9a22",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2348463-018",
      "text": "Bankruptcy and systemic risk disclosure obligations for hedge funds have different origins and serve different purposes: bankruptcy disclosure is meant to level the playing field in the restructuring process, while systemic risk disclosure is meant to help regulators detect and prevent systemic consequences.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "systemic-risk",
        "disclosure",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Bankruptcy and systemic risk disclosure obligations for hedge funds have different origins and are intended for different purposes. Bankruptcy disclosures are generally intended to level the playing field in the bankruptcy and restructuring process.",
      "text_sha256": "fcfef22cc1d7e606c4518fa95c93f260f561deaff7532b07870a962b5e843aae",
      "source_sha256": "b3682f24c0b277b3307fb9f54cd17a4e0a87b48eecba34b40e189212f20c9a22",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2348463-020",
      "type": "Claim",
