    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2714974-026",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2714974-026",
      "text": "Direct regulation of hedge fund leverage collapses on the details because balance sheet leverage is not an adequate measure of risk and would push funds into off-balance sheet avoidance strategies.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "regulatory-failure",
        "research-methods",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to proposals for direct leverage regulation"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2714974-026:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Balance sheet leverage is not an adequate measure of risk and would encourage avoidance behavior with off-balance sheet strategies.",
      "text_sha256": "10cc47c0e99ce9f8eed2a6c4ea26298ca2ffdeb8a23e02899c01048041f43f40",
      "source_sha256": "7764601d3ed5bb056b58949e8411eff9dfb9855f143719062030c980c5fa801b",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2714974-027",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2714974-027",
      "text": "Alternative risk measures such as value at risk have severe measurement problems, so any direct regulation of leverage would be set conservatively and would substantially limit hedge funds' ability to provide market liquidity.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "defi",
        "economics",
        "research-methods"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to direct regulation of hedge fund leverage"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2714974-027:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Any attempt to directly regulate leverage would likely be conservative, due to measurement problems, and put major limits on hedge funds' ability to provide market liquidity.",
      "text_sha256": "0850f57c2b91eac6841b3b6e80b33a940d86bfc2cb00e371439be44bb769e80c",
      "source_sha256": "7764601d3ed5bb056b58949e8411eff9dfb9855f143719062030c980c5fa801b",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2714974-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2714974-028",
      "text": "Direct regulation of hedge fund leverage increases moral hazard costs, because lenders and counterparties relax their own vigilance once they rely on government rules to constrain fund risk taking.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "economics",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies where government rules substitute for private monitoring"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2714974-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Direct regulation could also increase moral hazard costs as lenders and counterparties may relax their vigilance in reliance on the government rules.",
      "text_sha256": "6163e26d58c5496d87a2dc2049e7e5f795f30706b08e26060d445f772add4d80",
      "source_sha256": "7764601d3ed5bb056b58949e8411eff9dfb9855f143719062030c980c5fa801b",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2714974-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2714974-029",
      "text": "Any prescriptive regulatory regime for hedge funds risks leaving the financial system less stable rather than more stable, because counterparties relax vigilance when they believe authorities are monitoring and constraining fund risk taking.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to prescriptive position reporting and monitoring regimes"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2714974-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "A risk of any prescriptive regulatory regime is that, by creating moral hazard in the marketplace, it leaves the system less rather than more stable.",
      "text_sha256": "b676f4ae51d71823cd786295db0edc43bedae1d060ef0f4213f33b11d71fbbcc",
      "source_sha256": "7764601d3ed5bb056b58949e8411eff9dfb9855f143719062030c980c5fa801b",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2715083-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2715083-002",
      "text": "Regulatory convergence is not driven only by tightened post crisis rules: the liberalization of advertising restrictions after the Dodd-Frank Act also pushes hedge funds toward mutual fund form, so deregulation and reregulation work in the same convergent direction.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "U.S. private fund regulation after Dodd-Frank and the JOBS Act"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2715083-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This is not just a result of more stringent regulations enacted via the Dodd-Frank Act in the aftermath of the financial crisis; the liberalization of the advertising restrictions post Dodd-Frank Act also makes hedge funds more like mutual funds.",
      "text_sha256": "cbba66579c30284ca1f9163f81573e18967fdd7369f071dad6e11bb8bafc3803",
      "source_sha256": "b5c92186260d4a8499a14f81ee24ace093b24e7740af3effcd1c526fa4fa221e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2715083-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2715083-013",
      "text": "The author stipulates the term nominal confluence: legal requirements that are formally identical for mutual and hedge fund managers but that operate in materially different ways in practice, so formal legal convergence overstates actual convergence.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies where the same statute or rule governs both fund types"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2715083-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The term \"nominal confluence\" as used herein describes otherwise identical legal requirements for mutual and hedge fund managers that can be materially different in practice.",
      "text_sha256": "779db01097bb97a441e922394eda81ccc61523ff29abf72f530cda9bf8cd5dc5",
      "source_sha256": "b5c92186260d4a8499a14f81ee24ace093b24e7740af3effcd1c526fa4fa221e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2715083-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2715083-017",
      "text": "Alternative mutual funds generally cannot deliver the same absolute returns as hedge funds, a shortfall some attribute to the lighter touch regulation and better incentives available to hedge funds.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "private-funds",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
