    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2740477-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Private rulemakers can have a comparative advantage over public rulemakers because, unlike their public counterparts, they often can produce necessary, comparable, decentralized, and institution-specific information for rulemaking.",
