    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2748096-001",
      "text": "Government assessments of hedge fund systemic risk conflict directly: the OFR, FSB, and IOSCO treat private fund activities as important threats to the financial system, while the UK Financial Services Authority concluded from its first comprehensive survey of London's private fund industry that hedge funds pose no systemic risk.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "private-funds",
        "systemic-risk",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "comparison of post-crisis U.S. and UK regulator reports"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "By contrast, the Financial Services Authority (FSA) (2010) in the United Kingdom concluded in its first comprehensive survey of London's private fund industry that the hedge fund industry poses no systemic risk to the financial system.",
      "text_sha256": "15bfa632d4c49d31817df4022acb14259a3cc6ea2b30c2bde685d0a8a5a77f1c",
      "source_sha256": "8f30260f2c1db728b45c4f3b9b7c64358cf9d3217277bc3c63a910c32f87b508",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-006",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2748096-006",
      "text": "Because hedge fund losses are absorbed directly by a large and dispersed body of investors and their equity capital, private fund advisers are unlikely to trigger a systemic event, and their activity may even reduce market volatility.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "private-funds",
        "systemic-risk",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to funds financed by investor equity rather than short term debt"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-006:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "But some research suggests that private fund advisers are unlikely to trigger a systemic event because losses in hedge funds are directly absorbed by the multitude of investors and their equity capital and may actually reduce market volatility",
      "text_sha256": "8dc7b877139994e7d131201abf0e2260124aa83fdf5db236f2687b045e61392a",
      "source_sha256": "8f30260f2c1db728b45c4f3b9b7c64358cf9d3217277bc3c63a910c32f87b508",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2748096-010",
      "text": "Any conclusion that hedge funds contributed to the financial crisis of 2007-2008 is circumstantial or anecdotal, because the data needed to test it, on leverage, counterparty relations, AUM, and portfolio holdings, were not collected for any substantial period before the crisis.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "systemic-risk",
        "research-methods",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "citation-and-knowledge"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to retrospective assessment of the 2007-2008 crisis",
        "SEC systemic risk data collection began only after Title IV of the Dodd-Frank Act"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Without such data for a substantial time period before the financial crisis, concluding that hedge funds may have had a role in the financial crisis is circumstantial or anecdotal.",
      "text_sha256": "403bce972951e95e4f390527315349862b44810255a25b399d9ab298f8c41851",
      "source_sha256": "8f30260f2c1db728b45c4f3b9b7c64358cf9d3217277bc3c63a910c32f87b508",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-011",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2748096-011",
      "text": "The opacity of the hedge fund shadow banking system blocks direct measurement of hedge funds' role in the crisis, leaving researchers with indirect measures extracted from existing data rather than primary pre-crisis sources.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "systemic-risk",
        "research-methods",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "absence of access to primary pre-crisis hedge fund data"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-011:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "the shadow banking system of hedge funds and the lack of sufficient transparency create substantial obstacles to implementing direct measures, especially without the access to primary sources of data regarding hedge funds before the crisis.",
      "text_sha256": "2c0487d2c9153781885aae435d9c782af17998c9c3838a0466c1d1926e9055db",
      "source_sha256": "8f30260f2c1db728b45c4f3b9b7c64358cf9d3217277bc3c63a910c32f87b508",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2748096-012",
      "text": "The contagion story, in which hedge fund losses spread to other financial institutions and undermine systemic stability, is counterbalanced in practice because hedge fund collapses are rarely sudden and almost always unfold in incremental steps over a long period.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "systemic-risk",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "describes observed hedge fund collapse dynamics rather than theoretical models"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "First, hedge fund collapses are rarely sudden but in practice almost always occur in incremental steps over a long time period.",
      "text_sha256": "06471cf35382bec36685f96e33ae2eb9885812d37b92911b9aadddb1568a6c57",
      "source_sha256": "8f30260f2c1db728b45c4f3b9b7c64358cf9d3217277bc3c63a910c32f87b508",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-023",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2748096-023",
      "text": "Strategy diversification does not insulate the hedge fund industry from systemic risk: returns across different hedge fund strategies were more correlated during the financial crisis of 2007-2008 than before it, so the industry can pose systemic risk despite investing across a broad spectrum of assets and strategies.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "systemic-risk",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "periods of market stress",
        "evidence drawn from the 2007-2008 crisis"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-023:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "hedge fund returns should not affect their systemic risk. However, evidence exists that the returns of different hedge fund strategies were more correlated during the financial crisis of 2007-2008 than before the crisis",
      "text_sha256": "86ae868967598a47e679f75c96f1a6c12d142eec86a4d8d8b4d874d38f40a641",
      "source_sha256": "8f30260f2c1db728b45c4f3b9b7c64358cf9d3217277bc3c63a910c32f87b508",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2748096-029",
      "text": "About 18 percent of hedge funds ceased operations in 2008, yet little evidence exists that these failures generated losses at prime brokers or other financial institutions, which weakens the direct transmission account of hedge fund systemic risk.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "hedge fund closures during 2008",
        "RAND Corporation study"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "According to the report, about 18 percent of hedge funds ceased operations in 2008, although little evidence exists that these fund failures contributed to losses at prime brokers or other financial institutions.",
      "text_sha256": "aa6a4d5cc081a06db219d4d619406cbe294b1cfe874041f3bd98a7a3110ae1c8",
      "source_sha256": "8f30260f2c1db728b45c4f3b9b7c64358cf9d3217277bc3c63a910c32f87b508",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2748096-034",
      "text": "Traditional risk-adjusted alphas underestimate hedge fund risk: once correlation risk is controlled for, previously observed significant hedge fund alphas disappear, which makes correlation risk a systematic risk factor for hedge fund returns.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "research-methods"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "cross-sectional analysis of individual hedge fund returns"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This finding is important because traditional risk-adjusted alphas may underestimate hedge fund risk.",
      "text_sha256": "015a0bbae37694e850bb01caeac9fce06f4e70bab8795e188739c27ee912a8d8",
      "source_sha256": "8f30260f2c1db728b45c4f3b9b7c64358cf9d3217277bc3c63a910c32f87b508",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2748096-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2748096-035",
      "text": "Once liquidity risk is incorporated into the analysis, the superior performance previously attributed to predictability in managerial skills disappears in hedge fund portfolios.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "defi",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "hedge fund portfolios formed on predictability in managerial skill"
