    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Because national and international law do not currently recognize AI as a subject of law, AI has no legal personality and as such cannot be held personally liable for damages.",
      "text_sha256": "d8a23b273d84df578ee32c097f5f8dadd259276b729ca6226acd5b6e7435b7a3",
      "source_sha256": "9cd875ebdb0266febbdcdabfca5b9b9f0de1b7ad9e3d5a8a5971bdbe469323b7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2834531-008",
      "text": "The existing regulatory infrastructure cannot sufficiently distinguish beneficial innovation from other innovation, and therefore cannot harness it.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dynamic-regulation",
        "innovation",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The existing regulatory infrastructure cannot sufficiently distinguish and harness beneficial innovation.",
      "text_sha256": "7dc04ffa70d45a90eef387a013b6238603c9add65870227718b752bdbd6b1f82",
      "source_sha256": "9cd875ebdb0266febbdcdabfca5b9b9f0de1b7ad9e3d5a8a5971bdbe469323b7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-014",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2834531-014",
      "text": "Regulators too often define success negatively, as the avoidance of catastrophe, which makes regulatory experimentation unattractive to them.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where regulators are exposed to criticism for adverse outcomes"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-014:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Too often, regulators define \"success\" in negative terms, as in the avoidance of catastrophe.",
      "text_sha256": "49da608306f5444a421597f0e1605097e8e539447ed98c794ae87c8c15bbba6b",
      "source_sha256": "9cd875ebdb0266febbdcdabfca5b9b9f0de1b7ad9e3d5a8a5971bdbe469323b7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2834531-015",
      "text": "Because regulators seek to avoid grounds for criticism, they inevitably adopt an overly cautious posture, which is what the precautionary principle amounts to in practice.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "innovation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Avoiding grounds for criticism inevitably results in an overly cautious approach, called the \"precautionary principle.\"",
      "text_sha256": "ffeb6407ac5b1e6ccf575c3b4685c2d55e6734c6908f7d22f913a58752344cb2",
      "source_sha256": "9cd875ebdb0266febbdcdabfca5b9b9f0de1b7ad9e3d5a8a5971bdbe469323b7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-021",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2834531-021",
      "text": "The delegation of technology policy to politicians advised by experts rested on public trust that has since eroded: consistent empirical evidence shows that trust in both government and experts has declined in recent years.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "recent decades, drawing on Pew survey evidence"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-021:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Although the public once had a relatively high degree of trust in both the political process and the scientific/expert method, consistent empirical evidence demonstrates that both trust in government and experts has declined in recent years.",
      "text_sha256": "de13704eaa274fabc5de8c964429ecd125458c7bd9a0500e96fa14ce02a17760",
      "source_sha256": "9cd875ebdb0266febbdcdabfca5b9b9f0de1b7ad9e3d5a8a5971bdbe469323b7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-025",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2834531-025",
      "text": "Contesting the safety rationale offered for restricting Uber, the authors argue that the two way rating system and the algorithmic matching of drivers and customers already provide an effective means of policing drivers and ensuring a safe ride.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "ride hailing platforms with reciprocal ratings and algorithmic matching"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The two\u2013way rating system (drivers rate customers and customers rate drivers) and an algorithm\u2013based system for matching up drivers and customers appear to offer an effective means of policing Uber drivers and ensuring a safe ride for customers.",
      "text_sha256": "518607fc2556a06ec9e7f28458bb69729edd0b35b7114c10803eebccded2e76a",
      "source_sha256": "9cd875ebdb0266febbdcdabfca5b9b9f0de1b7ad9e3d5a8a5971bdbe469323b7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-026",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2834531-026",
      "text": "There is a systematic disconnect between the facts regulators identify as important and the actual experience and wishes of most consumers.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "regulatory debates over platform services such as Uber"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-026:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "There is a disconnect between the facts that regulators identify as important and the experience and wishes of most consumers.",
      "text_sha256": "343b6a6ca27da4fbdd7937a310c054f93c731690f74525c6db8f37ae4929fe33",
      "source_sha256": "9cd875ebdb0266febbdcdabfca5b9b9f0de1b7ad9e3d5a8a5971bdbe469323b7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2834531-028",
      "text": "The post truth diagnosis is self defeating as a basis for regulation: if there is no objective basis on which to act, the conclusion is inertia or reproduction of the status quo, which is precisely the regulatory paralysis the diagnosis purports to describe.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "if the skeptical post fact account of regulation is accepted"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "If we live in a post\u2013truth world then we don't have any objective basis on which to act, leading to inertia or the reproduction of the status quo.",
      "text_sha256": "30d20171d0808d8425050e0c722b253701b8a99a8eeda0c1d30a1a334b64d84a",
      "source_sha256": "9cd875ebdb0266febbdcdabfca5b9b9f0de1b7ad9e3d5a8a5971bdbe469323b7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2834531-033",
      "text": "Using investment data would let regulators act proactively, avoid wasting resources on technologies unlikely to reach the market, and define the scope of a technology more accurately by focusing on the type of firm attracting investor attention.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This might then allow regulators to be more pro\u2013active and avoid wasting resources on technologies that are unlikely to make it to market. It would also allow regulators to more accurately define the scope of a technology by focusing on the type of firm that is attracting attention.",
      "text_sha256": "b80767c5237d241952da16122769d39c5905a4183caa656f7d30f6f8c2232a35",
      "source_sha256": "9cd875ebdb0266febbdcdabfca5b9b9f0de1b7ad9e3d5a8a5971bdbe469323b7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-042",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2834531-042",
      "text": "The most interesting feature of the sandbox is that ideas, products, and services are tested in a live environment, made possible by a set of default parameters the FCA defined that can be altered case by case.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "default duration of three to six months",
        "customer numbers sufficient for statistically relevant data",
        "pre agreed safeguards and disclosure to customers"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2834531-042:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "What is perhaps most interesting about the sandbox is that new ideas, product, and services can be tested in a \"live\" environment.112 In order to create this environment, the FCA defined a set of default parameters that can be altered on a case\u2013by\u2013case basis.",
      "text_sha256": "e249d816d7e8212fa76d934dc0c2e8b7f1eb353a7434247844bc4c2355cf662f",
      "source_sha256": "9cd875ebdb0266febbdcdabfca5b9b9f0de1b7ad9e3d5a8a5971bdbe469323b7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2922176-010",
      "text": "Much corporate governance reform consists of repackaging old content under new or revised labels rather than introducing new governance.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "corporate-governance",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "illustrated by the 2016 Commonsense Principles of Corporate Governance"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Corporate governance reform often takes place by repackaging old content with new or revised labels.",
      "text_sha256": "9045b2396ee60fcd5152e6772b92bf7d8ae22d2038c63e812c74af4d8808cee5",
      "source_sha256": "fa4e986917d437cb1504281e7b986be2698e9507d8feaf426c9d7d1754ca882c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2922176-019",
      "text": "Platform companies embrace an unmediated, flat, and inclusive culture in which trust and value are generated through the platform itself rather than through the management of workers and physical assets.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "platform companies built on peer-to-peer transactions, such as Airbnb and Uber"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Most importantly, platform companies embrace an unmediated, flat, and inclusive culture.72 Trust and value are created through platforms, instead of the management of workers and physical assets.",
      "text_sha256": "5ad7805cede56f8d7a1d7ebde4900f48f1025ad980da2ddec2dd60d69750564a",
      "source_sha256": "fa4e986917d437cb1504281e7b986be2698e9507d8feaf426c9d7d1754ca882c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2922176-024",
      "text": "Inclusive and unmediated stakeholder relationships demand a much higher degree of cooperation, loyalty, and mutual trust than control-oriented, centralized, and vertical organizational forms do.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Compared to the more control-oriented, centralized, and vertical organizational forms, inclusive and unmediated relationships among firms' stakeholders require a high degree of cooperation, loyalty, and mutual trust.",
      "text_sha256": "bdf6ef7acea59c46e686ce2e9a75a58b6660f877e59566f1d47daa6420612ad9",
      "source_sha256": "fa4e986917d437cb1504281e7b986be2698e9507d8feaf426c9d7d1754ca882c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-026",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2922176-026",
      "text": "The use of legalese and substantial involvement of the legal department in corporate communications substantially damages the originality and authenticity of those communications, making them mediated and less effective.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "corporate communications intended to build trust and dialogue with stakeholders"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-026:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The use of legalese and any substantial involvement of the legal department in corporate communications can have a substantial detrimental effect on the originality and authenticity of corporate communications, making them mediated and less effective.",
      "text_sha256": "ebf7f35cf27c10e3c18d6cee6918c42e77433fd830bb297ef4f0bc670e9abe52",
      "source_sha256": "fa4e986917d437cb1504281e7b986be2698e9507d8feaf426c9d7d1754ca882c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2922176-030",
      "text": "The monitoring and advising roles of the board are no longer sufficient, and a board confined to those roles is a missed opportunity to obtain unmediated and relevant market feedback on company initiatives.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "corporate-governance",
        "compliance",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "successful companies already operating beyond the academic monitoring debate"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Successful companies recognize that the monitoring and advising role of the board is no longer sufficient and that the board of directors in many ways may constitute a missed opportunity for receiving feedback on company initiatives, e.g., unmediated and relevant input from the market.",
      "text_sha256": "cd439340439a4f1cd261534e5e57f99c75569f5ee87439ccef64391a918990f2",
      "source_sha256": "fa4e986917d437cb1504281e7b986be2698e9507d8feaf426c9d7d1754ca882c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2922176-033",
      "text": "It is feasible that in the not too distant future an artificial intelligence will hold an independent board seat with voting authority and be trusted to make smarter, data-driven choices than human directors.",
      "claim_type": "predictive",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "extrapolated from the appointment of the algorithm Vital at Deep Knowledge Ventures and Alicia T at Tieto"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "speculative",
      "relevance_score": 53
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In the not too distant future it seems feasible that artificial intelligence will have an independent board seat and may be trusted to make smarter \u2013 data-driven \u2013 choices than humans.",
      "text_sha256": "453d52080332f56962856cf5bbeecaecfa192b82f23efd21925c60bc9e6e7de8",
      "source_sha256": "fa4e986917d437cb1504281e7b986be2698e9507d8feaf426c9d7d1754ca882c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2922176-034",
      "text": "Critics who dismiss artificial intelligence on boards as science fiction not worth engaging are wrong: AI on boards is a real prospect, and technologies such as blockchain-based smart contracts will both disrupt corporate governance and supply solutions to it.",
      "claim_type": "predictive",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "blockchain",
        "governance-design",
        "corporate-governance",
        "innovation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Critics who argue that it is pointless to concern oneself with future science-fiction-type prospects are wrong.",
      "text_sha256": "57efad38c8c8cf07a6a14b876ff60ba7c2ace22e5efeb19df65c7378253e09ec",
      "source_sha256": "fa4e986917d437cb1504281e7b986be2698e9507d8feaf426c9d7d1754ca882c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2922176-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2922176-035",
