      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2957645-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Anticipatory regulation uses institution-specific, timely information and feedback effects to create new rules.24 Anticipatory dynamic regulation can help minimize costly and suboptimal ex-post, trial-and-error experimentation with stable and presumptively optimal rules.25",
