      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2957645-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While most of the design features of CCS and their triggering events are underdeveloped, despite these shortcomings, CCS could help allows regulators to anticipate regulatory needs in real-time, supported by feedback effects and improved information for regulation.",
      "text_sha256": "f22334e571ceb9a218239d6381cf7435a43417dcf2baf5adbf134e074e0c5ef8",
      "source_sha256": "250b10782a5ea5dece9235a7f711aee408feaf36f2e78e310d589b5ee6304be2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2959730-001",
      "text": "Private fund advisers' increasing use of blockchain technology, artificial intelligence, and big data is a distinct source of downward pressure on the traditional 2/20 fee structure that commentators have not examined.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "private-funds",
        "innovation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "private investment fund industry",
        "period of roughly 2007 to 2017"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "A factor contributing to the market pressure on the fee structure that has not been examined by commentators pertains to the increasing use of use of blockchain technology, artificial intelligence, and big data by private fund advisers.",
      "text_sha256": "d1b1ed4c2b2965e2df67fd45969b1f21b86950db1cfc4fbe5b7ac66648040293",
      "source_sha256": "ebd86972d8817b0c1c80326ae5564476983cedba3f258ff3b2610f156b93fb50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2959730-002",
      "text": "The majority of private fund advisers that deploy blockchain technology, artificial intelligence, and big data in their operations or strategy charge their investors lower fees, even though not all blockchain enabled funds charge per transaction fees.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "private-funds"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "advisers using the technologies in operations or strategy"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While not all blockchain-enabled private investment funds charge per-transaction fees, the majority of private fund advisers that use blockchain technology, artificial intelligence, and big data in different aspects of their operations or strategy charge their investors lower fees.",
      "text_sha256": "81f93bc976d60d81a58e1a4a17c80468ac4101ad9a5ea097a6b3d33e1b848abc",
      "source_sha256": "ebd86972d8817b0c1c80326ae5564476983cedba3f258ff3b2610f156b93fb50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2959730-007",
      "text": "New managers increasingly face contested track records, meaning the new firm cannot get a consensus from the manager's old employer about the manager's track record with that employer.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "first time managers spinning out of a prior employer"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Moreover, the industry is increasingly seeing contested track records for new managers, i.e., the new firm cannot get a consensus from the new manager's old employer about the manager's track record with that employer.",
      "text_sha256": "9ddc46f52303a3bf8d248dacedb55d94f876a47a92ae6231f2f3f6341fc1dd91",
      "source_sha256": "ebd86972d8817b0c1c80326ae5564476983cedba3f258ff3b2610f156b93fb50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2959730-017",
      "text": "Blockchain removes fraudulent transactions primarily through completely decentralized network connectivity via the Internet, rather than through digital signatures alone, which only establish the identity and authenticity of the parties.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized peer to peer networks with Internet connectivity"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While blockchain's use of digital signatures helps establish the identity and authenticity of the parties involved in the transaction, it is the completely decentralized network connectivity via the Internet that allows the most protection against fraud.",
      "text_sha256": "2ce71f016aac58a7c6dabb249b63f2c79d81ce82fdcc3843e397385a00d8e90f",
      "source_sha256": "ebd86972d8817b0c1c80326ae5564476983cedba3f258ff3b2610f156b93fb50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2959730-019",
      "text": "Blockchain's distributed consensus model, in which network nodes verify and validate chain transactions before execution, makes it extremely rare for a fraudulent transaction to be recorded in the blockchain.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "distributed consensus models with node verification prior to execution"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Blockchain's distributed consensus model, e.g., the network \"nodes\" verify and validate chain transactions before execution of the transactions, makes it extremely rare for a fraudulent transaction to be recorded in the blockchain.",
      "text_sha256": "47b8b561a7364903461c03725253b69d631531d4629869d0e9044cfad48d2701",
      "source_sha256": "ebd86972d8817b0c1c80326ae5564476983cedba3f258ff3b2610f156b93fb50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-020",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2959730-020",
      "text": "Cryptographic hashing makes blockchain manipulation immediately detectable because the hash incorporates all previous transactions, so that even a single digit change produces a different hash value.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "chained hashing that incorporates all prior transactions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-020:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The smallest change to the blockchain, even a single digit/value, results in a different hash value. A different hash value makes any form of manipulation immediately detectable.",
      "text_sha256": "2141006c24aa676eb9cb47947c6af92be1031c8787c8642ab2349ab92478db32",
      "source_sha256": "ebd86972d8817b0c1c80326ae5564476983cedba3f258ff3b2610f156b93fb50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-025",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2959730-025",
      "text": "In the Numerai model, the use of artificial intelligence achieves efficiency and optimum capital allocation by reducing overhead costs, because there is no cost of human capital.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "crowdsourced data scientist models synthesized into a meta model",
        "cryptocurrency incentivized contribution"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In the Numerai model, the use of artificial intelligence ultimately helps achieve the goal of efficiency and optimum capital allocation by reducing overhead costs because there is no cost of human capital.",
      "text_sha256": "4a326677bc85c3e99c91d760e47ae825f35d4ca0effca4c2ef27448355759ae5",
      "source_sha256": "ebd86972d8817b0c1c80326ae5564476983cedba3f258ff3b2610f156b93fb50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2959730-030",
      "text": "Traditional per transaction fee models failed because settlement and calculation created a prohibitive amount of work that made such operations very difficult to execute; blockchain technology overcomes all of these restrictions.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "fee models requiring manual reconciliation and settlement"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In contrast to the traditional settlement and calculation of fees in a per-transaction model that created a prohibitive amount of work making such operations very difficult to execute, blockchain technology overcomes all of these restrictions.",
      "text_sha256": "5bcbf2029288e67e8ad44aff9252561128a2259f1329b3860e50c0630884090c",
      "source_sha256": "ebd86972d8817b0c1c80326ae5564476983cedba3f258ff3b2610f156b93fb50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2959730-031",
      "text": "Manual per transaction fee calculation and settlement is prone to human error, and these errors are removed through the use of blockchain technology.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "fee calculation and settlement performed manually"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2959730-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While normally the use of this type of fee is prone to human errors that occur during manual calculation or settlement, these errors are removed through the use of blockchain technology",
      "text_sha256": "2d31e008756477b6373f162da2e5c8abbc9726f88cf2a74e4f4ac84145b5feb2",
      "source_sha256": "ebd86972d8817b0c1c80326ae5564476983cedba3f258ff3b2610f156b93fb50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
