    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Because the system operates largely autonomously, even if every user and supporter of the blockchain and their location were known, it would still not be possible to exercise jurisdiction in the traditional meaning of the word.",
      "text_sha256": "52b5fcc8dfbb23c058fccb92598ca934d64ee30803296296a85a3072220e25ad",
      "source_sha256": "80b92e67594394e38af41b769327936833de8e25d6cf3def966a6ba13bc83d17",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-006",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2992962-006",
      "text": "Because the challenges crypto transactions pose to the existing legal and jurisdictional infrastructure are severe, including good governance in crypto transactions requires instituting governance solutions inherent in the blockchain technology itself.",
      "claim_type": "normative",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "dynamic-regulation",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-006:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Because of the severity of these challenges for the existing legal and jurisdictional infrastructure, we conclude that the sensible approach for including good governance in crypto transactions necessitates instituting governance solutions inherent in the blockchain technology itself.",
      "text_sha256": "7a7bea6098890d69379f985f3f3a7db55ab414234fc7dce49bce7abc66f3dbbf",
      "source_sha256": "80b92e67594394e38af41b769327936833de8e25d6cf3def966a6ba13bc83d17",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2992962-007",
      "text": "Proof of work mining carries significant externalities: the authors estimate that the total energy cost of running the global network of computers solving proof of work puzzles was around 700 million US dollars per year before publication.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "proof of work consensus, before publication of the article in 2017"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "One problem with proof-of-work mining is that there are significant externalities. Before the publication of this article, the total energy costs for running the global network of computers devoted to solving the proof-of-work puzzles was estimated at around $700 million USD per year.",
      "text_sha256": "2281d11a26f691cae6e4698264266255a761f7417844bfaabfb6e15ace30fb22",
      "source_sha256": "80b92e67594394e38af41b769327936833de8e25d6cf3def966a6ba13bc83d17",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2992962-008",
      "text": "Anonymity survives the blockchain's permanent public record because a new private key can be created for each transaction, so although public key addresses are stored eternally, each transaction allows an entirely new cryptographically secured private identity.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "public-key cryptography as implemented in bitcoin and Ethereum"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "So, while we can track the public key of the addresses of each transaction, and that information is stored eternally in the blockchain, each transaction allows for an entirely new private identity which is cryptographically secured.",
      "text_sha256": "4b679f1bda4a3c8d6566a498b3372335bf91fe4a7df02c1d5776395f7c643fc4",
      "source_sha256": "80b92e67594394e38af41b769327936833de8e25d6cf3def966a6ba13bc83d17",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2992962-017",
      "text": "Because smart contracts are coded for computer programming rather than for a human observer, courts may not be able to hypothesize a reasonable human's interpretation of a given smart contract.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "smart-contracts"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "contract interpretation disputes over coded smart contracts"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Because of the emphasis on code for computer programming (and artificial intelligence), courts may not be able to hypothesize a reasonable human's interpretation of a given smart contract.",
      "text_sha256": "4682a07720d8852f6442a71f62277bc6281a6cd15055d891fb491d023f44042b",
      "source_sha256": "80b92e67594394e38af41b769327936833de8e25d6cf3def966a6ba13bc83d17",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2992962-019",
      "text": "Real world court decisions on smart contract disputes, even where attainable, may not carry the same legitimacy and authority for the parties as intra-blockchain dispute resolution mechanisms.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "blockchain",
        "governance-design",
        "systemic-risk"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In other words, real world court decisions even if attainable may not have the same legitimacy and authority as other intra-blockchain dispute resolution mechanism may have.",
      "text_sha256": "9779e15b185c093e9b3a728805349db2df372ba82e247fc0dd09e245fc03c583",
      "source_sha256": "80b92e67594394e38af41b769327936833de8e25d6cf3def966a6ba13bc83d17",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-020",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2992962-020",
      "text": "Even if courts were given authority to order changes to smart contract code, a programmer coerced by a court could not override the will of the majority of anonymous international blockchain users to make an effective change.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized blockchains maintained by an anonymous global user majority"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 17
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-020:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Even if courts were given such authority, no programmer so coerced by the court would be able to override the will of the majority of anonymous international blockchain users to make an effective change.",
      "text_sha256": "a2bf33a9291b446b38f72fbeed8bfdf750de89bbf2546be51627c86f3a95a497",
      "source_sha256": "80b92e67594394e38af41b769327936833de8e25d6cf3def966a6ba13bc83d17",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2992962-035",
      "text": "The economic incentive for Aragon judges to follow the more popular vote, since judges keep their bond only if they voted with the majority, calls into question whether the mechanism delivers effective, non arbitrary, and fair dispute resolution.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design",
        "systemic-risk",
        "law-and-legal-systems"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "the Aragon bond and majority reward mechanism, despite anonymous voting"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-035:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "the economic incentives for judges to follow a more popular vote (in the Aragon system judges keep their bond if they voted with the majority), despite the overall anonymity of the voting, may call required notions of effective, non- arbitrary, and fair dispute resolution mechanisms into question.",
      "text_sha256": "ce4cbc07fb7b577b3a7c5504046911ed19f8e33f3ec4adef572f5ef1df5e61d3",
      "source_sha256": "80b92e67594394e38af41b769327936833de8e25d6cf3def966a6ba13bc83d17",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2992962-039",
      "text": "Because no conceivable way exists to permanently hide an arbiter's reputation from the arbiter in an open system, the corruption risk created by high reputation arbiters becoming valued counselors for disputants is an insoluble problem with the authors' own proposal.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "open reputation systems for anonymous arbiters"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2992962-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Because no conceivable way exists to permanently hide an arbiter's reputation from the arbiter in an open system, this is an insoluble problem with the proposal.",
      "text_sha256": "acd7477d45a4fc3dcf09d34cc3d24b18f9f7d146abcc93d43633328856ff13d4",
      "source_sha256": "80b92e67594394e38af41b769327936833de8e25d6cf3def966a6ba13bc83d17",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2998033-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2998033-001",
      "text": "Blockchain technology lowers transaction costs by eliminating intermediaries, and it substitutes immutability and cryptography for the trust that intermediaries previously supplied.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "economics",
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "citation-and-knowledge"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 53
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2998033-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Blockchain technology's elimination of intermediaries removes transaction costs and creates a platform for trust through truth and transparency for parties through its immutability and use of cryptography.",
      "text_sha256": "6ee0c719d2d5ddc63e5c094655a072d091b79c5bd108a9605151469a6dc92fb6",
      "source_sha256": "aafb1be3c25cd33da477d759df9ca2f856f0a8fe133d6396da2e75d0af573dbd",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2998033-005",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2998033-005",
      "text": "Blockchain creates a data protection paradox: the technology itself offers strong privacy protection, yet storing blockchain data across a global network of nodes will often violate specific consumer protection rules and directives in individual jurisdictions.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies where consumer protection or data protection rules impose jurisdiction specific storage requirements"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 17
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2998033-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While blockchain technology itself offers unprecedented genuine data and privacy protection, the storage of blockchain data across a global network of nodes often will not comply with specific consumer protection rules, directives, and guidelines around the world.",
      "text_sha256": "e2f19e16710eb73b7d7b5a7a2a0ff74cc610251aff497aaa07d6375ac2472d95",
      "source_sha256": "aafb1be3c25cd33da477d759df9ca2f856f0a8fe133d6396da2e75d0af573dbd",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2998033-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2998033-007",
      "text": "The DAO failed because of fundamental flaws in its own code, which allowed hackers to move one third of its funds to a subsidiary account, showing that governance built entirely on smart contracts inherits the defects of its code.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "smart-contracts"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to organizations whose governance and asset control rest entirely on open source smart contract code"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2998033-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Alas, things went terribly wrong with the DAO. Fundamental flaws in the DAO code enabled hackers to transfer one third of the total funds to a subsidiary account.",
      "text_sha256": "3a9567123f97b69f510b0faebcdef30102093574f11c24c0f6799d9ce8d1be0d",
      "source_sha256": "aafb1be3c25cd33da477d759df9ca2f856f0a8fe133d6396da2e75d0af573dbd",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2998033-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2998033-012",
      "text": "The SEC's denial of the Winklevoss Bitcoin exchange traded fund on grounds of susceptibility to fraud reflects the agency's distrust of the crypto asset class as a whole, and especially of funds that trade digital currencies.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "securities-law",
        "tokenomics",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2998033-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The SEC's decision regarding the Bitcoin ETF reflects its distrust towards the crypto asset class as a whole, especially funds attempting to trade digital currencies.",
      "text_sha256": "a3456a5aa242432cc09ee964e6ec771c5dc10916d343392ac75209c38280d499",
      "source_sha256": "aafb1be3c25cd33da477d759df9ca2f856f0a8fe133d6396da2e75d0af573dbd",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2998033-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/2998033-017",
      "text": "Cryptocurrency gains are massively underreported to the IRS: despite Bitcoin rising from under twenty dollars in 2013 to over twelve hundred dollars in 2017, the IRS received only around 900 Form 8949 filings indicating crypto gain or loss over four years.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
