    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:2998097-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Rules can become adaptable if institutions and rulemaking processes integrate feedback effects, including feedback effects between the industry and regulators, that produce timely, relevant, and decentralized information for rulemaking ex- ante before rulemakers finalize rules.137 By increasing the",
