      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3002908-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Private investment funds' bank disintermediation through the implementation of blockchain technology will depend on their ability to find scale opportunities.",
      "text_sha256": "a4c51e19f430069ab59e7b57ccac602794976bd69292b6676faae9c8a2d608bb",
      "source_sha256": "06a7b61e75f905ee07e422e875d83a65c5033a248a6e05a213523b034e5db534",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3002908-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3002908-037",
      "text": "The Northern Trust and IBM blockchain program removes the need for parties to reconcile multiple copies of deal documents by letting every party to a private equity deal look at a single compiled version of the transaction.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "private-funds",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "private equity deal administration, partnership announced February 2017"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3002908-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "which requires parties to reconcile multiples copies of the documents that form the deals to understand the greater picture, the blockchain program announced by Northern Trust and IBM allows all involved parties in an equity deal to look at a single compiled version",
      "text_sha256": "d64b58f258d9bf21553ddb0e02f34dfef13ab2953baaf8b97b1ab7e9dd013b87",
      "source_sha256": "06a7b61e75f905ee07e422e875d83a65c5033a248a6e05a213523b034e5db534",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3002908-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3002908-038",
      "text": "The Numerai model reduces overhead costs because there is no cost of human capital, and it eliminates barriers to entry because participating users need neither capital nor any special finance or data knowledge.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to the Numerai crowdsourced data science model running on the Ethereum blockchain"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3002908-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "reducing overhead costs because there is no cost of human capital.135 In addition, Numerai eliminates barriers to entry because users do not need capital or any special finance or data knowledge.",
      "text_sha256": "f5c68cc8a384a25388d6f90313bd6858b051af4e2ca0f4900c7b1bf9b80df582",
      "source_sha256": "06a7b61e75f905ee07e422e875d83a65c5033a248a6e05a213523b034e5db534",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-005",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3017612-005",
      "text": "Under MBCA Section 7.32 the ten year duration limit is only a default rule, unlike the corresponding limit for voting trusts, so parties who specify a longer term are permitted to have it.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "agreements formed under MBCA Section 7.32"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The section specifies a 10 year limit, a similar period to voting trusts, but unlike voting trusts, this period is just a default rule, so that if the parties specify a longer period it is permitted.",
      "text_sha256": "3c5c53435946c865f3c7746c1c72eb53891d5702ef5daf6bac39539f95bbb8b5",
      "source_sha256": "33821db406f92efbe1698fbaed37687595c13b7ce5463b4a879df679fd4af1ac",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-006",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3017612-006",
      "text": "Duration ceilings contained in voting trust statutes do not carry over to other types of shareholder agreements, and courts have repeatedly sustained shareholder agreements intended to run indefinitely.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "governance-design",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "agreements other than voting trusts"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-006:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Duration limitations in the voting trust statutes do not apply to other types of shareholders' agreements.15 Numerous decisions have sustained shareholders' agreements which were to remain in effect indefinitely.",
      "text_sha256": "899871c108a135d93d36cb8a89a9d49e82f089954137879afae38b605edc66a3",
      "source_sha256": "33821db406f92efbe1698fbaed37687595c13b7ce5463b4a879df679fd4af1ac",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3017612-010",
      "text": "MBCA Section 7.32 requires a writing but, departing from earlier statutes, does not require the agreement to sit in the articles or bylaws, so stand alone written shareholder agreements are expressly valid.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "MBCA Section 7.32 agreements"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The agreement must be in writing, but unlike some earlier statutes, the written agreement does not have to be in the articles or bylaws\u2014stand-alone written agreements are specifically allowed.",
      "text_sha256": "5654fab5c03d3faec38ea68389e0f36c50bde1ab42988537a146bb09a459b84b",
      "source_sha256": "33821db406f92efbe1698fbaed37687595c13b7ce5463b4a879df679fd4af1ac",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3017612-013",
      "text": "Voting arrangements are not self executing: their existence does not relieve the corporation of observing the legal formalities of director and shareholder action.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "voting trusts, pooling agreements, and irrevocable proxies"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Voting arrangements are not self-executing, and the mere existence of a voting arrangement does not mean that the corporation should dispense with the legal formalities of director and shareholder actions.",
      "text_sha256": "78add6504a983ad4102c2ef3730c45d1e99229f5fe61b938646ab22dc6990382",
      "source_sha256": "33821db406f92efbe1698fbaed37687595c13b7ce5463b4a879df679fd4af1ac",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3017612-016",
      "text": "A shareholder suing derivatively sues on the corporation's behalf and cannot convert the action into a personal one, even where the corporate injury has impaired the value of that shareholder's own stock.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "corporate-governance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "injury runs to the corporation"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The shareholders are simply suing on the corporation's behalf and cannot maintain actions on their own behalf to redress an injury to the corporation even if the value of their stock is impaired as a result of the injury.",
      "text_sha256": "91eed7b873610701192bb85df3bd86b948ea8f00a6016fee72674519a6c4d8b4",
      "source_sha256": "33821db406f92efbe1698fbaed37687595c13b7ce5463b4a879df679fd4af1ac",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3017612-031",
      "text": "Where a shareholder agreement is folded into the charter or bylaws, it thereby becomes subject to whatever amendment procedure those documents or the statute provide, so charter integration exposes the arrangement to later modification.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "agreement incorporated into charter or bylaws rather than free standing"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Because shareholder agreements are often designed to avoid corporate formalities such as majority rule, \"it is not unreasonable to require that the degree of deviation intended be explicitly set out.",
      "text_sha256": "f4c68df8b29d4995c8c466b6126e17316b09fd8433bd4857aa53febecddbf658",
      "source_sha256": "33821db406f92efbe1698fbaed37687595c13b7ce5463b4a879df679fd4af1ac",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3017612-033",
      "text": "Shareholders frequently fail to place their agreements in the charter or bylaws, sometimes through ignorance or inadvertence and sometimes deliberately, because charters are public records and the parties prefer not to expose their arrangement to outsiders.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "closely held corporations"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Still, shareholders often fail to include their shareholder agreements in the charter or bylaws\u2014whether by ignorance or inadvertence.124 Sometimes this is intentional because charters are public records, and shareholders may not want their agreements open to outsiders.",
      "text_sha256": "43b338d63c0e7456efc76284b51059a1c3b280ecdf8897183b41095874616001",
      "source_sha256": "33821db406f92efbe1698fbaed37687595c13b7ce5463b4a879df679fd4af1ac",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3017612-034",
      "text": "Absent explicit statutory authorization, many courts have refused to enforce veto provisions contained in shareholder agreements, which is why such provisions should be implemented through charter or bylaw amendment.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "states without statutes specifically authorizing shareholder control agreements",
        "veto or supermajority provisions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "explicit statutory authorization, many courts have refused to enforce veto provisions in shareholders' agreements.",
      "text_sha256": "dc1861ad320aae9a02329b6ba6cda3d4852db506c593f462e913ce0284f0e169",
      "source_sha256": "33821db406f92efbe1698fbaed37687595c13b7ce5463b4a879df679fd4af1ac",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3017612-036",
      "text": "Even though New York decisions such as Adler v. Svingos suggest veto arrangements outside the charter will be specifically enforced, the better practice remains to amend the charter to insert them.",
      "claim_type": "normative",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "New York close corporations",
        "high voting or unanimity requirements"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While shareholders of New York close corporations may be able to set up veto provisions without amending the corporation's charter, the better practice is to amend the charter to insert such arrangements.",
      "text_sha256": "9971360c5b0e5e42c4ba1761e1eb57f3e5a684167c6542a5227074551f46feae",
      "source_sha256": "33821db406f92efbe1698fbaed37687595c13b7ce5463b4a879df679fd4af1ac",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3017612-038",
      "text": "Because damages rarely provide an adequate remedy for breach of a shareholder agreement, refusing specific enforcement amounts in substance to declaring the agreement invalid.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "suits to enforce shareholder voting agreements"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3017612-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Most often a suit for damages does not provide an adequate remedy for a breach of a shareholder agreement, so the denial of specific enforcement essentially declares the agreement invalid.",
      "text_sha256": "92a5869137698664e49ff409aa3f579408e3c32d8929112ba6f96a827a6c08b0",
      "source_sha256": "33821db406f92efbe1698fbaed37687595c13b7ce5463b4a879df679fd4af1ac",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3067615-003",
      "text": "ICOs cannot be qualified as donations and are therefore distinguishable from crowdfunding, because ICO participants acquire a financial stake in the company and, as the case may be, a right to vote on future decisions.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "systemic-risk",
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "comparison of ICOs to crowdfunding platforms such as Kickstarter"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Unlike crowdfunding, ICOs involve a financial stake in the company including, as the case may be, the right to vote on future decisions. Therefore, ICOs cannot be qualified as a donation.",
      "text_sha256": "2eefcda5962a96447731f8adee96941fb5888af36f30cef9fc0df05e3ce0c5f5",
      "source_sha256": "164ce15b9eb1e8847ebcb073f5b23a96b4974ad0308d77469a9455d4a1ebeb38",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-004",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3067615-004",
      "text": "Because Ethereum's decentralized platform incorporating smart contracts lets developers build applications directly on its blockchain, the majority of developers chose to write smart contracts on the Ethereum Virtual Machine rather than create their own blockchain technology, giving ICOs a uniform protocol.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "smart-contracts",
        "open-source-and-code"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "ICO market through 2017"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Given these advantages, the majority of developers opted for writing smart contracts on the Ethereum Virtual Machine rather than creating their own blockchain",
      "text_sha256": "098cb4142d844597bc6820b3e9ca90f90c9d012df666910adf52ba438b8bf67d",
      "source_sha256": "164ce15b9eb1e8847ebcb073f5b23a96b4974ad0308d77469a9455d4a1ebeb38",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-005",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3067615-005",
      "text": "Because whitepapers are not audited by any authority, the preliminary steps of the ICO roadmap, project announcement, executive summary, and investor comments, carry the burden of building market credibility and investor trust in the soundness of the project.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "reputation",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "standard ICO roadmap practice as of 2017"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Whitepapers are not audited by any authority. Therefore these preliminary steps are crucial in order to build a general market credibility and investors' trust in the soundness of the project",
      "text_sha256": "d3115149e79f08e30b38d324787fbe2d97d0e99a4c8d99ed8a27426bf9578bf7",
      "source_sha256": "164ce15b9eb1e8847ebcb073f5b23a96b4974ad0308d77469a9455d4a1ebeb38",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3067615-019",
      "text": "Token holders, unlike shareholders in the traditional corporate infrastructure, cannot vote for or against directors or nominate directors, so ordinary ICO investors have no governance channel and simply must trust the promoters and their business intent.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "corporate-governance",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "typical ICO token structures",
        "ordinary investors as distinct from institutional pre-sale investors"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Further limitations for token holders that amount to significant risk factors include token holders' inability, unlike shareholders in the traditional infrastructure, to vote for or against directors or to nominate directors.",
      "text_sha256": "cfbdac46e289ba0dddf5a37db902c0f5089b66748683b32ecfda2d8276ba7646",
      "source_sha256": "164ce15b9eb1e8847ebcb073f5b23a96b4974ad0308d77469a9455d4a1ebeb38",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-022",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3067615-022",
      "text": "Associated with the lack of an existing product is the inability of most crypto platforms to generate revenue to offset costs the way traditional businesses do, since they typically have neither employees who create and advertise a product nor customers who generate revenue.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "crypto platforms organized as foundations"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-022:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Associated with the lack of an existing product is the inability of most crypto platforms to generate revenue to offset costs like traditional businesses.",
      "text_sha256": "2e2bc523fd643f2976a1392203580b6f3c81229a47275c40ea9032db9192ef6c",
      "source_sha256": "164ce15b9eb1e8847ebcb073f5b23a96b4974ad0308d77469a9455d4a1ebeb38",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-026",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3067615-026",
      "text": "Because token offerings are built on open source code, the utility of an issued token can at any time be recreated in another token with essentially identical features at marginal cost, so investors cannot rely on the implicit promise that promoters and developers will increase the value of the acquired token rather than launch a duplicate.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "open-source-and-code",
        "tokenomics",
        "economics",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "token offerings based on open source software"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-026:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Investors cannot rely on the implicit promise that the token promoters and their developers will increase the value of the acquired token and not create another token with identical features.",
      "text_sha256": "9122669d78de532c627eb6aeb3946b9c9daf7798a9cbc6796201a68806967fae",
      "source_sha256": "164ce15b9eb1e8847ebcb073f5b23a96b4974ad0308d77469a9455d4a1ebeb38",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-027",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3067615-027",
      "text": "Legacy businesses own their code and can sue competitors who copy it, whereas open source crypto start-ups rely only on licenses, and this weaker incentive structure makes ICO investments riskier.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "open-source-and-code",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "open source crypto start-ups compared to legacy code-owning businesses"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-027:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While open-source crypto start-ups have licenses that help protect them from competitor companies who may be using their code for profit, legacy businesses that own their code and can sue competitors who copy such code which provides a different incentive structure and makes ICO investments riskier.",
      "text_sha256": "bfa0ad04274fffa277d9d31c94af100946e38d4ba409112d8d7301d9c353c5ea",
      "source_sha256": "164ce15b9eb1e8847ebcb073f5b23a96b4974ad0308d77469a9455d4a1ebeb38",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3067615-036",
      "text": "The Gnosis ICO shows how a reverse dutch auction can mitigate the inefficiencies and risks of a capped sale: the offering was capped at $12.5 million and the time needed to complete the sale determined the quantity of tokens distributed to investors, with the rest held by the start-up team.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "capped token sales exposed to first mover rush dynamics"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "To mitigate the inefficiencies and the risks of a capped sale, the Gnosis ICO was structured as a reverse dutch auction",
      "text_sha256": "63b24e5da12695fd4e38bf7d2261c559b31250a3dbd127e6531d88c16fde0f1a",
      "source_sha256": "164ce15b9eb1e8847ebcb073f5b23a96b4974ad0308d77469a9455d4a1ebeb38",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3067615-037",
      "text": "ICO promoters should not allow tokens to be traded before the underlying protocol network or application is live, and should not use a landing page that focuses almost exclusively on the ICO while providing less content on the product, project, technology, and team.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "disclosure",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "emerging bad ICO practices identified in 2017"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Such practices include allowing tokens to be traded before underlying protocol network or application is live, using a landing page that focuses almost exclusively on the ICO with project timeline etc. but provides less content on product, project, technology, and team.",
      "text_sha256": "6414406bfd0a86dcd311465d27169b899cf2ef6a2ba23653aeedc41c36e6b7b0",
      "source_sha256": "164ce15b9eb1e8847ebcb073f5b23a96b4974ad0308d77469a9455d4a1ebeb38",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3067615-038",
      "text": "ICO promoters should make significant and ongoing disclosures on vesting and lockup periods and should never manipulate the smart contract to change ICO sales rules mid-course during the offering.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "smart-contracts",
        "governance-design",
        "disclosure"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "ongoing ICO sales governed by smart contracts"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3067615-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Moreover, ICO promoters should include significant and ongoing disclosures on vesting and lockup periods, should never manipulate the smart contract to change ICO sales rules mid-course during the ICO.",
      "text_sha256": "1406cb6dac56d4e1343f131cdce374e2558bc35acf5bd4798fc7680a5fa47d87",
      "source_sha256": "164ce15b9eb1e8847ebcb073f5b23a96b4974ad0308d77469a9455d4a1ebeb38",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3071378-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3071378-001",
      "text": "Blockchain technology delivers anonymous and secure transactional guarantees through democratized trust and disintermediation, and its anti-discrimination features allow minorities and disenfranchised communities to benefit from the technology.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "reputation",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "public, permissionless blockchain networks"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3071378-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Blockchain technology provides anonymous and secure transactional guarantees through democratized trust and disintermediation. Minorities and disenfranchised communities can benefit from the evolving technology and its anti-discrimination features.",
      "text_sha256": "7790e1c918b61329cd862bf30e145fcffa72535847c5d8b1d85c955e2980cd68",
      "source_sha256": "125f01674d13b6bb0310c4be7a20ff538dccbc36ecf352770b3c580028387edd",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3071378-004",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3071378-004",
      "text": "Because network nodes verify and validate chain transactions before execution under a distributed consensus model, recording a fraudulent transaction on the blockchain is extremely rare.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "distributed consensus with node verification before execution"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3071378-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Blockchain's distributed consensus model, e.g., the network \"nodes\" verify and validate chain transactions before execution of the transactions, makes it extremely rare for a fraudulent transaction to be recorded in the blockchain.34",
      "text_sha256": "2547e87c9caee7556015a73f2611607d1f6b2e9a3e97f1189a7cc3d9e753fa39",
      "source_sha256": "125f01674d13b6bb0310c4be7a20ff538dccbc36ecf352770b3c580028387edd",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3071378-005",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3071378-005",
      "text": "Because each new block's hash value is generated from all previous transactions, the smallest change to the blockchain produces a different hash value, which makes any form of manipulation immediately detectable.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "chained cryptographic hashing of prior transactions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 23
    },
    {
