      "id": "kaal:claim:3117224-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3117224-039",
      "text": "World governments largely either apply existing laws to cryptocurrencies or wait to see how other countries react to the crypto evolution.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "top 25 ICO jurisdictions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 13
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3117224-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "For the most part, the general view of the world governments appears to be that they are using existing laws to regulate cryptocurrencies or wait to see how other countries react to the crypto evolution.",
      "text_sha256": "7d05b6598e07dd69a41dcc86d03d4480908adb5b2d36d9cdc9467717c169335c",
      "source_sha256": "83e9ccb9219a217d9fcfc5c098b897229ee7cf85623bee3ae22d2e986548466b",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125822-002",
      "text": "Reputation value in any decentralized reputational system can be corrupted through three channels: direct purchase of reputation, automated worthless work, and degeneration of the system into a majority of inexpert opinions.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized reputation systems",
        "anonymous participants"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 48
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In any such decentralized reputational system there is always the potential to corrupt the value of reputation by purchasing it directly, or through automated worthless work, or through the degeneration of a majority of inexpert opinions.",
      "text_sha256": "ffbb3cd7ef8d2d4e92ad1a5c28a812bd8076cc598249af086d075adfa7733d63",
      "source_sha256": "d4d0bbaa3260968226186131d60e6d64a53e904d94e4295c61fd17042f1191ef",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125822-003",
      "text": "The problems of corruption, Sybil attacks, and tyranny of the majority have plagued every previous autonomous decentralized reputation platform, so they are the design constraints any new architecture must meet.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "prior autonomous decentralized reputation platforms"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 48
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "These are the respective problems of corruption, Sybil attacks, and tyranny of the majority that have plagued all previous autonomous, decentralized reputation platforms.",
      "text_sha256": "8b2e7a6920121337830e695396bd9fdcaeafdb7afe81191631ac694dc3f65686",
      "source_sha256": "d4d0bbaa3260968226186131d60e6d64a53e904d94e4295c61fd17042f1191ef",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125822-010",
      "text": "The chosen expert is deliberately not paid directly out of the fee but only indirectly in newly minted tokens, because the architecture secures itself by making reputation more valuable than any one time payment.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to off-platform work engaged through the platform"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "One counterintuitive element is that the chosen expert is not paid directly in fees, only indirectly in newly minted tokens. The platform was designed to ensure security, and encourage maximal productive cooperation, by valuing reputation over all else.",
      "text_sha256": "074050c4f8be7c1b583867ab91813eb1a7a834bbf49e2a074d56cccaa69a125a",
      "source_sha256": "d4d0bbaa3260968226186131d60e6d64a53e904d94e4295c61fd17042f1191ef",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125822-012",
      "text": "The platform is Sybil attack resistant because all power is weighted by reputation rather than by account: an owner of a single account holding 1000 tokens has the same or more power than an owner of 1000 accounts holding one token each.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "assumes every power in the system is reputation weighted"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 48
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The platform is Sybil attack resistant because all power in the platform is weighted by reputation. An owner of a single account with 1000 tokens has the same or more power than an owner of 1000 accounts with one token.",
      "text_sha256": "6e919bb9a1a4ba125338fb997c3a76fc19f309c375d8f5edb77af903b0428a5e",
      "source_sha256": "d4d0bbaa3260968226186131d60e6d64a53e904d94e4295c61fd17042f1191ef",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-014",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125822-014",
      "text": "Reddit's upvote system imposes insignificant punishment for voting randomly, and this lack of cost compromises the informational value of an upvote, which is the failure mode a staked validation pool is designed to avoid.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to unstaked voting systems"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 57
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-014:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As a second example, Reddit's upvote system currently has insignificant punishment for voting randomly, which compromises the value of the meaning of an upvote",
      "text_sha256": "cbf95cd1ad6372b5394f95f7c43248568f9296eaa0aa99c879d1e2c49f33b3b4",
      "source_sha256": "d4d0bbaa3260968226186131d60e6d64a53e904d94e4295c61fd17042f1191ef",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125822-016",
      "text": "A 51 percent collusion that votes against common sense is visible in an open system, which erodes trust, reduces use and fees, and lowers the value of the attackers' own reputational salary, so the tactic can destroy an expertise tag but cannot enrich the attackers.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "requires an open and observable system",
        "assumes attacker value is held in the attacked tag"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 56
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This would erode trust in the platform, and therefore use and fees would diminish, making the 51% holding of reputational salary less valuable. Therefore this tactic generally has the potential to destroy the expertise tag, but not enrich the attackers.",
      "text_sha256": "4f236f9a681cd5d1bc371b8de4c0bfd357e856ba71770337ba01a4288f828b8c",
      "source_sha256": "d4d0bbaa3260968226186131d60e6d64a53e904d94e4295c61fd17042f1191ef",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125822-018",
      "text": "Healthy expertise tags are secure not because attack is impossible but because it is easier to profit from them by improving them than by harming them.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "economics",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to healthy expertise tags, defined as those generating fees"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 56
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Healthy expertises are secure because it is easier to profit from them by improving them than by harming them.",
      "text_sha256": "95fb5aa9d9d12f7a651a9f7baa5c9989e7b5784c2d162edfbd24ff6b574c2b61",
      "source_sha256": "d4d0bbaa3260968226186131d60e6d64a53e904d94e4295c61fd17042f1191ef",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125822-024",
      "text": "The platform becomes fully autonomous almost immediately after deployment, because once the Ethereum DApp is posted its authors have no more control over the evolution of the expertise tags than any other Ethereum user.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "after the DApp is deployed to the blockchain"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The platform achieves full autonomy almost immediately. Once the Ethereum DApp is posted to the blockchain, its authors have no more control over the evolution of the expertise tags in its forum than any other Ethereum user.",
      "text_sha256": "211035ba5c256b9cc9db523137e952e44b6278ea10a0fed06552de177067df3b",
      "source_sha256": "d4d0bbaa3260968226186131d60e6d64a53e904d94e4295c61fd17042f1191ef",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125822-037",
      "text": "Because absolute certainty is unavailable, the architecture substitutes a calculable probability of confidence built on verified reputation, which is enough for business to proceed even though no provably certain algorithm exists.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "defi"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies where an impossibility result rules out guaranteed fair exchange"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "the architecture provides a means for developing a platform which can give users confidence that business can proceed through a system of verified reputation. This gives a calculable probability of confidence, even if no provably certain algorithm exists.",
      "text_sha256": "8797132cb12bc8cd95a459e6bf76e8e3734118e366c4d7ed583899ca94d8decd",
      "source_sha256": "d4d0bbaa3260968226186131d60e6d64a53e904d94e4295c61fd17042f1191ef",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-040",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125822-040",
      "text": "Faking a reputable expertise tag is nearly costless: a successful tag's open record can be copied and reposted under a new name for the price of the anti denial of service fees, and the capital used to mimic fees paid into the sham tag is mostly recovered by the sham owners through the salaries they control.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "sham owners hold the majority of the sham tag's tokens"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125822-040:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "easily be copied and reposted under a new tag name for the low cost of the anti-DoS fees. The capital used to mimic fees paid to the sham expertise tag is mostly recovered by the sham owners through the salaries they control.",
      "text_sha256": "c5960aca4ccd70c9779c53161e0b739f33ad975394c7af2dd2057557f9a6bfb0",
      "source_sha256": "d4d0bbaa3260968226186131d60e6d64a53e904d94e4295c61fd17042f1191ef",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125827-001",
      "text": "No single, fixed, entirely algorithmic policing solution can completely prevent independent nodes in a distributed system from gaming block production to advantage some parties over others. Any consensus protocol that relies on a permanently fixed rule set will therefore be gamed as conditions change.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "regulatory-failure",
        "blockchain",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "distributed systems with independent, self interested nodes",
        "protocols that are fixed rather than continually revisable"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In fact it is obvious there can be no single, fixed, entirely algorithmic policing solution which completely prevents independent nodes in a distributed system from gaming the system by producing blocks with transactions that advantage some parties over others1.",
      "text_sha256": "a0e58dc8ffa7a7ac5650eb43941f98b235fdcbb5e92eb30f5c4061fafcabd416",
      "source_sha256": "598d9bd95e4af7a0a35328677c6bfc069f69f2e32c30c720b3a0be98a23a40cb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-004",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125827-004",
      "text": "Because all block creation fees are shared with the whole group as a reputation weighted salary, SPoS removes the direct monetary reward for forming mining pools or block production cartels, which the authors identify as a decentralization threat that raises the likelihood of 51% attacks.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "decentralization",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "fees distributed as a reputation weighted salary rather than paid to the producer"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Therefore, unlike every other implemented platform, there is no direct monetary reward incentive for creating mining pools or block production cartels, which are a threat to decentralization which increases the likelihood of 51% attacks.",
      "text_sha256": "25777d1e710a12b1532ba4866fa6c808f6bfa4b22b46aebbd40b4b6ae5cd80f1",
      "source_sha256": "598d9bd95e4af7a0a35328677c6bfc069f69f2e32c30c720b3a0be98a23a40cb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-005",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125827-005",
      "text": "Because the stakes in SPoS are reputation tokens that are far less fungible than cryptocurrency stakes, long term probity is incentivized and many short term arbitrage opportunities are eliminated. Fungibility of the staked asset is what makes short horizon attacks profitable in other proof of stake systems.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "stakes denominated in non fungible reputation tokens rather than currency"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In particular, the stakes (sem tokens) are naturally far less fungible than cryptocurrency stakes, so long-term probity is incentivized, eliminating many short- term arbitrage opportunities.",
      "text_sha256": "cb9d5b046efa28bfa1ff90d10f0d1598747429c002468b9f8dadf50113d034ae",
      "source_sha256": "598d9bd95e4af7a0a35328677c6bfc069f69f2e32c30c720b3a0be98a23a40cb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-006",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125827-006",
      "text": "Staking tokens with the potential for slashing is necessary to avoid the tragedy of the commons in a validation pool. Voting without something at risk does not produce honest evaluation of contributions.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "community voting on the value of contributions",
        "anonymous or pseudonymous participants"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-006:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The staking of tokens, with its potential for slashing, is necessary to avoid the tragedy of the commons.",
      "text_sha256": "dbe1ea99de1c97275816edf6a66d370bd7c4126433b57fe89fbaf343dcde7555",
      "source_sha256": "598d9bd95e4af7a0a35328677c6bfc069f69f2e32c30c720b3a0be98a23a40cb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125827-009",
      "text": "Even though proof of stake mitigates the economy of scale advantage, block production cartels can still arise in PoS systems through lotteries, through built in voting delegations, or because the stakes required to be a block producer can simply be bought.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "PoS systems that use lotteries, delegation, or purchasable stakes"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, block production cartels may still arise due to lotteries, or the fact that voting delegations are built into the system, or the fact that the stakes needed to be a block producer may be bought",
      "text_sha256": "4f06245b8db0d90ddc07445e67d4343ec5bbf007cbf264ed37a689968eb2603c",
      "source_sha256": "598d9bd95e4af7a0a35328677c6bfc069f69f2e32c30c720b3a0be98a23a40cb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-011",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125827-011",
      "text": "If block producers' identities are revealed, the supranational independence and security of the blockchain are threatened, because local jurisdictions can then exert legal power over block production. This threat is most acute in delegated proof of stake, where delegates must win popularity contests.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design",
        "law-and-legal-systems"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "protocols where producers must identify themselves to be chosen",
        "especially delegated proof of stake"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-011:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "identities are revealed, the supranational independence of the blockchain is threatened as is its security. In this case local jurisdictions could exert legal power over block production",
      "text_sha256": "264632357e7e5461df304053693c8f6963d2821e88b2d33e115346df74aaf0ca",
      "source_sha256": "598d9bd95e4af7a0a35328677c6bfc069f69f2e32c30c720b3a0be98a23a40cb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125827-019",
      "text": "Any blockchain whose soft forks are decided through private communication between famous token holding whales is ultimately less secure than legacy centralized systems, which at least address centralized security risks deliberately.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "governance-design",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "off chain governance conducted privately among large holders and developers"
