    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125827-034",
      "text": "Finality in SPoS is measurable because forking away from a given block would cost the community all sem tokens created on the chain after it, and that quantity equals half of all fees sent since the block was produced.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "tokenomics",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "sem minted in proportion to fees on every validated block"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "the sem that members gain from policing block production is equal to half of all fees sent since the production of the block. In order to fork a chain from that particular block, the community will lose all sem tokens created subsequently",
      "text_sha256": "79317d5966d9160d692922c4f34de95d3562b8f831798c6ad5e91afce044c365",
      "source_sha256": "598d9bd95e4af7a0a35328677c6bfc069f69f2e32c30c720b3a0be98a23a40cb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-040",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125827-040",
      "text": "A malicious party using Sybil accounts cannot be prevented from cloning the structure of a successful proof of stake blockchain at far lower cost than cloning a proof of work chain, leaving a new user unable to distinguish the truly decentralized chain from a clone that has manufactured even more tokens. The authors answer that this is resolved off chain, by a trusted user interface, as with cloned web pages.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "new users joining without prior knowledge of the genuine chain",
        "PoS chains where clone creation costs only new public keys"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 63
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-040:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Then, when a new user joins the network, how will they be able to distinguish a truly decentralized blockchain from a cloned blockchain that has manufactured an even larger number of tokens?",
      "text_sha256": "a1a15342ca61c3d998515944b9d1aa7f8904b39e5637a12c4a5ff22e7e0f9efa",
      "source_sha256": "598d9bd95e4af7a0a35328677c6bfc069f69f2e32c30c720b3a0be98a23a40cb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-015",
      "text": "Semada is stipulated as an autonomous, decentralized, open source protocol on the Ethereum blockchain that enables domain specific reputation verification for human task crowdsourcing.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 60
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Semada is an autonomous, decentralized, open-source protocol29 that enables domain specific reputation verification for human task crowdsourcing, built on the ETHEREUM blockchain.",
      "text_sha256": "f69e861e95d9441ee2e602cb46f4b3d1c7bccb53bbf76de8b2720aa5f771031d",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-016",
      "text": "The protocol lowers cost because it removes the manual verification step and the associated multiplication of micro task work that centralized systems require, letting decentralized workers capture the gains from disintermediation.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "micro task crowdsourcing under the Semada Protocol"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "the Semada Protocol removes the manual verification and the associated multiplication of micro task work necessitated by centralized systems, enabling its decentralized micro task workers to profit from the disintermediation.",
      "text_sha256": "f1e1d2f5e6db14dfb3f4e63a2c5d308d3c42b6a1c35c246caceda4ace6ac7f2a",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-017",
      "text": "Reputation tokens supply a staking mechanism that incentivizes high quality work and task completion by workers, and that simultaneously lets requesters verify and track worker quality, integrity, and quantity.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "participants staking reputation tokens on the platform"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 87
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Through the reputation tokens, the Semada Protocol provides a micro task worker reputation staking mechanism that incentivizes high quality work and task completion by workers.",
      "text_sha256": "0a521ab5ff37dee60b817f13e4f5d96e865ac6ab67e4f121da9f1a05077b267e",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-018",
      "text": "Unlike its decentralized competitors, the Semada Protocol is claimed to be resistant to both Sybil attacks and Tyranny of the Majority attacks.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "comparison with existing decentralized mechanical turk protocols"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 65
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, unlike its decentralized competitors, the Semada Protocol ensures Sybil Attack and Tyranny of the Majority attack resistance.",
      "text_sha256": "391ca1a76812d268a01e502239bf1ebb63ef1a2aabae4861df03a360ac5f7b41",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-019",
      "text": "The protocol architecture together with its incentive structure is what produces enhanced 51 percent attack resistance, which the author claims exceeds prior reputation verification attempts in both decentralized and centralized networks.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation verification networks"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 77
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The Semada Protocol architecture and its incentive structure facilitates enhanced 51% attack resistance unlike any previous reputation verification attempts in decentralized and centralized networks.",
      "text_sha256": "e65b5d5d5057493881d76c85dc8496dd1b3c41e21ccb948cf292f3b1544bed91",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-023",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-023",
      "text": "Rather than repeating the same task across many workers to reach quality, the architecture verifies quality directly by examining and validating individual worker task performance through reputation verification.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "micro tasks routed through the reputation verification architecture"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 70
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-023:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Instead of repeating work on given tasks to attain high quality work products for micro tasks, Semada uses an architecture of reputation verification that examines micro worker task performance and verifies the validity and quality of the work.",
      "text_sha256": "ba5551661e84ce2ff26b44e3f2a905314d17adff366e7981244ec968a639c471",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-024",
      "text": "Staking creates disincentives for malicious actors, and it is this disincentive structure that makes the network both more efficient and attack resistant.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "workers and verifiers who have reputation tokens at stake"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 74
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Semada staking mechanism creates disincentives for malicious actors, enhancing the efficiency of the Semada Network and making it attack resistant.",
      "text_sha256": "5258c7e8874d16e25e758c2b51d4f2f843ab85400d905514a6ab80b1e187a471",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-037",
      "text": "Attack resistance should be designed to increase as the platform grows, in contrast to designs like GEMS that detect and ban malicious actors, because a self enforcement mechanism lets the incentive system steer users away from bad actors once the system matures.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "compliance",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "after the system reaches maturity"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 74
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Unlike GEMS, which bans malicious actors detected through the GEMS trust mechanism from the platform, the Semada platform has a self-enforcement mechanism.",
      "text_sha256": "6b07adc051822d27c518e6669a51b73774928679d00421ddc3cb9df91cc599fa",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-045",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-045",
      "text": "Centralized platforms cannot simply drop identity verification, because they need it to keep malicious actors from abusing the network and to ensure work quality; this is the tradeoff a staking based design is meant to dissolve.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "centralized micro task platforms"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 64
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-045:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, centralized micro task platforms need to verify identity to prevent malicious actors from abusing the network and ensure work quality.",
      "text_sha256": "2a43089b86d9a883388b8cbb71b6ca488dd4743152b11fa8ce591dcf01fa0675",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-046",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-046",
      "text": "Because the reputation token staking mechanism supplies attack resistance directly, users need not verify their identity to complete micro tasks, which circumvents the costs, delays, and privacy surrender attached to centralized identity verification and thereby enlarges the willing labor pool.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "workers staking reputation tokens rather than proving identity"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 75
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-046:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "By contrast, on the Semada Platform, users do not need to verify their identity to complete micro tasks. The Semada Protocol architecture, and specifically its reputation token staking mechanism, make the Semada Platform attack resistant.",
      "text_sha256": "738f9e0381878f9f5a4288d573b6cda5f5d338441f11e62c62d96457e6737ed7",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227933-003",
      "text": "Centralized, hierarchical organizations fail on two fronts in a fast changing environment: they adapt too slowly to changing reality and they are losing public trust.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "fast-changing reality"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Most obviously, such organizations are slow to adapt to a fast-changing reality and are losing public trust.",
      "text_sha256": "02e1e41764b18da36f43eab0ba545a60372fa4922e7b59312924ea3f89ccaddc",
      "source_sha256": "a9e9660c4dc25a2202f1da4e762f5885256e05f68c53ca51942f5833a7a4c108",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227933-013",
      "text": "Peer-to-peer transactions are possible because a distributed consensus model has network nodes verify, validate and audit transactions before and after execution, and this is often safer than routing transactions through a single trusted third-party intermediary.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "blockchain",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "\"Peer-to-peer\" transactions are possible because the technology uses a \"distributed consensus model\" where the network \"nodes\" verify, validate and audit transactions before and after they are executed.",
      "text_sha256": "373228ca4c8b3db4a86dcd73298ad1745f3373e1f85bc57ca240466f2fdd5485",
      "source_sha256": "a9e9660c4dc25a2202f1da4e762f5885256e05f68c53ca51942f5833a7a4c108",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227933-016",
      "text": "Blockchain technology creates an independent and transparent platform for establishing truth and building trust, replacing intermediaries, bureaucracy and old procedures with what the authors call the four Cs of code, connectivity, crowd, and collaboration.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In short, blockchain technology creates an independent and transparent platform for establishing truth and building trust. Intermediaries, bureaucracy, and old-fashioned procedures are replaced by the \"4 Cs\" of code, connectivity, crowd, and collaboration.",
      "text_sha256": "db4e4d57775f3cf1018cda218238d8eb8dd1d695037ee63e7d82a9246c9434d2",
      "source_sha256": "a9e9660c4dc25a2202f1da4e762f5885256e05f68c53ca51942f5833a7a4c108",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-027",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227933-027",
      "text": "Centralized organizations also lose the competition for talent, because the younger generation views centralization as a threat to personal autonomy, choice and happiness and is increasingly sceptical of traditional hierarchies.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "younger, Millennial workforce"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-027:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The younger \"Millennial\" generation view centralization as a threat to personal autonomy, choice, and happiness.",
      "text_sha256": "d5623cf7352fd0e1bc0de1828a951a2f1a7e09642a4615bec2d9119c91481ef1",
      "source_sha256": "a9e9660c4dc25a2202f1da4e762f5885256e05f68c53ca51942f5833a7a4c108",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227933-029",
      "text": "The design premise of the DAO was that because people do not always follow rules even when the rules are well designed, it is better to use computer code to manage an organization.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "organizations aiming to automate governance"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The DAO intended to automate governance and was based on the idea that since \"people\" don't always follow the rules (even if the rules are well-designed), it is better to use computer code to manage an organization.",
      "text_sha256": "ef0c2f4162fdf6a40ae8729668fbb673d274cc6d3235c8896aa03b8ba54e1955",
      "source_sha256": "a9e9660c4dc25a2202f1da4e762f5885256e05f68c53ca51942f5833a7a4c108",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227933-030",
      "text": "The DAO showed that a corporate-type organization can operate with no physical address, no directors, no managers and no employees, with its governance structure built entirely from software, code and smart contracts running on Ethereum.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "smart-contracts"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "the DAO, 2016"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Indeed, the DAO didn't have any directors, managers or employees. The governance structure was built with software, code and smart contracts that ran on the public decentralized blockchain platform, Ethereum.",
      "text_sha256": "f80fd667555d94dade56ac1e92a1f0aa4feafc1a2881dcd36b1ef7b963396b61",
      "source_sha256": "a9e9660c4dc25a2202f1da4e762f5885256e05f68c53ca51942f5833a7a4c108",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227933-032",
      "text": "In a DAO, blockchain-based smart contracts granting token holders voting rights perform the function that articles of association or bylaws perform in a conventional corporation.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "smart-contracts",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "A series of smart contracts granted the holders of the tokens voting rights. In this respect, the blockchain-based smart contract mimicked the role of articles of association or bylaws.",
      "text_sha256": "a607f409a1b066b2fb4c73915efb1761fb84ff8335de20cbe816d40c0fb9cc81",
      "source_sha256": "a9e9660c4dc25a2202f1da4e762f5885256e05f68c53ca51942f5833a7a4c108",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227933-033",
      "text": "A DAO inhibits rent-seeking and delivers transparency because its governance protocols are open source, so weaknesses are constantly tested and revised in the open rather than hidden inside a managerial hierarchy.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "dao",
        "open-source-and-code"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "open source governance protocols"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Such an organization inhibits \"rent-seeking\" and offers transparency. And they are secure. For instance, the governance protocols used in a DAO are open source and weaknesses are constantly tested and revised.",
      "text_sha256": "2ac7e225262b87156f43a9c7c0d7125a9c7e805671ac0f391a07bd6af22d1620",
      "source_sha256": "a9e9660c4dc25a2202f1da4e762f5885256e05f68c53ca51942f5833a7a4c108",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227933-035",
      "text": "Fundamental flaws in the DAO's code allowed hackers to transfer one third of the total contributed funds to a subsidiary account, and this together with other technological limitations ended the initiative, but the authors argue it did not end the underlying vision of decentralized autonomous organization.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "the DAO, 2016"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-035:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "To be sure, fundamental flaws in the DAO code made it possible for hackers to transfer one-third of the total contributed funds to a subsidiary account. This, and other technological limitations meant the end of the initiative",
      "text_sha256": "9ae4c42ef592cab751d00e67e40b2ad3efa47e61b3def1b30e0f604357b94474",
      "source_sha256": "a9e9660c4dc25a2202f1da4e762f5885256e05f68c53ca51942f5833a7a4c108",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227933-038",
      "text": "Issuing coins or tokens across all ecosystem participants creates a level playing field and helps establish a flatter, community-owned platform that is not based on the traditional hierarchies between shareholders, executives, managers and staff.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "well-designed token distribution across ecosystem participants"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227933-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As such, the issuance of coins or tokens creates a \"level playing field.\" Crucially, this helps establish a flatter, \"community-owned\" platform, which isn't based on traditional hierarchies between the platform participants",
      "text_sha256": "3af642f0557f9f50a4d176c511ee920e356752933ad3bcffb14b4a0c863c869c",
      "source_sha256": "a9e9660c4dc25a2202f1da4e762f5885256e05f68c53ca51942f5833a7a4c108",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227967-010",
      "text": "The result of this pattern is reputational: lawyers have developed a reputation as the least trusted of professions.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "education-and-practice",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 41
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As a result, lawyers have developed a reputation as the least trusted of professions.",
      "text_sha256": "aff475ad7f33b3c42b7568869ea1828a4e643cc4ed242765b54c4a621a6b03ac",
      "source_sha256": "f6e13b956f864ab32ec3305d095a35a127770327d75b3688f785cefc437d369f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227967-018",
      "text": "Because blockchain network nodes verify, validate and audit transactions both before and after execution, the model is safer than a traditional one in which transactions can only be accomplished through third party intermediaries such as a bank, judiciary or notary.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "decentralization",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "peer to peer networks using a distributed consensus model"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "verify, validate and audit transactions before and after they are executed. 49 This is safer than a traditional model in which transactions can only be accomplished through third-party intermediaries, such as a bank, judiciary or notary.",
      "text_sha256": "d463e19329111abb3983a771064d6a45fab0700a774f7716d9e5db294e22b736",
      "source_sha256": "f6e13b956f864ab32ec3305d095a35a127770327d75b3688f785cefc437d369f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-023",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227967-023",
      "text": "A decentralized autonomous organization is merely computer code with no directors, managers or employees, its governance structure built with software, code and smart contracts running on a public decentralized blockchain platform.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "smart-contracts",
        "blockchain",
        "governance-design",
        "corporate-governance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "DAOs built on public platforms, in most cases Ethereum"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-023:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "DAOs are \"merely\" computer code. They don't have any directors, managers or employees. The governance structure is built with and on software, code and smart contracts that ran on a public decentralized blockchain platform (in most cases Ethereum).",
      "text_sha256": "b3c1c3a093ce99c6dc1d0b671c3fe2dcd70960f123fce53edb8ce13d28a2aa5c",
      "source_sha256": "f6e13b956f864ab32ec3305d095a35a127770327d75b3688f785cefc437d369f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-027",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227967-027",
      "text": "In a digital world trust can be embedded directly in software code, and recent interest in smart contracts suggests this will be a significant growth area in the near future.",
      "claim_type": "predictive",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "smart-contracts"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "digital transactions where code can carry contractual terms"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-027:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In a digital world, trust can be embedded in software code. Recent interest in smart contracts suggests that this is going to be a significant growth area in the near-future.",
      "text_sha256": "e7b3ae12a6ca58b1d1ef98ec73db9332fa91d9fd97f520c1e80b8c6d09897202",
      "source_sha256": "f6e13b956f864ab32ec3305d095a35a127770327d75b3688f785cefc437d369f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227967-028",
      "text": "As machine to machine interaction becomes normal in an Internet of Things environment, trust ceases to be primarily a legal question and becomes a technical and design problem.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "machine to machine transactions in an Internet of Things environment"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "code is also crucial in machine-to-machine (M2M) based transactions. As M2M interaction becomes normal in an Internet of Things environment, the issue of trust becomes a technical and design problem.",
      "text_sha256": "beb9bd02c33dd9ac980450a11aa18015de2589de5ade7115a18fe37800d0befb",
      "source_sha256": "f6e13b956f864ab32ec3305d095a35a127770327d75b3688f785cefc437d369f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227967-030",
      "text": "Building lawyers' capacity to think about the social and ethical implications of code is both essential and inevitable, but saying anything sensible about the ethics of technology first requires understanding coding and coders.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "education-and-practice",
        "open-source-and-code",
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "ethical questions raised by automation, artificial intelligence and driverless vehicles"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Building the capacity of the lawyers of the future to think about the social and ethical implications of code is both essential and inevitable. But, to say something sensible about the ethical aspects of technology, it is necessary to understand both more about coding and coders.",
      "text_sha256": "b4b01afdb1997fb4e32dd0b31280fde23c495fa67f4cb03cb2802ff0f6d0b2b7",
      "source_sha256": "f6e13b956f864ab32ec3305d095a35a127770327d75b3688f785cefc437d369f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227967-032",
      "text": "Existing blockchains and DAOs still lack genuine decentralization, and there are currently no true DAOs: Bitcoin's proof of work protocol has produced mining pools because of economies of scale and unbalanced reward structures.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "dao",
        "decentralization",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "proof of work blockchains as of 2018"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In our discussion, the following weaknesses were highlighted. There is still a lack of decentralization (there are currently no \"true\" DAOs). For instance, Bitcoin's proof of work protocol has led to \"mining pools\" because of economies of scale and unbalanced reward structures.",
      "text_sha256": "b87eb1560a8e74cc4f29ced261a5dcb29cf15cdc3479b2e12b8905d45a918dcf",
      "source_sha256": "f6e13b956f864ab32ec3305d095a35a127770327d75b3688f785cefc437d369f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227967-035",
      "text": "A reputation verification platform matters because trust created through an eternal reputational record would be open to review and driven by proper incentives.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "blockchain",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "blockchain based reputation systems that reward trustful parties and punish bad actors"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-035:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This was considered to be important because if the trust were to be created through an eternal reputational record, it would be open to review and driven by proper incentives.",
      "text_sha256": "c686dd27e8799b2da5915ca253e0b1ad6d65657265352aed58e100cde1e4af54",
      "source_sha256": "f6e13b956f864ab32ec3305d095a35a127770327d75b3688f785cefc437d369f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227967-036",
      "text": "The real design challenge for consensus protocols is to find a proof of stake protocol that offers both trust and security without unintentionally creating just another centralized validation system.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "decentralization",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "blockchain consensus protocol design"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The students understood that the real challenge is to find a \"proof of stake\" protocol that offers both trust and security (without unintentionally creating just another centralized validation system).",
      "text_sha256": "a96ded0bac367b8f6e35bb35924fa56bd57210c44136d9dced103522690b415d",
      "source_sha256": "f6e13b956f864ab32ec3305d095a35a127770327d75b3688f785cefc437d369f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3227967-038",
      "text": "Coders and developers do not always understand the industry or business environment they target with their software solutions, nor do they always consider the trust or ethical issues raised by the technology based business solutions they implement.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "education-and-practice",
        "reputation",
        "open-source-and-code"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "technology based business solutions built by developers"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3227967-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Coders, programmers, and other developers do not always understand the industry or business environment they target with their software solutions. Nor do they always consider the trust or ethical issues when implementing technology-based business solutions.",
      "text_sha256": "1168e614411e75c9c23dd1a5015fa2d4763eeec273e59724195a3cb1234cfc87",
      "source_sha256": "f6e13b956f864ab32ec3305d095a35a127770327d75b3688f785cefc437d369f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3249860-003",
      "text": "Crypto-economics is arguably a misnomer, since it is really just economics; what may legitimate the label is the unprecedented combination of disciplines required to analyze incentive designs in decentralized systems.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Crypto-Economics really is just economics and, in fact, may be a misnomer.",
      "text_sha256": "aa1a2b8602874a04fe57c6992e7e83cfc77567b4559e15678716f629d452c015",
      "source_sha256": "72b13f11002ba26206cd53e74c324b913d1830c642bfa024da6bac0d3af3a7b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-005",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3249860-005",
      "text": "DAOs can replace the coordination and monitoring functions supplied by the firm, because they can measure each member's contribution to the finished work product more efficiently and allocate rewards accordingly.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "compliance",
        "reputation",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "supported by trust enhancing technologies such as reputation verification in decentralized anonymous systems"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 41
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Arguably, DAOs can replace the otherwise needed functions that are supplied by the firm that acts as the coordinator and monitor of a team because DAOs can more efficiently measure the contribution of each DAO member to the finished work product and allocate respective rewards accordingly.",
      "text_sha256": "19133b65ec1e5d88c81fa203189755bfd9908f30e6ed9cb45b8e49910b0caa50",
      "source_sha256": "72b13f11002ba26206cd53e74c324b913d1830c642bfa024da6bac0d3af3a7b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-006",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3249860-006",
      "text": "In decentralized systems the functions previously performed by policy designers, central bankers, and economists in centralized markets are taken over by the token designer for the respective token economy.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "systemic-risk",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-006:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Whereas policy designers, central bankers, and economists previously coordinated market design and economic regulations in centralized systems, these functions are taken over by the token designer for the respective token economy.",
      "text_sha256": "cb02614d32ec567f6cb01738139fdadb4e85eb9f3f9cc256ba3a1c7fb718a1ff",
      "source_sha256": "72b13f11002ba26206cd53e74c324b913d1830c642bfa024da6bac0d3af3a7b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3249860-017",
      "text": "Many token whitepapers omit information necessary for a full economic analysis, and the research team could not find a single project among the top 100 that had examined blockchain governance fully.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "disclosure",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "whitepapers of the top 100 cryptocurrencies by market capitalization as of April 2018"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Many whitepapers do not include all the information that would generally be necessary for a full economic analysis. For instance, the researchers could not find a project that had examined blockchain governance fully.",
      "text_sha256": "3ac2a828f5dbdebdc5cc1bee25b56360cb60c9fa831a5214e410f33333b0a82d",
      "source_sha256": "72b13f11002ba26206cd53e74c324b913d1830c642bfa024da6bac0d3af3a7b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3249860-038",
      "text": "Proof of Work remains the most popular consensus protocol type among the top 100 tokens, and the Other category alone comprises thirty-four tokens.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "empirical-evidence"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "N=100 dataset; consensus time series n=97"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Figure 9a shows that the \"Other\" consensus protocol type, made up of thirty-four tokens.",
      "text_sha256": "c9e7bcc83a75b1de9100bef46903f4e89e35fc8230172f98c3dd8a67f59b83e6",
      "source_sha256": "72b13f11002ba26206cd53e74c324b913d1830c642bfa024da6bac0d3af3a7b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3249860-039",
      "text": "Attempts to increase throughput and scale in consensus protocols concentrate on proof of stake, and the data are consistent with anecdotal evidence that proof of stake may be the most dominant attempt at scaling.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "empirical-evidence"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "top 100 tokens by market capitalization"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Attempts to increase throughput and scale for consensus protocols often focus on proof of stake attempts. The data is consistent with anecdotal evidence that suggests that proof of stake may be the most dominant attempt at scaling.",
      "text_sha256": "a87fedb97ce838b4bf9799cd8a0e0d792b1d2af0c1dba8acd7891297aaa356d8",
      "source_sha256": "72b13f11002ba26206cd53e74c324b913d1830c642bfa024da6bac0d3af3a7b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-040",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3249860-040",
      "text": "To date no blockchain coherently and comprehensively combines scale, security, and decentralization, the three objectives of the blockchain trilemma, although continued experimentation with consensus algorithms can help overcome it over time.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "as of the study's 2018 data"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-040:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "To date, no blockchain truly combines these three objectives coherently and comprehensively. Experimentation with different consensus algorithms can, over time, help overcome the blockchain trilemma.",
      "text_sha256": "198386fc17123c410d16bc8c584ae8ab6297c12f5b3b63b741e39c53d3b936c1",
      "source_sha256": "72b13f11002ba26206cd53e74c324b913d1830c642bfa024da6bac0d3af3a7b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-041",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3249860-041",
      "text": "Tokens experimenting with alternative consensus protocols typically change the transfer process in an effort to become more efficient.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "outlier consensus protocols among the top 100 tokens"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-041:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Tokens experimenting with alternative consensus protocols often change the transfer process in an effort to become more efficient.",
      "text_sha256": "820c2d6f0da2ef4b9cc82f6cf3d95013f7ea5070feb487246867879511091fc3",
      "source_sha256": "72b13f11002ba26206cd53e74c324b913d1830c642bfa024da6bac0d3af3a7b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-042",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3249860-042",
      "text": "Tokens launched before 2015 were overwhelmingly developed on a hardfork governance mechanism or a combination of hardfork and one other governance type.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "empirical-evidence"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "top 100 tokens, governance types coded as hard fork, soft fork with tokenholder voting, masternodes, or other"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-042:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Tokens launched prior to 2015 were overwhelmingly developed on a hardfork or a combination of hardfork and one of the other governance types depicted.",
      "text_sha256": "fa86a574b5bae4b38598f35ee2b75ae27107a08ea53c324ce18d6c8424898dce",
      "source_sha256": "72b13f11002ba26206cd53e74c324b913d1830c642bfa024da6bac0d3af3a7b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-043",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3249860-043",
      "text": "Outlier governance mechanisms rose sharply in the dataset: three per year in 2015 and 2016, then eighteen in 2017, and five in the first six months of 2018.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "empirical-evidence"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "governance types coded as other"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3249860-043:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "During 2015 and 2016, three outlier tokens were launched per year. These tokens were Tether, Factom, and Iota; DigixDAO, Gas, and Ark. During 2017, this figure jumped to eighteen tokens.",
      "text_sha256": "bb943e95b7567b6414293fc1a78b06749f9c1b82e4b88edd0df88e7abdf47379",
      "source_sha256": "72b13f11002ba26206cd53e74c324b913d1830c642bfa024da6bac0d3af3a7b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-005",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3266953-005",
      "text": "Today's internet is designed for hierarchical societal structures on an underlying authoritative trust model, and that traditional hierarchical trust model carries many inefficiencies including serious cyber security vulnerabilities.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 55
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Worse yet, today's internet is designed for hierarchical societal structures and with an underlying authoritative trust model. Many inefficiencies are associated with the traditional hierarchical trust model including serious cyber security vulnerabilities.",
      "text_sha256": "64c9e8f617ac8498928b47e08f1d9682e76812ee6441117ccd417aaefa608933",
      "source_sha256": "781758dea356e55d79c73ad7f1debe7c83de398bd1cd9e0a9a6c2802f276b4c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3266953-008",
      "text": "Every centralized reputation score can be sybil attacked, because fake internet accounts or fictitious ratings disrupt true reputation scoring.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "decentralization",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "centralized reputation scoring systems"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 55
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "All centralized reputation scores can be sybil attacked, e.g. fake internet accounts (sockpuppets) or fictitious ratings disrupt true reputation scoring",
      "text_sha256": "8dddd709a6910fcc5480a5927df916bf2c44763d126fb7268396269415f9489d",
      "source_sha256": "781758dea356e55d79c73ad7f1debe7c83de398bd1cd9e0a9a6c2802f276b4c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3266953-009",
      "text": "Users on internet based platforms earn their reputation but do not own it, so if a platform deletes an account, years of reputation data disappear and users have near zero ability to reclaim it.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "centralized platforms such as Facebook"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Users earned their reputation but do NOT own reputation - e.g. if Facebook and other internet-based platform businesses accidentally deleted user account, years of data would be removed and users have near zero ability to reclaim the data",
      "text_sha256": "5307a00adcdcf0ff12361b012ddbc9131fcee6175a7b9a43b6754348eb9c3297",
      "source_sha256": "781758dea356e55d79c73ad7f1debe7c83de398bd1cd9e0a9a6c2802f276b4c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
