    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "giving the proper incentives for guaranteeing secure proof-of- stake consensus protocols for block production. This eliminates the unsustainable inefficiencies of proof-of-work based blockchains.",
      "text_sha256": "7351288eb5717f3e87995cfb3d63cc4bc92db4161ad42cce2fbce6dbad18c22c",
      "source_sha256": "781758dea356e55d79c73ad7f1debe7c83de398bd1cd9e0a9a6c2802f276b4c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3266953-018",
      "text": "Semada replaces fungible currency staking with reputation staking for block propagation, a consensus algorithm the authors call Semada Proof of Reputation.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Semada platform block propagation"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 61
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Block propagation in the Semada platform is facilitated by staking reputation, not a fungible currency as in PoS. Accordingly, the consensus algorithm is called Semada Proof of Reputation (PoR).",
      "text_sha256": "9e795ac374b5d389174b17b4148106c2a3c4c3180f2618e3254a114230f1d548",
      "source_sha256": "781758dea356e55d79c73ad7f1debe7c83de398bd1cd9e0a9a6c2802f276b4c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-021",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3266953-021",
      "text": "Because Semada's Anchor Protocol uses reputation scores as a non fungible currency to qualify for block propagation, the resulting proof of reputation consensus is attack resistant, fully decentralized, scalable, and open to evolutionary protocol upgrades.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation scores that cannot be transferred"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 61
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-021:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Unlike traditional PoS, PoR, e.g. Semada's Anchor Protocol, uses reputation scores as a non-fungible currency to qualify for block propagation. As such, the Anchor protocol (PoR) is attack resistant, fully decentralized, scalable and allows evolutionary protocol upgrades.",
      "text_sha256": "86c83c1d7e88ca47519c4e6763be98e9caff83c5a720e595b2b197d3f49f7523",
      "source_sha256": "781758dea356e55d79c73ad7f1debe7c83de398bd1cd9e0a9a6c2802f276b4c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3266953-028",
      "text": "A Web of Trust reputation system can be gamed with sockpuppet accounts, because an attacker can behave well for a while and then transact with himself repeatedly and rate himself high to raise his reputation arbitrarily.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "regulatory-failure"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation systems based on counting positive peer rated transactions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 57
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "If I use a lot of sockpuppet accounts, I can raise my reputation arbitrarily high, by behaving well for a while, then making a lot of transactions with myself and rating myself high.",
      "text_sha256": "50dccaf74f8c3270d83cf808a35990dd777cb94eeabc400b88abe5df6fa3ca09",
      "source_sha256": "781758dea356e55d79c73ad7f1debe7c83de398bd1cd9e0a9a6c2802f276b4c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3266953-030",
      "text": "The other horn of the identity verification dilemma is that when reputation is not valuable, honest users will not bother to go through the hoops required to identify themselves securely.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "low value reputation systems"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 57
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "If the reputation is not valuable, then you won't be able to get honest users to go through the hoops required to identify themselves securely, since it",
      "text_sha256": "5aaa6ce2d3ece1bbca15b870c2e6b768ae88943881f23ba3fb20adf9b1a8f337",
      "source_sha256": "781758dea356e55d79c73ad7f1debe7c83de398bd1cd9e0a9a6c2802f276b4c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3266953-032",
      "text": "In an economic network where real money is at stake, historical good behavior cannot be assumed to prove future good behavior, because sockpuppet accounts allow participants to game the system automatedly, create valuable reputation falsely, and leach value out of the system.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "regulatory-failure",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "networks where trust must support real monetary value"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 57
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "you can't just assume their historical good behavior will prove their future behavior will also be good. Sockpuppet accounts allow us to automatedly game the system and falsely create valuable reputation, so we can leach whatever value there is out of the system.",
      "text_sha256": "110cbb9ee6048652890c2036a9aace9073e174195b88fe560d39473a39a29c2c",
      "source_sha256": "781758dea356e55d79c73ad7f1debe7c83de398bd1cd9e0a9a6c2802f276b4c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3266953-034",
      "text": "Semada's voting algorithm is designed so that gaming the system is not economically feasible without contributing genuinely valuable improvements, because value is proven through the fees added to the system and every fee is subject to a fair validation pool.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "fees attached to each contribution",
        "validation pool review of every fee"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 59
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The voting algorithm of Semada core is designed to combat that very system, so that it is not economically feasible to game the system without adding genuinely valuable improvements, as proven with the fees that are added to the system and the fair validation pool that every fee is subject to.",
      "text_sha256": "c32d7bf3360b26fc6855cb422e5a9ff4d99e75cca068ab58c92ecc073fb09551",
      "source_sha256": "781758dea356e55d79c73ad7f1debe7c83de398bd1cd9e0a9a6c2802f276b4c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3373393-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3373393-007",
      "text": "Agency problems originate from the lack of trust between principals and agents, which itself stems from information asymmetries and agents' opportunistic self-interested behavior.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "disclosure"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
