    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396522-007",
      "text": "JPM Coin's closed structure, restricting the token to existing J.P. Morgan clients, is an anachronism, because closed ecosystems are unsustainable in emerging decentralized commerce.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to permissioned stable cryptocurrencies limited to a single institution's clients"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The close structure of the JPM coin, e.g. JPM makes it only available to existing clients, appears to be an anachronism.95 Closed ecosystems are unsustainable in the emerging decentralized commerce.",
      "text_sha256": "7853c2b3c755e24b5dff73bc914cf053faf5f65313f304579f78c2d14889dc85",
      "source_sha256": "ef5031b16aa53476ed618f0bdf92601cd4affb893692c701134bd9cba3ea8acf",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396522-009",
      "text": "A fiat backed stable cryptocurrency that is not fully collateralized is exposed to arbitrage trade attacks of the kind George Soros used against the pound sterling; full collateralization is therefore a necessary defense.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to stable cryptocurrencies claiming a fiat peg"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Without a 100% fiat collateralization, such projects would run the risk of arbitrage trade attacks similar to what Financier George Soros used to \"break the bank of England",
      "text_sha256": "6a6f22bbb9622b018f5507720556088970c0dfad7712fcb2b877c2a2ae39bf9b",
      "source_sha256": "ef5031b16aa53476ed618f0bdf92601cd4affb893692c701134bd9cba3ea8acf",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396522-010",
      "text": "Fiat currency collateralization is expensive and inefficient because the entire backing value must be held liquid; anything less opens arbitrage opportunities of the Soros type.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "defi",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "assumes the backing must remain fully liquid to prevent arbitrage"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Fiat currency collateralization is expensive and inefficient because all of the value that is backing the cryptocurrency needs to be liquid, otherwise arbitrage opportunities, such as the Soros attack, are possible.",
      "text_sha256": "776576c9f6a4b9bf8773190a6d0106c4cb3b425559edce57f7b3a892e8bcec11",
      "source_sha256": "ef5031b16aa53476ed618f0bdf92601cd4affb893692c701134bd9cba3ea8acf",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396522-015",
      "text": "A well established stable cryptocurrency and a universal exchange form a positive feedback loop: the exchange's liquidity is enhanced by the stable cryptocurrency, and the stable currency's stability and adoption are enhanced by the exchange.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "defi",
        "institutional-design",
        "tokenomics",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "requires a universal exchange bridging traditional and crypto assets"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In essence, the combination of a well- established stable cryptocurrency with a universal exchange create a positive feedback loop. The exchange liquidity is enhanced by the stable cryptocurrency and the stability and adoption of the stable currency is enhanced through the exchange.",
      "text_sha256": "6455bbf9728232aa03eeb1dc1923b9fed35048ca0880221897d54d03fe40e0ca",
      "source_sha256": "ef5031b16aa53476ed618f0bdf92601cd4affb893692c701134bd9cba3ea8acf",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-025",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396522-025",
      "text": "Because hardcoded cryptocurrency policy is transparent and therefore predictable, market participants can anticipate policy and adjust behavior in advance, and such anticipatory reactions could over time make actual policy making the exception rather than the rule.",
      "claim_type": "predictive",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "tokenomics",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "assumes policy rules remain largely hardcoded and transparent"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Because of this transparency and associated predictability, market participants can anticipate policy making and adjust behavior accordingly. In fact, such anticipatory policy reactions could, over time, make actual policy-making the exception rather than the rule.",
      "text_sha256": "df6cad61ad49ad2ff8353871365608a9c9bee74480be5d73fef497dc6a8fe7ff",
      "source_sha256": "ef5031b16aa53476ed618f0bdf92601cd4affb893692c701134bd9cba3ea8acf",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-026",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396522-026",
      "text": "Full hardcoding is impossible: no stable cryptocurrency can encode all required policies and policy actions with full transparency, because future policy needs cannot be anticipated ex ante.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-026:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "No stable cryptocurrency can hardcode all required policies and policy making actions with full transparency as future policy cannot be fully anticipated ex ante, before the needs occur.",
      "text_sha256": "1ed11db23527b3aa22e85790314337219b22a15e80706ab49d97cce479350438",
      "source_sha256": "ef5031b16aa53476ed618f0bdf92601cd4affb893692c701134bd9cba3ea8acf",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-027",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396522-027",
      "text": "Monetary policy for stable cryptocurrencies should combine hardcoded transparent rules with protocols enabling decentralized autonomous organizations, with decentralized but fully transparent policy DAOs functioning as the policy makers for what cannot be hardcoded.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "tokenomics",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "depends on DAO governance designs that address expertise and incentive problems"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-027:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "monetary policy for cryptocurrencies can additionally be supported by protocols enabling decentralized autonomous organizations (DAOs).152 Decentralized but fully transparent policy DAOs can help function as policy makers.",
      "text_sha256": "dd35a2fd3cec084f322069dc98fef09f3540572111d93cc2b96e48fc3676fec1",
      "source_sha256": "ef5031b16aa53476ed618f0bdf92601cd4affb893692c701134bd9cba3ea8acf",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396522-029",
      "text": "The interoperability deficit in cryptocurrency markets is partly intrinsic to blockchain technology itself, because the consensus mechanism that allows block propagation on one chain in some ways negates interoperability with other chains and their consensus.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "blockchain",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The lack of interoperability can in part be traced back to blockchain technology itself. The consensus created to allow block propagation in some ways negates interoperability with other chains and their consensus.",
      "text_sha256": "ee8e83b37dec4e001a8c10afc422bd0354c3d1688e93b4a806ba0a19ee1d8b33",
      "source_sha256": "ef5031b16aa53476ed618f0bdf92601cd4affb893692c701134bd9cba3ea8acf",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396522-036",
      "text": "Mass adoption fails at the user level: the average user will not identify, research, and purchase diverse sets of tokens even where those tokens would create value, because the existing cryptocurrency market structure is simply too cumbersome.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "economics",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The average user is unwilling to identify, research, and purchase diverse sets of tokens, even if their application and use cases would create value. The existing market structure for cryptocurrencies is simply too cumbersome for the average user.",
      "text_sha256": "a008aee0d711b318dcda988f8a0c16104caf0015c3a57e37cdb03e76bf9c7273",
      "source_sha256": "ef5031b16aa53476ed618f0bdf92601cd4affb893692c701134bd9cba3ea8acf",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396522-039",
      "text": "Near instant settlement with stable cryptocurrencies removes counterparty risk, and the resulting reduction in counterparty risk boosts consumer confidence and increases transactional certainty relative to systems like Visa that take five to seven business days to pay merchants.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396522-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Such speed in settlement takes away the counterparty risk and with less counterparty risk, speed of settlement with cryptocurrencies boosts consumer confidence and increases certainty for transactions.",
      "text_sha256": "03ca56ac97192830764f7858da2abdf29e96f830c20f61962ecba73d43377b4b",
      "source_sha256": "ef5031b16aa53476ed618f0bdf92601cd4affb893692c701134bd9cba3ea8acf",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-004",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396542-004",
      "text": "The reputation tokens of the underwriting DAO are separate and distinct from the cash currency that insureds use to pay premia; the two must not be conflated.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "It is important to note that the reputation tokens are separate and distinct from the cash currency that the insured use to pay their premia.",
      "text_sha256": "6b4a87a90e9bd811cc242c0269159f7ca55068eefc2fea01cda882eaef4eab7b",
      "source_sha256": "ce2bda03a0b788ea3e7747f02c3c351ef7c808a41150d5cda34767bbe98800c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-005",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396542-005",
      "text": "Tokens in the proposed DAO function as reputation because an agent's proportional token holdings will grow over time only if that agent follows sound and successful underwriting practices.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "dao",
        "defi"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "tokens are minted as rewards for staking on underwritten policies"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "We will refer to these tokens on occasion as reputation tokens as an agent's proportional holdings of these tokens is likely to increase over time only if the agent were to follow sound and successful underwriting practices.",
      "text_sha256": "7e0977fd1de905bbf3c90d2a72f5ab4d83cec805dbec144ba948893edf3d87c4",
      "source_sha256": "ce2bda03a0b788ea3e7747f02c3c351ef7c808a41150d5cda34767bbe98800c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-006",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396542-006",
      "text": "Participation in underwriting is gated by token ownership: only token holders may underwrite insurance policies in the DAO, and inbuilt processes assign new business among them.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "defi"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-006:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "First, only token holders are allowed to participate in underwriting insurance policies. Inbuilt processes are used to assign new business to token holders.",
      "text_sha256": "02329f2bd26b9e7669440054504fae1be103f88eb2cd8a56393e0586c0dba802",
      "source_sha256": "ce2bda03a0b788ea3e7747f02c3c351ef7c808a41150d5cda34767bbe98800c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396542-007",
      "text": "Insurance premia are treated as revenue of the entire DAO rather than of the underwriters who wrote the policy, and are shared among DAO participants; consequently the value of a token is a function of the DAO's expected future cash flows.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "economics",
        "dao",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Instead, the premia are treated as the revenue of the entire DAO and shared among the DAO participants. Thus, the value of the tokens is a function of the expected future cash flows of the DAO.",
      "text_sha256": "a1e41649fd077d1eaeec5df6c23be14d3644ac2e12d2fd2b479cd2e1a9e506e2",
      "source_sha256": "ce2bda03a0b788ea3e7747f02c3c351ef7c808a41150d5cda34767bbe98800c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396542-008",
      "text": "Because newly minted reward tokens go only to agents who stake tokens on policies, passive holders are diluted over time, which pushes agents toward active underwriting while still permitting passive investment.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reward tokens minted per policy underwritten"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Thus, the total number of tokens grows over time. This implies that \"passive\" agents who hold the tokens purely to receive a share of future premia will find their proportional ownership in the DAO decrease over time.",
      "text_sha256": "425d64237c4c8f25efeb5709327c67dc647099a0f8f62ecc66f263df21433fbb",
      "source_sha256": "ce2bda03a0b788ea3e7747f02c3c351ef7c808a41150d5cda34767bbe98800c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396542-016",
      "text": "Unlike prior token research, the purpose of issuing tokens here is not only to raise capital but also to give owners the opportunity and incentive to develop the DAO's business.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Another key difference is that in our study, the purpose of issuing tokens is not only to raise capital but also to provide the owners the opportunity and incentive to develop the business of the DAO.",
      "text_sha256": "88d9a2d1c1ee4dbc91bdb91d650ff2b5e027e0efc3dbd2159ce8bb895ab89552",
      "source_sha256": "ce2bda03a0b788ea3e7747f02c3c351ef7c808a41150d5cda34767bbe98800c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396542-033",
      "text": "The design's innovative features stem from tokens serving several purposes at once: as reward for risk taking and as a substitute for both reputation and capital.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In sum, many of the innovative features of this design stem from the fact that the tokens serve multiple purposes: as reward for risk- taking, and a substitute for reputation and capital.",
      "text_sha256": "efdba9eaf9e9dacf276cd031d943055218e6742b1bd4b72ae47bf912ce9eb0e4",
      "source_sha256": "ce2bda03a0b788ea3e7747f02c3c351ef7c808a41150d5cda34767bbe98800c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396542-034",
      "text": "Trust requirements in the DAO are minimized by appropriately designed economic incentives rather than by intermediary reputation or regulation.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "dao",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
