      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The need to trust is minimized by appropriately designed economic incentives.",
      "text_sha256": "74cdecb45560ed40563b84b509ef7dee70641ddb3b3aa3e549e084bbbd2470ea",
      "source_sha256": "ce2bda03a0b788ea3e7747f02c3c351ef7c808a41150d5cda34767bbe98800c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396542-035",
      "text": "The governance rules of the DAO can be set up so as to ensure that minority token holders are appropriately protected.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-035:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The governance rules of the DAO can be set up so as to ensure that minority token holders are appropriately protected.",
      "text_sha256": "a197c84d7aeb2cd09c3ec360331bb82d03577573364920870231c86d58ddaf4a",
      "source_sha256": "ce2bda03a0b788ea3e7747f02c3c351ef7c808a41150d5cda34767bbe98800c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3396542-036",
      "text": "Assuming all agents are active underwriters, the DAO's rules can be designed so that the proportion of policies an agent writes in the long run is commensurate with that agent's proportion of token holdings.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "defi",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "all agents are active underwriters"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3396542-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In general, assuming all agents are active underwriters, the rules can be designed to ensure that the proportion of policies written by an agent in the long run is commensurate with the proportion of the agent's token holdings.",
      "text_sha256": "e46327de3679baf9fc8bd7b66bce657acec38a24e821405dd3ef4c5ba42f390d",
      "source_sha256": "ce2bda03a0b788ea3e7747f02c3c351ef7c808a41150d5cda34767bbe98800c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3402701-007",
      "text": "Good governance principles are crucial to every aspect of a long-term stable currency because markets inevitably change and because the Folk Theorems of game theory pose a fundamental obstacle to any fixed protocol.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "long-term stable currency designs"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Most importantly, good governance principles are crucial for every aspect of instituting any long-term stable currency due to inevitable changes in the market and the fundamental obstacle represented by the Folk Theorems of game theory",
      "text_sha256": "0eb8d94895ac4dae1587ab373b7eec5db402e2161c1ab2adeccbc092a22ffbdc",
      "source_sha256": "72ed2581b4cac2bd18a5b2640be959487a3cbc34c86ab5e5664924bcdb53c8e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-011",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3402701-011",
      "text": "The Folk Theorems of game theory imply that no matter how complicated a stable coin protocol becomes, a powerful and patient player has strategies to subvert the system and profit at the expense of the group.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "economics",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "any fixed protocol, however complex"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-011:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "No matter how complicated the protocols become for creating a stable coin, there are strategies that a powerful and patient player can use to subvert the system to profit at the expense of the group",
      "text_sha256": "0f02cee8c4e38d235c596b3e271a4f5a24bb976378055851f77a468d3e467fc0",
      "source_sha256": "72ed2581b4cac2bd18a5b2640be959487a3cbc34c86ab5e5664924bcdb53c8e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-020",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3402701-020",
      "text": "The reserve argument depends on two requirements, and failing either one grounds a criticism of an existing protocol: the stable-value requirement criticizes MakerDAO and the maintenance-cost requirement criticizes the Reserve protocol.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reserve held in a volatile asset",
        "reserve maintenance cost exceeds arbitrage profit"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-020:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The first requirement leads to a criticism of the MakerDAO protocol (e.g.), the second requirement leads to a criticism of the Reserve protocol (e.g",
      "text_sha256": "65637879b56e83c240303c06add8088c8f54062824325b86708e65c2683557f5",
      "source_sha256": "72ed2581b4cac2bd18a5b2640be959487a3cbc34c86ab5e5664924bcdb53c8e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3402701-024",
      "text": "Misestimating the hot money ratio fails in both directions: overestimation makes the currency more costly to use, and underestimation leaves it insecure, so efficiency and security are in direct tension.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "economics",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "A currency that overestimates this hot money ratio will cost more to use. A currency that underestimates the ratio will be insecure",
      "text_sha256": "fc5d2ecc79c8caf26a51fe9e7b15b6c869e83fa7e9bd69f3689c3169a5e062e2",
      "source_sha256": "72ed2581b4cac2bd18a5b2640be959487a3cbc34c86ab5e5664924bcdb53c8e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3402701-032",
      "text": "The day-to-day stability mechanism can be fully automated by algorithm, but monetary and fiscal policy choices cannot be: the algorithm's parameters must be chosen by hand and adjusted regularly to balance security against efficiency.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "stability mechanisms operating in changing markets"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, monetary and fiscal policy choices cannot be fully automated. The parameters for the algorithm must be chosen by hand and adjusted regularly to balance security with maximal efficiency in response to network performance",
      "text_sha256": "f6af9069907d90c29000175aef1ce9ffa86041e1177fc98b2502ab5aa69ddcb8",
      "source_sha256": "72ed2581b4cac2bd18a5b2640be959487a3cbc34c86ab5e5664924bcdb53c8e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3402701-033",
      "text": "Parameter and policy choices for a stable cryptocurrency should be made by a decentralized autonomous organization, the Stability DAO or SDAO, which functions as a transparent, decentralized, open analog of the US Federal Reserve.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "decentralization",
        "dao",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 53
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Such choices need to be made by a decentralized autonomous organization, which we call the Stability DAO or SDAO",
      "text_sha256": "c8694151658a90170dcd0e9583c96342254bc7a2d2f60f491b4046f4f0d0a6ab",
      "source_sha256": "72ed2581b4cac2bd18a5b2640be959487a3cbc34c86ab5e5664924bcdb53c8e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3402701-035",
      "text": "Transparency is not an unqualified good for monetary policy: a currency only partially backed by reserves can be arbitraged by a Soros-style shorting strategy much more easily when the quantity of reserves is public.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "partial reserve backing",
        "reserve quantities publicly known"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-035:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "For instance, a currency partially backed by reserves can be successfully arbitraged by Soros' shorting strategy much easier if the quantity of reserves is known",
      "text_sha256": "2a92a321ab8d127868b547695d276ed20a69d2fdbd0d21f628acc8d7093f7e5a",
      "source_sha256": "72ed2581b4cac2bd18a5b2640be959487a3cbc34c86ab5e5664924bcdb53c8e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3402701-036",
      "text": "The Folk Theorems of game theory prove that no protocol, however complex or well engineered, can eliminate corruption, understood as behavior that profits a minority at the greater expense of the majority.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Finally, we repeat the idea that the Folk Theorems of game theory prove that it is impossible to create protocols, no matter how complex or well- engineered, which can eliminate corruption",
      "text_sha256": "c475274ddf4071c21aced04e50eb66c98dbf4862ca3ad0bdc494cc3ba8bb8d9f",
      "source_sha256": "72ed2581b4cac2bd18a5b2640be959487a3cbc34c86ab5e5664924bcdb53c8e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3402701-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3402701-039",
      "text": "Commonly held expressions of organizational values are essential to designing and implementing any governance structure and are far more important in decentralized organizations, which inherently have less motivational structure than centralized hierarchies.",
