    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-014:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Trust barometers, such as the Edelman report, assessing the level of trust in centralized institutions suggests radical depreciation in trust between the years 2017 and 2018.",
      "text_sha256": "fbf92c09f3cfa09d3387ac4cfe37d90c7d486d0adf6554894636cd3033081038",
      "source_sha256": "bc2d6f0ddc0852fb4085c4543c7c1dec19aaf8745eb67e3acc637e552bd7fb7d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405401-015",
      "text": "Although smart contracting in decentralized systems is perceived as creating trust through preordained coded coordination without agency problems, decentralized commerce is equally afflicted with trust issues.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "decentralization",
        "smart-contracts"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 63
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While smart contracting in decentralized system can be perceived as creating trust through mathematical and coded \u2014 preordained coordination without agency problems, several factors suggest that decentralized commerce via decentralized solutions is equally afflicted with trust issues.",
      "text_sha256": "9ad505162b15402b7f3bb17c1d5aa3451c72ae943485020ddaae7b1507940846",
      "source_sha256": "bc2d6f0ddc0852fb4085c4543c7c1dec19aaf8745eb67e3acc637e552bd7fb7d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405401-016",
      "text": "Trust between counterparties in decentralized systems can only limitedly be assured by smart contracts, because the contract cannot verify the underlying qualities or future conduct of the parties.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "smart-contracts",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized systems with anonymous counterparties"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Trust between counterparties in decentralized systems can only limitedly be assured by smart contracts.",
      "text_sha256": "1d292430fdb128933d95f975bfa4734f6098d25911764f4ad32b3c36ecbcd024",
      "source_sha256": "bc2d6f0ddc0852fb4085c4543c7c1dec19aaf8745eb67e3acc637e552bd7fb7d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405401-017",
      "text": "Smart contracts leave counterparty information asymmetries unresolved: the tenant of a smart property cannot fully know whether the landlord is providing a worthy property, and the landlord cannot know in advance how likely the tenant is to destroy the premises.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "smart property rental scenario"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In our example above, the tenant of the smart property cannot fully know if the landlord is providing a worthy property. In turn, the landlord cannot know in advance how likely the tenant will destroy the premises.",
      "text_sha256": "5b7cf91df15d6814c4b46c4d545d1b45ab7ed38f1fe01f1bb6f8258ceef65fe2",
      "source_sha256": "bc2d6f0ddc0852fb4085c4543c7c1dec19aaf8745eb67e3acc637e552bd7fb7d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405401-018",
      "text": "Counterparty trust in the programmed parameters of a smart contract is more justified in simpler contracts, and specifically where the smart contract template has a history of successful executions.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "smart-contracts",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "simpler smart contracts",
        "template has a prior record of successful executions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 56
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In simpler smart contracts such trust may be more justified if the smart contract template has a history of successful executions.",
      "text_sha256": "eba74401f1b9700455f36135aad42f04b93a676bf1778656824ddf2af6aa8646",
      "source_sha256": "bc2d6f0ddc0852fb4085c4543c7c1dec19aaf8745eb67e3acc637e552bd7fb7d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405401-019",
      "text": "In more complex smart contracts the counterparties cannot fully know whether the contract will do what it was programmed to do, or whether it will contain bugs or follow a logic the parties did not anticipate.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "smart-contracts",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "more complex smart contracts"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 54
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In other words, in more complex smart contracts, the counterparties to the contract cannot fully know if the contract will do what it was programmed to do and whether it will have bugs or otherwise follow another logic that was not anticipated by the parties to the contract.",
      "text_sha256": "fbaa5a7d0b750fe9cbf1099efedc42d295587c6afff231b8e9c16c108f5a121a",
      "source_sha256": "bc2d6f0ddc0852fb4085c4543c7c1dec19aaf8745eb67e3acc637e552bd7fb7d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-021",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405401-021",
      "text": "Solving the trust problem in decentralized commerce requires an intangible value system, not a further transferable store of value.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized commerce"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-021:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "To solve the issues of trust in decentralized commerce, an intangible value system is needed.",
      "text_sha256": "f40819ae04f8c112b155d24c4e05a75746aecb76f0ed34c17376afa41df4a315",
      "source_sha256": "bc2d6f0ddc0852fb4085c4543c7c1dec19aaf8745eb67e3acc637e552bd7fb7d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405401-028",
      "text": "Until blockchain technology was introduced via bitcoin in 2009, decentralized reputation systems mostly relied on the old and corruptible concept of the Web of Trust.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "period before 2009"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Until blockchain technology was introduced via bitcoin in 2009, decentralized reputation system mostly relied on the old and corruptible concept of the Web of Trust.",
      "text_sha256": "8e165b0364f63fbf761607c58b98d3e4cfdd31430fcd30a95cd4ac579b3c4010",
      "source_sha256": "bc2d6f0ddc0852fb4085c4543c7c1dec19aaf8745eb67e3acc637e552bd7fb7d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405401-031",
      "text": "Validated smart contract templates increase trust for counterparties and remove the need for costly back testing and experimentation with smart contract templates.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "smart-contracts"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "templates have been validated through reputation verification"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 56
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Validated templates of smart contracts increase trust for counterparties. The validation removes the need for costly back-testing and experimentation with smart contract templates.",
      "text_sha256": "f32e6b15ccb79af5636d438a632c98cb7e1942fa164a61650a887dcd13fee240",
      "source_sha256": "bc2d6f0ddc0852fb4085c4543c7c1dec19aaf8745eb67e3acc637e552bd7fb7d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405401-033",
      "text": "Truly increasing counterparty trust in decentralized smart contract based commerce requires that counterparties be able to review a long history of each other's conduct in decentralized commerce and of performance in earlier smart contracts.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized smart contract based commerce"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405401-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "To truly increase trust for counterparties in decentralized smart contract-based commerce, counterparties need to be able to review a long history of each other's conduct in decentralized commerce and the history of performance in earlier smart contracts.",
      "text_sha256": "6952495458e5950a2bf4e79c534335c42a3d55deb1f72d091df00b53ffcb11ad",
      "source_sha256": "bc2d6f0ddc0852fb4085c4543c7c1dec19aaf8745eb67e3acc637e552bd7fb7d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-006",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405660-006",
      "text": "LTCM was diversified across markets but not across strategy, so its positions failed together; market level diversification does not imply strategy level diversification.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "systemic-risk",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "private-funds"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "stress conditions in which risk spreads widen across markets simultaneously"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 13
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-006:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "It became obvious that while the fund was diversified in terms of markets, its overall strategy was not diversified.",
      "text_sha256": "fe56e1810471a0f45c6cd12f13b4ba5327de684571861d0fc77f228f3590cabc",
      "source_sha256": "cf507b1833071765bc13a5605f38c2591582eca85f40869e38b6ff075c04d29d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405660-007",
      "text": "Conventional risk models understated LTCM's losses because the models were estimated during more stable periods and therefore did not describe behavior under stress.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "models calibrated on data from stable market periods",
        "subsequent stress conditions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 13
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "markets greatly exceeded what conventional risk models suggested were probable, but these were estimated during more stable periods.",
      "text_sha256": "a0c841f82e755ce7d1aa4cd71cde62f9e6a8151428260979296b0a6c0f73c262",
      "source_sha256": "cf507b1833071765bc13a5605f38c2591582eca85f40869e38b6ff075c04d29d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405660-008",
      "text": "The same leverage that produced LTCM's high returns magnified its losses, so leverage is a symmetric amplifier rather than a one directional source of performance.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "private-funds",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 11
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In spite of the fact that leverage was key to LTCM \u0301s high returns, it also magnified LTCM \u0301s losses.",
      "text_sha256": "a0701f05ff0d672510f3483b911b3e8104bd38e9555bd27d9c933ab4013338d3",
      "source_sha256": "cf507b1833071765bc13a5605f38c2591582eca85f40869e38b6ff075c04d29d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405660-009",
      "text": "Before its collapse LTCM held roughly $4.8 billion in capital while controlling $160 billion in stocks and bonds, with derivatives of a notional value of $1 trillion.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "empirical-evidence",
        "systemic-risk",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "position as of the period immediately before the 1998 crash"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 11
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "LTCM had $4.8 billion in capital prior to the crash and controlled $160 billion in stocks and bonds. In addition, derivatives of the fund had a notional value of $1 trillion.",
      "text_sha256": "b22a5d92c2a190a236c7dff3e5d7e6ba3afe0bd46fa57323324466efc06bcbaf",
      "source_sha256": "cf507b1833071765bc13a5605f38c2591582eca85f40869e38b6ff075c04d29d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405660-010",
      "text": "Hedge fund disclosure to counterparties and investors relies on balance sheet concepts that are uninformative about the actual nature of market risk and credit risk exposures.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "economics",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "private-funds"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 11
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Disclosure by hedge funds to counterparties and investors are often made by using balance-sheet concepts, which are not informative about the nature of the exposures to market risk and credit risk.",
      "text_sha256": "66d9f04230d026fd1760cf0835553b2115fb4e75bb06516867fc3481cf8ea558",
      "source_sha256": "cf507b1833071765bc13a5605f38c2591582eca85f40869e38b6ff075c04d29d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-011",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405660-011",
      "text": "LTCM reached systemically dangerous size because banks lent to it without regard to repayment capacity, and in doing so the banks endangered their own existence.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "systemic-risk",
        "defi",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 11
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-011:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "LTCM grew as large as it did because banks lent it money without regard for whether this money could be paid back. Banks put their own existence at risk with their lending practices during this time.",
      "text_sha256": "2e4872f23d8f51136de6be807cc067337e1d03f050252eccc4d3fbbe07c528ef",
      "source_sha256": "cf507b1833071765bc13a5605f38c2591582eca85f40869e38b6ff075c04d29d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-014",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405660-014",
      "text": "Additional direct limitations on hedge funds spill over onto other private investment pools such as venture capital funds and structured financings, which do not present the same systemic risk concerns.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "innovation",
        "systemic-risk",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "rules drafted broadly enough to capture private investment pools generally"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 11
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-014:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The imposition of additional limitations on hedge funds can impose unwarranted burdens on other types of private investment pools, such as venture capital funds and structured financings that do not raise the same concerns as hedge funds in terms of systemic risk.",
      "text_sha256": "7e6883afa22a75e38f7158729cdbc8febda4c4345805a5040003c1bfdb9c4b81",
      "source_sha256": "cf507b1833071765bc13a5605f38c2591582eca85f40869e38b6ff075c04d29d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3405660-018",
      "text": "The complex trading, investing and corporate structures of active international hedge funds are a major constraint on effective prudential supervision.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "internationally active hedge funds with complex group structures"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 13
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3405660-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "One of the major constraining factors that constricts effective prudential supervision of hedge funds is the complex trading-, investing- and corporate structure of active international hedge funds.",
      "text_sha256": "dd3e766b921d0f4bd0f809414a72f2657a97cb94805cc6ab2f865ffa06e6f8dd",
      "source_sha256": "cf507b1833071765bc13a5605f38c2591582eca85f40869e38b6ff075c04d29d",
