    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411110-003",
      "text": "Blockchain reduces counterparty credit risk through a specific mechanism: a single shared ledger compresses the settlement cycle so that cash or securities are verifiably in the account within seconds of the trade, leaving almost no window for counterparty default.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "a single shared ledger used across trading firms",
        "near instantaneous settlement"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "credit risk is reduced because cash (if selling) or the securities (if purchasing) are in the account for verification shortly after the trade (which could be seconds, if not fractions of a second), because the settlement cycle is substantially reduced.",
      "text_sha256": "33953c33066de57481c4011f23f940d59428ff13fb0f93a7090bd5799c76674f",
      "source_sha256": "c7626eeb7642045b79f8745df1f7232a8fe8bc44a1f7e87b592850e35b392b50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411110-007",
      "text": "Because direct ownership on a blockchain removes the need for the Depository Trust Corporation to hold the certificate and for a broker to record beneficial ownership, agency costs can be cut and ownership clarity increases.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "corporate-governance",
        "decentralization",
        "defi"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "direct registration of ownership on the ledger",
        "no third party custodian"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "By establishing a system that makes the DTC obsolete, agency costs have the potential to be cut and clarity surrounding ownership will increase.",
      "text_sha256": "94dc94aee41fe9ed215c3ba43a8c5176e98ae53169645ee5c27bbb3d21cacb37",
      "source_sha256": "c7626eeb7642045b79f8745df1f7232a8fe8bc44a1f7e87b592850e35b392b50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411110-012",
      "text": "Transfer agents become unnecessary in blockchain based trading models because every function they perform, including maintaining the holding record, can be automated in code and is already produced by the ledger's design.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "decentralization",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "fully blockchain based trading and settlement models"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In blockchain- based trading models, transfer agents will not be needed because every task they preform can be automated through coding.",
      "text_sha256": "5af8929589c2a77ea702fa130e964e16c1986fe7c60aad53134059412b1e7918",
      "source_sha256": "c7626eeb7642045b79f8745df1f7232a8fe8bc44a1f7e87b592850e35b392b50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411110-013",
      "text": "The double spending problem has not been eradicated in theory: a group or syndicate obtaining 51 percent control of a network could reverse transactions and create a private chain that the market could only limitedly discern as not real.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "a decentralized network where one party can amass majority hashing control"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "There is the possibility a group or syndicate could gain 51% control over the network and would therefore be able to reverse transactions and create a private blockchain, which the market could only limitedly discern as not real.",
      "text_sha256": "2a7d8d2ca53ce48905358f5a3eeafbfb51dfc072f0ea4ada78a803ab0462a9ee",
      "source_sha256": "c7626eeb7642045b79f8745df1f7232a8fe8bc44a1f7e87b592850e35b392b50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-020",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411110-020",
      "text": "Blockchain based offerings introduce technology risks from code design and functioning and from third party intrusions that are generally absent in traditional offerings, and these risks cannot really be quantified.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "blockchain based offerings compared with traditional offerings"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-020:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Technology-based risks include risks from the design and functioning of code, and from third-party intrusions. Such risks are generally not present in a traditional offering.",
      "text_sha256": "deef0f3265316c21fbe1a3f6fa6c9fd7979103e0711abb34141b2fa657152d25",
      "source_sha256": "c7626eeb7642045b79f8745df1f7232a8fe8bc44a1f7e87b592850e35b392b50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-026",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411110-026",
      "text": "Near instant settlement creates its own regulatory problem: there is no practical ability to correct trade errors when settlement is same day, whereas the T+2 or T+3 structure supplies a correction window even as its delay causes other trading violations.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "same day or near instant settlement compared with T+2 and T+3"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-026:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Settlement-related issues (e.g., no practical ability to correct trade errors because of same-day / near-instant settlement versus T+3 / T+2 structure).",
      "text_sha256": "947d47a214f809cd3da6291897dd2594995c560c2d42ceb93b8b3af0a0a1ce28",
      "source_sha256": "c7626eeb7642045b79f8745df1f7232a8fe8bc44a1f7e87b592850e35b392b50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-027",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411110-027",
      "text": "Despite an early call for regulatory leadership from Commissioner Stein in 2015, the SEC has not addressed core recognition questions for blockchain in finance, including cryptocurrencies, tokens as securities, and DAOs as investment advisers.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "securities-law",
        "tokenomics",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "SEC action between 2015 and the time of writing"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-027:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Despite this early cautioning and call for action, the SEC has not yet addressed core issues pertaining to the recognition of blockchain technology applications in finance.",
