      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The SEC's decision regarding the Bitcoin ETF reflects its distrust towards the crypto asset class as a whole, especially funds attempting to trade digital currencies.",
      "text_sha256": "a3456a5aa242432cc09ee964e6ec771c5dc10916d343392ac75209c38280d499",
      "source_sha256": "c7626eeb7642045b79f8745df1f7232a8fe8bc44a1f7e87b592850e35b392b50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411110-037",
      "text": "Development of blockchain based processes will take several years if not decades, so the most likely outcome is that legacy and blockchain based issuance, trading, and settlement systems coexist side by side for the foreseeable future.",
      "claim_type": "predictive",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "transition period for securities market infrastructure"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "will take several years if not decades, and so the most likely circumstance is that legacy and blockchain-based securities issuance, trading, settlement, and related systems and processes will have to co-exist side-by-side for the foreseeable future.",
      "text_sha256": "1c0414b7f96b9ba4cfe6161e1c3381df00e28b96aa9de489a74c8f6d0d427cac",
      "source_sha256": "c7626eeb7642045b79f8745df1f7232a8fe8bc44a1f7e87b592850e35b392b50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411110-039",
      "text": "The Overstock structure fails to deliver investor privacy, because all existing broker-dealer customer agreements contain provisions allowing the broker-dealer to share the customer's identity, whereas ideally the individual's privacy would be contained.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "existing broker-dealer customer agreements"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411110-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "For instance, all existing broker-dealer customer agreements included provisions which allows the broker-dealer to share the identity of the customer. Ideally, the privacy of the individual would be contained.",
      "text_sha256": "100347878695721f679f841f93fb4e2def012ea87e151f9cfc71873eac9f2299",
      "source_sha256": "c7626eeb7642045b79f8745df1f7232a8fe8bc44a1f7e87b592850e35b392b50",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411897-003",
      "text": "Decentralized systems mutate and change easily because their information flow is optimized through dynamic feedback effects, and this capacity to mutate is what makes them more attack resistant on multiple levels.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "institutional-design",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "holds for systems whose information flow is genuinely distributed"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Decentralized systems can also very easily mutate and change because the information flow is optimized through dynamic feedback effects. As a result, such systems become more attack resistant on multiple levels.",
      "text_sha256": "6b5de249ee6891d6a2ecb4d5ab299abcae9c6b83ce8d801150cb4b11503c7cdb",
      "source_sha256": "82f0aea026b3e3a526ec51bc073b3b864dc06cd9083ff9c54c550037045edaa9",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411897-007",
      "text": "eBay's user rating system, despite being its biggest competitive advantage, is clearly flawed, and the persistence of those flaws demonstrates the unmet need for a decentralized reputation verification system, since no better technology has yet been produced.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to centralized platform reputation systems as of 2019"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While the user ratings eBay uses clearly have flaws (that illustrate the need for a decentralized reputation verification system \u2013 discussed in Chapter 6), so far, nobody has been able to come up with a better technology.",
      "text_sha256": "926e71e229f9529289bd60e05c0d6bacbed2e308ed750accea3884e2fac150c9",
      "source_sha256": "82f0aea026b3e3a526ec51bc073b3b864dc06cd9083ff9c54c550037045edaa9",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411897-008",
      "text": "Decentralized Autonomous Organizations challenge the core belief that governance necessitates agency, attacking organizational design at a fundamental level rather than merely reforming it.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to DAOs built on smart contracting platforms such as Ethereum"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While it is still difficult to imagine a world without governance structures facilitated by agency constructs, Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs) have started to challenge the core believe that governance necessitates agency.",
      "text_sha256": "f1d6c15c04cd3e45cfe158e246e10ad807a44c9d39745a1a4f7261797b7dd3ee",
      "source_sha256": "82f0aea026b3e3a526ec51bc073b3b864dc06cd9083ff9c54c550037045edaa9",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-022",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411897-022",
      "text": "DAOs are in their infancy and cannot currently overcome core governance problems while maintaining a decentralized structure; the two objectives are, as of 2019, in tension.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "state of DAO technology as of 2019"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-022:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "DAOs are in their infancy and cannot currently overcome core governance problems while maintaining a decentralized structure.",
      "text_sha256": "b95567a06e776b4dd51281614c5577af25653893ce601db5e0af55a87e986339",
      "source_sha256": "82f0aea026b3e3a526ec51bc073b3b864dc06cd9083ff9c54c550037045edaa9",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411897-034",
      "text": "The flexibility that human business requires will unlikely ever be attained in existing decentralized protocols unless a decentralized verification system is built into decentralized commerce.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "smart-contracts",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "existing decentralized protocols",
        "even as smart contracts grow more sophisticated"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While more sophisticated smart contracts over time can fulfill some of these human business requirements, the needed flexibility in existing decentralized protocols will unlikely ever be attained unless a decentralized verification system is built into decentralized commerce.",
      "text_sha256": "f54c605e0a7c1ce0187151b99d99e5e651fdf6251cbc7905bedaac0922efe61d",
      "source_sha256": "82f0aea026b3e3a526ec51bc073b3b864dc06cd9083ff9c54c550037045edaa9",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411897-035",
      "text": "Until blockchain technology arrived with Bitcoin in 2009, decentralized reputation systems rested on the roughly twenty five year old and corruptible concept of the Web of Trust.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "pre 2009 decentralized reputation systems"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-035:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Until blockchain technology was introduced via Bitcoin in 2009, decentralized reputation systems mostly relied on the roughly 25 year old corruptible concept of the Web of Trust.",
      "text_sha256": "f1959e42fa8d7aae6ba257b5256684f82276d082953277d99b679eef9d49ecd2",
      "source_sha256": "82f0aea026b3e3a526ec51bc073b3b864dc06cd9083ff9c54c550037045edaa9",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411897-036",
      "text": "It is immaterial whether security incidents occur on centralized exchanges, on centralized systems appended to decentralized structures, or in the decentralized systems themselves, because the public perceives the resulting security concerns as a technology risk across all of these technologies.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "public perception of cryptocurrency and blockchain security"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "structures or the decentralized systems themselves is immaterial in this context. The security concerns are seen by the public as a technology risk across technologies.",
      "text_sha256": "9896e6480b326882e93cc2bd8df81da15c13a1bfe40353b6d8cf16c298ee16e0",
      "source_sha256": "82f0aea026b3e3a526ec51bc073b3b864dc06cd9083ff9c54c550037045edaa9",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411897-037",
      "text": "Decentralized reputation verification systems make mathematically rigid smart contracts more adjustable for the needs of business by serving as the backstop for smart contracting.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "smart-contracts"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "requires an operational decentralized reputation verification layer"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 48
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "mathematically rigid smart contracts to become more adjustable for the needs of business. Reputation verification becomes the backstop for smart contracting.",
      "text_sha256": "6d7311ef9620786e99d8ecd24175996414de56b81cde0b68e34d97b6d6024ba1",
      "source_sha256": "82f0aea026b3e3a526ec51bc073b3b864dc06cd9083ff9c54c550037045edaa9",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411897-039",
      "text": "Without a core common ethical denominator, decentralized systems cannot last: they lose coherence, become attackable, and can be corrupted, leading to suboptimal societal outcomes.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to decentralized systems as to all attempts to organize society"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Without a core common ethical denominator, decentralized systems cannot last, they lose coherence, become attackable, and can be corrupted, leading to suboptimal societal outcomes.",
      "text_sha256": "84cc3b3f9cd505739cfc43cb3ba554b11b90f4e8877eb5809055e92db43bfed7",
      "source_sha256": "82f0aea026b3e3a526ec51bc073b3b864dc06cd9083ff9c54c550037045edaa9",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-040",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3411897-040",
      "text": "For any static set of rules in an infinitely repeated game using reputation stakes, there is a way to subvert the rules for an individual's profit at the expense of the group, which is why static decentralized governance rules can always be gamed and only dynamic, changing rules can address the problem.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "economics",
        "governance-design",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "infinitely repeated games with reputation or stake based rules",
        "static rule sets"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 54
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3411897-040:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "For any static set of rules in an infinitely repeated game using reputation (stakes), there is a way to subvert the rules for an individual's profit at the expense of the group.",
      "text_sha256": "f0f0c9d5e134cce7a2b7633c7ef64114b0ec7f60805e757bd1cdcea1a4f197f3",
      "source_sha256": "82f0aea026b3e3a526ec51bc073b3b864dc06cd9083ff9c54c550037045edaa9",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3441904-005",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3441904-005",
      "text": "Forking a chain is an insufficient governance mechanism, and even attempts to create socially optimal chain forking rules cannot suffice as a substitute for evolutionary blockchain governance protocols.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "blockchain",
        "governance-design",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "existing blockchain governance that relies on forks"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3441904-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Existing blockchain governance still mainly consist of forking a given chain. Even attempts to create socially optimal chain forking rules cannot suffice.",
      "text_sha256": "4209ceb2be4ca2a0aed17e0d89acc7bc3b16874ba6cf4612846cd2a5fe49be6e",
      "source_sha256": "e6b562527f7f19accaa35491db0a0db168b6a936755e1dca424e9f30bee7a815",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3441904-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3441904-010",
      "text": "Dynamic power organization in a DAO succeeds only if the decentralized governance structure motivates token holders to collaborate productively by fairly rewarding development, work, and the policing of any diminishments.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "DAO designs that distribute autonomous power to members"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 54
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3441904-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The successful implementation of such dynamic power organization requires a decentralized governance structure that motivates DAO token holders to collaborate productively, by fairly rewarding development, work, and the policing of any diminishments.",
      "text_sha256": "44fee61c231c23d93ca58ab25a177c41075d2c711e1d75942deea537f7352cd4",
      "source_sha256": "e6b562527f7f19accaa35491db0a0db168b6a936755e1dca424e9f30bee7a815",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3441904-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3441904-018",
      "text": "Participants must be incentivized to improve their own utility while simultaneously benefiting the institution over the long run; without that duality of incentivization, rational and opportunistic internal and external constituents will attempt to game the governance design.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design",
        "regulatory-failure",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "all blockchain governance structures, especially on chain governance"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3441904-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Without that duality of incentivization, rational and opportunistic internal and external constituents will attempt to game the governance design.",
      "text_sha256": "76174b619aebe54285efe40b7ea8b11c891563940a444f1f9c26d449eba8262f",
      "source_sha256": "e6b562527f7f19accaa35491db0a0db168b6a936755e1dca424e9f30bee7a815",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3441904-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3441904-036",
      "text": "Ex post code based majoritarian rules generated by DAOs are superior to ex ante majoritarian default rules because they rest on more accurate real time information from the edge and decentralized feedback effects, and are not subject to the same information asymmetries.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "DAOs with dynamic governance mechanisms allowing token holder votes on code"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3441904-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Ex-post code-based majoritarian rules are superior to ex-ante majoritarian rules because they are based on more accurate real-time information from the edge and decentralized feedback effects.",
      "text_sha256": "47f87fc930659841abdbdde2ddeaa8579dea4703ea7cccba8e2a9c9667528c43",
      "source_sha256": "e6b562527f7f19accaa35491db0a0db168b6a936755e1dca424e9f30bee7a815",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3441904-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3441904-037",
      "text": "A decentralized on chain precedent system makes reputation based DAO governance dynamic: a post or template that is increasingly referenced gains non fungible reputation weight and associated fungible salaries, while unused precedent dissipates over time.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "reputation",
        "governance-design",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "DAO designs with a weighted directed acyclic graph and public on chain posts"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 56
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3441904-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As a post/template on the blockchain gets increasingly referenced by the DAO members and other users, it increases in non-fungible reputation weight and associated fungible salaries.",
      "text_sha256": "32104f954e276be2c4152196cd9259574a9bf2ca34f19d068b8914973baaf15c",
      "source_sha256": "e6b562527f7f19accaa35491db0a0db168b6a936755e1dca424e9f30bee7a815",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3441904-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3441904-038",
      "text": "Optimized DAO governance should pay members only indirectly, through fungible salary tokens issued in proportion to non fungible merit tokens, because the indirect economic effects remove corruptive elements and make the design more attack resistant and stable in the long run.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
