    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3606663-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Creating consensus requires increase costs of prepping, processing, and storing information.333 On the other hand, fewer computational checks for consensus increase the risk of collusion attacks that could change the record.",
      "text_sha256": "9081ec8d1636427649812a34224c055523f5d62111959c54173fc8125765ae28",
      "source_sha256": "d1d4a15a293b715bb6a5a32e689f59c3a1587915039ba9a1cf4eeb8ee2a1e57c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3606663-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3606663-038",
      "text": "Conducting monetary policy through a central bank digital currency imposes a requirement on the technology layer: the underlying network protocol must enable the central bank to adjust the money supply at will and to act as lender of last resort with access to unlimited supply.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "systemic-risk"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "CBDC built on a blockchain style protocol",
        "central bank intends to conduct monetary policy through the CBDC"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3606663-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Moreover, in order to be able to conduct monetary policy with CBDC, the underlying network protocol would have to enable the central bank to adjust the money supply at will.",
      "text_sha256": "35fce2d67417a615fb5f2f41f0645dfd7828220439acc725916feff60b3714bc",
      "source_sha256": "d1d4a15a293b715bb6a5a32e689f59c3a1587915039ba9a1cf4eeb8ee2a1e57c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3606663-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3606663-039",
      "text": "The Bank of Canada's year long Jasper trial revealed a tradeoff rather than a solution: Ethereum would make the wholesale payment system more resilient but was costly and raised privacy issues, while Corda addressed cost and privacy but made the system less resilient, and the Bank concluded in May 2017 that blockchain was not mature enough to run a national interbank payment system.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "systemic-risk",
        "decentralization",
        "blockchain",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Bank of Canada Jasper trial",
        "national interbank payment system use case",
        "as of May 2017"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3606663-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While Ethereum would make the wholesale payment system more resilient but would be costly and raised privacy issues, Corda was able to address the cost and privacy concerns but made the system less resilient.",
      "text_sha256": "9a44fd1309e03b130a4066b91c373b595cb1e515238fcf8621e4c6b627ef15e1",
      "source_sha256": "d1d4a15a293b715bb6a5a32e689f59c3a1587915039ba9a1cf4eeb8ee2a1e57c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3606663-040",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3606663-040",
      "text": "Although the public realm of coins could not exist without prior private experimentation, it is possible that the public realm will impact or even pre empt private coin development, for example if central banks attempt to censor the use of digital currencies they did not issue.",
      "claim_type": "predictive",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "systemic-risk",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "coexistence of central bank digital currencies and privately issued coins"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "speculative",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3606663-040:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "it is possible that the public realm of the coin evolution could attempt to impact or even pre- empt the private coin development and use. For example, some central banks may attempt to censor the use of non-centrally-issued digital currencies.",
      "text_sha256": "eaa37042877e9c4abd3c63b393dba1fe7db476f2deffcb07a3456e874e5202d3",
      "source_sha256": "d1d4a15a293b715bb6a5a32e689f59c3a1587915039ba9a1cf4eeb8ee2a1e57c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
