    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Crucially, non-performance reputational penalties are entirely free from racial or cultural biases and associated implications as the token holders are unlikely to even know each other.",
      "text_sha256": "35643604b1af0e915361b739640c831ae11f2a1224313eea3f3b40613df6c4d9",
      "source_sha256": "530b3a40c244aeca2eb4c53f4c9b4d6b2962bd6be9f92b4ebe17139c17f4c0e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3652481-008",
      "text": "Absent continual effort to maintain decentralized order, the very values that initially unite DAO members tend to produce ever tighter and more complex hierarchical structures inside the DAO, ending in a fully centralized tree structure.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "institutional-design",
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "no ongoing effort is made to preserve decentralized order"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Without continual efforts to maintain decentralized order, values that initially unite DAO members have a tendency to result in ever tighter and complex hierarchical structures in the DAO.",
      "text_sha256": "c0b440f510d45f3add7adaa32d894d78675271531208b56ddca9bc2b84854715",
      "source_sha256": "530b3a40c244aeca2eb4c53f4c9b4d6b2962bd6be9f92b4ebe17139c17f4c0e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3652481-009",
      "text": "The immutability of blockchain ledgers is itself a vulnerability, because once a DAO is in operation its essential construction is very difficult to alter should a bug in the code appear.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "smart-contracts",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "a bug exists in deployed DAO code"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The immutable nature of blockchain ledgers could also make the DAO vulnerable to attacks because it is so difficult to alter the essential construction of the DAO once the system is in operation, should a bug in the code arise.",
      "text_sha256": "247f0fa678944f082c921bf73f77ecee91b5f418ad8f620afe46c5f351d4fbf3",
      "source_sha256": "530b3a40c244aeca2eb4c53f4c9b4d6b2962bd6be9f92b4ebe17139c17f4c0e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-021",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3652481-021",
      "text": "The identity of actors in a DAO governance design typically creates corruptive elements, and merit identifiers other than individual identity remove the most corruptive influences.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-021:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Similarly, the identity of actors in a DAO governance design creates typically corruptive elements. Merit identifiers other than individual identity remove the most corruptive influences.",
      "text_sha256": "2fef46cd8eabc0769b5277a9f67d37c5bf55dca5d32d7c480205661d5bd683b0",
      "source_sha256": "530b3a40c244aeca2eb4c53f4c9b4d6b2962bd6be9f92b4ebe17139c17f4c0e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3652481-031",
      "text": "Reputation based staking removes the corruptive elements of fungible tokens because a third party is less likely to be able to take over a non fungible asset such as reputation that was organically grown and maintained through actual expertise in the DAO's subject matter.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation is non fungible and expertise based"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 64
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The corruptive elements of fungible assets/tokens are removed because third parties are less likely able to take over a non-fungible asset, such as reputation, that is organically grown and maintained through actual expertise in a given DAO subject matter.",
      "text_sha256": "5fee0f595be97933661b7d4f24cf3307719882be28238182e851a6d48ee8e36a",
      "source_sha256": "530b3a40c244aeca2eb4c53f4c9b4d6b2962bd6be9f92b4ebe17139c17f4c0e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3652481-036",
      "text": "Paying DevDAO salaries in fungible stable tokens in proportion to members' non fungible reputation scores makes the economic benefit indirect, which removes corruptive elements and makes the governance design more attack resistant and stable over the long run.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "a bifurcated token design with non fungible reputation tokens and fungible salary tokens"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 65
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The salary payments in fungible stable tokens are in proportion to DevDAO members' respective non-fungible reputation token scores. The indirect economic effects remove corruptive elements and make the governance design more attack resistant and stable in the long run.",
      "text_sha256": "8cf90d036e763066f0c5757b667e3c60da1d6c06b9e443fe031493ee438cc86b",
      "source_sha256": "530b3a40c244aeca2eb4c53f4c9b4d6b2962bd6be9f92b4ebe17139c17f4c0e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3652481-037",
      "text": "The reputation based DevDAO governance design creates a positive sum game, because members have incentives to build lasting non fungible value through a long term record of productive cooperation that improves the DevDAO itself.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation is non fungible and publicly reviewable"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "By contrast, the reputation- based DevDAO governance design creates a positive-sum game because DevDAO members have incentives to create lasting non- fungible value for the DevDAO by developing a long-term non- fungible record of productive cooperation that in effect improves the DevDAO.",
      "text_sha256": "fcd6fafe3fe1f678431a68c21d62d3d70160d3a53f3e0848957897e05b9695e4",
      "source_sha256": "530b3a40c244aeca2eb4c53f4c9b4d6b2962bd6be9f92b4ebe17139c17f4c0e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3652481-038",
      "text": "DevDAO member reputation is inflationary by design, so that non use, meaning failure to stake reputation tokens or to vote, causes value depreciation, which incentivizes action and makes liveness faults less likely.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 60
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The DevDAO member reputation is inflationary in the DevDAO design. As such, non-use, e.g. non-staking of reputation tokens or non-voting, would lead to value depreciation, which incentivizes action and thus value enhancement. Liveness faults become less likely.",
      "text_sha256": "c67784fd122a622b34ee94be18ebb8d14e0e1092a9c9fa0c452805e5c06a2b65",
      "source_sha256": "530b3a40c244aeca2eb4c53f4c9b4d6b2962bd6be9f92b4ebe17139c17f4c0e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3652481-039",
      "text": "Reputation weighted salary distribution defeats sock puppet attacks, because a member who creates ten accounts holding one reputation token each ends up in the same position as one account holding ten reputation tokens.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "salary is distributed in proportion to reputation token holdings"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 61
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This solves the sock- puppet attack because if a DevDAO member creates 10 accounts with 1 reputation token each, it is the same as 1 account with 10 reputation tokens.",
      "text_sha256": "0e473dda768300ce95faaf277ea59ec44422f7cc5a38a35c5cc9ea121e119c9f",
      "source_sha256": "530b3a40c244aeca2eb4c53f4c9b4d6b2962bd6be9f92b4ebe17139c17f4c0e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3709041-001",
      "text": "Centralized coordination of behavior for the common good risks undermining individual effort, whereas blockchain technology's autonomous and anonymous decentralized coordination of individual action can deliver common good outcomes without suppressing individualism and its welfare enhancing effects.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "institutional-design",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies where common good objectives require coordinating many individuals"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While centralized common good coordination of human behavior risks undermining individual effort, blockchain technology's autonomous and anonymous decentralized network coordination of individual human action can help overcome the threat to individualism and its welfare enhancing effects.",
      "text_sha256": "2bd7a336aad0ac69ca189411ff3fdb51bbf5c801f45e4eb84df1ec1637b85a7d",
      "source_sha256": "5216a7bca45a48e3bef11ec524936e66af737c0fd66271e9f6866dc20a4482cc",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3709041-003",
      "text": "Blockchain's formal immutable guarantees, improved data ownership, transparency, network integrity, and data privacy together generate a form of trust that helps optimize both business and society.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "disclosure"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Through its formal immutable guarantees, improved data ownership, transparency, network integrity, and data privacy, blockchain technology facilitates unprecedented trust that helps to optimize business and society.",
      "text_sha256": "5e81a27ddea409faba7a01ae2036dcf1b35fca6516fefd7e69c3f75990d056eb",
      "source_sha256": "5216a7bca45a48e3bef11ec524936e66af737c0fd66271e9f6866dc20a4482cc",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-004",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3709041-004",
      "text": "Power in a blockchain system is exercised through the consensus protocol, which places control of data with multiple networked parties and thereby creates checks and balances that prevent any single vested interest from controlling the system.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Power is exercised by way of blockchain's consensus protocol. The consensus protocol enables the control of data by multiple networked parties. It facilitates a system of checks and balances that prohibits any vested interest and control of the system.",
      "text_sha256": "17fbd6945f8e62e6535fe73ed5b4acfffe1ebd1f130e83923d2f23ddb2c20676",
      "source_sha256": "5216a7bca45a48e3bef11ec524936e66af737c0fd66271e9f6866dc20a4482cc",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-014",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3709041-014",
      "text": "Trust created by law is often limited because it is only indirectly democratically legitimized, inflexible, untimely, resistant to change, dependent on fallible human centric decision processes, and constrained to human speed.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "compliance",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to trust generated by legal guarantees and judicial enforcement"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-014:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Legally created trust is often limited as it can be arbitrary because it is only indirectly democratically legitimized, inflexible, untimely, resistant to change, with fallible human-centric decision processes, and human speed.",
      "text_sha256": "adcd8d16970001df9c5ad4b3a1aef9dcc02333a8bc9b55d11e1d6ac9b4c967ff",
      "source_sha256": "5216a7bca45a48e3bef11ec524936e66af737c0fd66271e9f6866dc20a4482cc",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3709041-018",
      "text": "Microdemocratic vote allocation improves outcome quality because a voter's proportional allocation of votes to an issue is itself evidence of that voter's higher knowledge of the issue, and voters are unlikely to give top priority to issues they know little about.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Moreover, part of the power of this microdemocratic approach derives from the higher levels of knowledge a given voter has on a particular issue that is evidenced by the voters' proportional allocation of votes on such issue.",
      "text_sha256": "5f64454d6bb39509ba57599a94d7e361922a97f19c02477c4f50003cf7a4183d",
      "source_sha256": "5216a7bca45a48e3bef11ec524936e66af737c0fd66271e9f6866dc20a4482cc",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-022",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3709041-022",
      "text": "Representative democracies in the early 2020s were slow and inflexible because of their constitutional and institutional infrastructure and their legal systems, with change typically depending on the election of a new government after around four years at the earliest.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "describes representative democracies as of the early 2020s"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-022:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In the early 2020s, representative democracies were largely slow and inflexible because of their constitutional and institutional infrastructure and their respective legal systems.",
      "text_sha256": "2d3ea1140ed791c6a7e1138efb47d0e6d3860798998d2b28d285015fcd19b46b",
      "source_sha256": "5216a7bca45a48e3bef11ec524936e66af737c0fd66271e9f6866dc20a4482cc",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3709041-024",
      "text": "Decentralized voting pools can become supplemental voting systems that help overcome the legitimacy deficit of representative democracies, but installing them as upgrades to existing representative democracies would require constitutional or democratic support that is dubious at best.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "requires constitutional or democratic authorization for adoption"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Of course, such upgrades to existing representative democracies may require constitutional or democratic support which is dubious at best.",
      "text_sha256": "0d5e6df11bc47d383d5d6a12ed87d581aad3c4800fc4679cba86f4c09ecd24e9",
      "source_sha256": "5216a7bca45a48e3bef11ec524936e66af737c0fd66271e9f6866dc20a4482cc",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3709041-028",
      "text": "Blockchain based land title records can serve as collateral for credit or as identity verification, removing a requirement that is often challenging and prohibitive for accessing both financial and non-financial services.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies where identity or title verification is a prerequisite to service access"
      ],
