    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3709041-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The transparency blockchain technology offers can help address the public's diminishing trust in traditional charities.",
      "text_sha256": "17b679ac8f8a3b1590e7515ba9d845a2412934dee47e947a0f22c0c6e7bd50ee",
      "source_sha256": "5216a7bca45a48e3bef11ec524936e66af737c0fd66271e9f6866dc20a4482cc",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782191-007",
      "text": "Decentralization is not merely delegation, deconcentration, devolution, or the redistribution of centrally organized authority or centrally collected revenue; equating it with those terms misstates what decentralization is.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Termino- logically, decentralization is not just synonymous with delegation, deconcentration, disassortative, devolution, circulation, or partnership.",
      "text_sha256": "ced922079c23958e84d1ba4a787ec966801f4ef54d50bfa186eba7362bf61ee0",
      "source_sha256": "b0bf0529c3cf69839879bc4da476714efee2717a4beb768bd5c859b810e6174e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782191-009",
      "text": "The degree of decentralization can be delineated by distinguishing logical decentralization, architectural or hardware decentralization, and political or governance decentralization, though some overlap among these concepts is unavoidable.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The degree of decentralization can be delineated by distinguishing several core con- cepts such as logical decentralization, architectural decentralization, and political de- centralization.",
      "text_sha256": "3943339e28187ae459f3d233035dcf299871f6788d5f49b6b9ee66b5750c549f",
      "source_sha256": "b0bf0529c3cf69839879bc4da476714efee2717a4beb768bd5c859b810e6174e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782191-013",
      "text": "Because information in decentralized systems is continuously outdated by a changing environment, decentralized governance must be autonomous and automated, able to evolve, mutate, and create new information precedent, in the way mitosis replaces worn out cells.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized systems whose information changes continuously"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Like mitosis, this decentralized governance process has to be autonomous and automated in the system. Decentralized governance has to be able to evolve and mutate and create new information precedent for the continuous efficient operation of the system.",
      "text_sha256": "0bfb665bb09487eb3b65e2da3dba682c039b59f1f6952f98d140f860769bd8df",
      "source_sha256": "b0bf0529c3cf69839879bc4da476714efee2717a4beb768bd5c859b810e6174e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-014",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782191-014",
      "text": "Natural selection operates as a decentralized selection mechanism: no centralized authority determines which organisms survive, and the population with the most adaptable and heritable traits gains a natural comparative advantage without any centralized mechanism.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "biological evolution as an analogy for decentralized systems"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 17
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-014:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The natural selection of the most adaptable and survivable population char- acteristics materializes without a centralized mechanism.",
      "text_sha256": "617cc38d5001baa62e26325f6178ff35294d7e0ad77d59bf988785ac5f0108d5",
      "source_sha256": "b0bf0529c3cf69839879bc4da476714efee2717a4beb768bd5c859b810e6174e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782191-015",
      "text": "Technology-driven decentralized systems depend on existing infrastructure and follow existing natural network patterns, just as predator populations could not evolve without prey.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "technology-driven decentralized systems"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 17
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Technology-driven decentralized systems depend on an ex- isting infrastructure.",
      "text_sha256": "c09c61ea64465632b86335103b9294b4f1f1333ced8d524760456b29ba822cc7",
      "source_sha256": "b0bf0529c3cf69839879bc4da476714efee2717a4beb768bd5c859b810e6174e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782191-016",
      "text": "Decentralized systems depend on network effects, which occur when increasing numbers of participants in a network improve the value of network access for the entirety of users; however, a network's infrastructure can compromise its network effects and the associated user benefits.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "networked decentralized systems"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 17
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Decentralized systems depend on network effects. Network effects occur when in- creasing numbers of participants or users in a given network improve the value of network access for the entirety of the users.",
      "text_sha256": "e24a81cfc4946b85c6d364ddde54686b9d41d3e7f7a0a6ffadcc90090901e86c",
      "source_sha256": "b0bf0529c3cf69839879bc4da476714efee2717a4beb768bd5c859b810e6174e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782191-019",
      "text": "Information in decentralized systems originates at the edges and is optimized through feedback: peers who receive information transmit its changed relevance back to the original generator, who evaluates and amends it, constantly updating and optimizing information quality.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "peer-to-peer decentralized networks"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This feedback constantly updates and optimizes the quality of infor- mation.",
      "text_sha256": "203a2606f98437b27eb1ddab870a5ebe868e2f75f8192d131baa65397612754e",
      "source_sha256": "b0bf0529c3cf69839879bc4da476714efee2717a4beb768bd5c859b810e6174e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-021",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782191-021",
      "text": "Independent and autonomous subgroups, formed randomly based on members' ability to contribute to a common cause and characterized by equality and mutual trust, form the backbone of decentralized structures.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized collaborative structures"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-021:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Independent and autonomous subgroups create the backbone of decentralized structures. Subgroups are formed randomly based on individual members' ability to contribute to the common cause of the group.",
      "text_sha256": "611237054d2ae1e9fa4b96481805b8ad2c37610535d35f7e1c8bf5770e0205e0",
      "source_sha256": "b0bf0529c3cf69839879bc4da476714efee2717a4beb768bd5c859b810e6174e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-022",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782191-022",
      "text": "Centralized coordination enables attack coordination because the hierarchical structure allows attackers to identify a single point of failure, whereas the constantly morphing information flow of decentralized systems increases their attack resistance.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "comparison of centralized and decentralized system security"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-022:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Centralized coordination enables attack coordination because the hierarchical struc- ture allows the identification of a single point of failure.",
      "text_sha256": "e2527a9b136cc9f93f279de798e61397bae5c1aa7a95c8b489267029e28801f9",
      "source_sha256": "b0bf0529c3cf69839879bc4da476714efee2717a4beb768bd5c859b810e6174e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782191-029",
      "text": "There is no clear-cut discrete difference between centralized and decentralized; organizations fall along a spectrum whose essential differentiator is the freedom of each member in the network.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782191-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "There is no clear-cut, discrete difference between centralized and decentralized. There is a spectrum between the two that any organization will fall along. The essen- tial differentiator is the freedom of each member in the network.",
      "text_sha256": "6134ef8de3dc7c72fbdca1ad1b3d6000a54cff2667ba92693befd5b8467ab4dc",
      "source_sha256": "b0bf0529c3cf69839879bc4da476714efee2717a4beb768bd5c859b810e6174e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782192-001",
      "text": "Human group coordination progresses through three stages: chaos, then decentralized organization, then centralized hierarchy. Decentralized organization is not a deviation but the natural intermediate stage between no organization and a completed hierarchy.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "human group coordination and institutional development generally"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Human group coordination naturally progresses from the first stage, chaos (barbari- ans ravaging the landscape, \"Raahr!\"), to decentralized organization (\"Let's all agree to band together to defend ourselves from the barbarians\"), to centralized organiza- tion (\"Long live the king\").",
      "text_sha256": "af609ec52768df07a70e5c36f863aad5c2fdaa55f742edc0393af6f39bfa7ece",
      "source_sha256": "e7eafd56cb8a8bd15b64cf58216bb655f939bdcc296387e362fd9191976d67ae",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782192-002",
      "text": "At the decentralized stage the individual nodes remain autonomous and the network assigns no fixed roles; coordination comes from alignment on a shared transcendental goal rather than from formal position, so that, as the authors put it, the values are the organization.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized stage of organization, before a hierarchy has formed"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The individual nodes remain autonomous; the network does not have fixed roles for each member. But they are all responding to a higher calling as they unite in purpose.",
      "text_sha256": "b4b3e8e8866126843bcbdff77f0b9d75776c675e580586d0f6a5c1b04a167d77",
      "source_sha256": "e7eafd56cb8a8bd15b64cf58216bb655f939bdcc296387e362fd9191976d67ae",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782192-015",
      "text": "As members constantly probe the edge of acceptable behavior, policing the rules becomes more expensive, the rules become divorced from the shared goals, and relationships become brittle and formal instead of warm and loose.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "compliance",
        "reputation",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "organizations relying on formal rule enforcement"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As members constantly probe the edge of acceptable behavior, policing the rules becomes more expensive. The rules become divorced from the shared goals. Relationships become brittle and formal instead of warm and loose.",
      "text_sha256": "8499b4f956f56c66ef2ee1fae22f3a116d81203ffd895ef82ffc705cd4971184",
      "source_sha256": "e7eafd56cb8a8bd15b64cf58216bb655f939bdcc296387e362fd9191976d67ae",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782192-018",
      "text": "Long-term organizational stability requires a dynamic governance system that can adapt the rules to changing circumstances, a requirement that holds for any organization but especially for decentralized ones.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "organizations seeking long-term stability",
        "especially decentralized organizations"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The fact that any set of rules can be corrupted illustrates two necessities for the long-term stability of any organization, but especially for decentralized organiza- tions. First, a dynamic governance system must be designed that can adapt the rules to the circumstances.",
      "text_sha256": "9878ca2e0a863f740b624f30a3fccf58a44d7f744fc5e0ec858f23983f6e2630",
      "source_sha256": "e7eafd56cb8a8bd15b64cf58216bb655f939bdcc296387e362fd9191976d67ae",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782192-024",
      "text": "Decentralization, though it may look wastefully redundant, gives every member greater autonomous power, whereas centralization limits members' powers and reduces them to cogs in the machine.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Decentralization, while it may be seen as wastefully redundant, gives every member greater autonomous power. Centralization limits its members' powers, reducing them to mere cogs in the machine.",
      "text_sha256": "99b105fceb4cde7ba5d71f62457037fd686ee769654a757e268d54a2b4cbf255",
      "source_sha256": "e7eafd56cb8a8bd15b64cf58216bb655f939bdcc296387e362fd9191976d67ae",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-030",
