    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The Ma- ghribis built a sophisticated decentralized trade network using WWth century infor- mation technology, and reputation. Wcth century farmers used dynamic governance designs to create the most powerful decentralized organization in history.",
      "text_sha256": "b25bda8c005e643c7cea9311bb71f8fa675fb73f55568e5262cb79fad7e621b9",
      "source_sha256": "e7eafd56cb8a8bd15b64cf58216bb655f939bdcc296387e362fd9191976d67ae",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782192-031",
      "text": "Western democracies still run on structures developed decades or centuries ago and have no formal interaction with the new data stream produced by modern information technology.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "contemporary Western democracies"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Western democracies are still using the structures developed decades or centuries ago, and lack any formal interaction with this new data stream.",
      "text_sha256": "a014391b82efbb7c31924a8b1d1f305375ea332d3ef82addadaf96bbe23ddec4",
      "source_sha256": "e7eafd56cb8a8bd15b64cf58216bb655f939bdcc296387e362fd9191976d67ae",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782192-037",
      "text": "The autonomous element of a DAO comes from its governance system being programmed through smart contracts, which makes a DAO ultimately democratic rather than relying on a benevolent dictator to correct course during black swan events.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "smart-contracts",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized autonomous organizations governed by smart contracts"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The autonomous aspect of a DAO stems from its programmed governance system through smart contracts. A DAO is ultimately democratic, instead of having a benev- olent dictator behind the scenes to efficiently correct course during black swan events.",
      "text_sha256": "ace5a4e533b728904bab4260cd92ebf5891f1ca721cd70ac2d133083555abb4c",
      "source_sha256": "e7eafd56cb8a8bd15b64cf58216bb655f939bdcc296387e362fd9191976d67ae",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782192-038",
      "text": "Decentralized money and decentralized contracts have been built, but decentralized business will not work until roughly eight further decentralized institutions that people actually use in business are built.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "institutional-design",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized commerce built on blockchain infrastructure"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Two important tools have been built, decentralized money (Bitcoin) and decentral- ized contracts (Ethereum). But it won't work until eight more decentralized institu- tions are built that people use to do business.",
      "text_sha256": "194993896959c32f098c86b76a34256159fe02cddcaeb2af41f1ea15fc9d9403",
      "source_sha256": "e7eafd56cb8a8bd15b64cf58216bb655f939bdcc296387e362fd9191976d67ae",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782192-039",
      "text": "Money and contracts are worthless in business with counterparties who cannot be trusted to keep a bargain, so decentralized commerce requires a system in which reputation means something.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "decentralization",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized business among parties without prior trust"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782192-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Money and contracts are worthless in business with barbarians who can't be trusted to keep a bargain. To do business, we need a system where reputation means something.",
      "text_sha256": "9b483b698724ee53c568ffcb2e73e935e801ce08ea5179a6220ae6993ff89bfb",
      "source_sha256": "e7eafd56cb8a8bd15b64cf58216bb655f939bdcc296387e362fd9191976d67ae",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782193-007",
      "text": "The unstoppable power of decentralization is threatened by unregulated competition for profits, but it can be maintained even in extreme circumstances by a secure and meaningful reputational system.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "reputation",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized organizations exposed to profit competition",
        "requires the reputation system to be secure and meaningful"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The \"unstoppable power of decentralization\" is threatened by unregulated competition for profits, but can be maintained in the most extreme circumstances by a secure and meaningful reputa- tional system.",
      "text_sha256": "02a270bb2cf71478c09e665e7cf35fafd22a05bb4a3bae48c15da24a77a1caee",
      "source_sha256": "74df9cc9a19a098bdacd0424a4174795f6e184f7a31c8ee7541195186701ebd2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782193-008",
      "text": "Modern Western democracies, which the authors treat as the largest DAOs ever assembled, show that a network whose members hold diverse values can be united by protocol centralization, and that the destabilizing effect of that protocol centralization can be ameliorated by power decentralization through dynamic governance design.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "networks uniting members with diverse values",
        "requires dynamic design of governance"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Analyzing modern Western democracies, the largest DAOs ever as- sembled, shows networks of members with diverse values can be united with proto- col centralization, and its destabilizing effect can be ameliorated by power- decentralization through dynamic design of governance.",
      "text_sha256": "f8460465f6a2aa539f23015c6d5338761547eeec607778847371f9bacfdd8ad1",
      "source_sha256": "74df9cc9a19a098bdacd0424a4174795f6e184f7a31c8ee7541195186701ebd2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782193-018",
      "text": "The centralized hierarchy built by the Chinese Communist Revolution was extremely successful at the military goal it was designed for, but once the military threat was gone it failed completely at solving other important problems, producing catastrophic reforms such as the Cultural Revolution and the Great Leap Forward.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "institutional-design",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "China from 1949 until Mao Zedong's death in 1976"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This centralized hierarchy was extremely successful at the military goal it was designed for, but completely failed at solving other important problems once the military threat was gone.",
      "text_sha256": "99212504f414257989842d54bceef8cb519b8ca0df6648cf4730866ec952acad",
      "source_sha256": "74df9cc9a19a098bdacd0424a4174795f6e184f7a31c8ee7541195186701ebd2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782193-019",
      "text": "The lesson the authors draw from Imperial China and Pharaonic Egypt is that decentralization of power and individual autonomy give long-term stability when the society also has unifying ideals it can believe in.",
      "claim_type": "normative",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "requires unifying ideals the society believes in"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The lesson of Im- perial China, and Pharaonic Egypt before it, is that decentralization of power, individ- ual autonomy, gives long-term stability when there are unifying ideals that the society can believe in.",
      "text_sha256": "0939ddec7b7ef19ff2be7e8b357ad53dc1ce262fd4d6ab1b46bf5fbecf6a4350",
      "source_sha256": "74df9cc9a19a098bdacd0424a4174795f6e184f7a31c8ee7541195186701ebd2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782193-030",
      "text": "The strong trust that sustained Maghribi trade, in which embezzlement was rare despite extreme information asymmetry, cannot be explained by a strong centralized government, since the Maghribis could not form a centralized legal or political hierarchy and the official legal channels were slow and unreliable.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance",
        "disclosure",
        "reputation",
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Maghribi Jewish traders around 1000 AD under the Fatimid caliphate"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 63
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In point of fact, the records show that such embezzlement was rare. Instead, a strong sense of trust pervaded. So what mechanism protected the principals from their agents' asymmetric information? The answer was not a strong centralized gov- ernment.",
      "text_sha256": "6081ab1bcb7a2692d2e73da08266e18421cac27f37c52d600425c095fef38762",
      "source_sha256": "74df9cc9a19a098bdacd0424a4174795f6e184f7a31c8ee7541195186701ebd2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782193-031",
      "text": "Honesty would be the wrong strategy for an agent if the contract were anonymous and its resolution did not affect future contracts, because that situation is a single-stage zero-sum game in which stealing all the entrusted wealth is optimal.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "economics",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "anonymous contracting",
        "no effect of the outcome on future business"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 63
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Honesty would be a bad strategy for the agent if the contract was anonymous and the resolution didn't affect future contracts.",
      "text_sha256": "42d04149ac40305572c2d0a17ad8b3e01966f793399848ab2e30ceebc45dc797",
      "source_sha256": "74df9cc9a19a098bdacd0424a4174795f6e184f7a31c8ee7541195186701ebd2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782193-032",
      "text": "Adding reputation to the contracting game converts it from a single-stage zero-sum game into a repeated positive-sum game in which the rest of the community becomes relevant, because reputation is a future-oriented commodity that pays off with the promise of future contracts.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "economics",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "networks where reputation is observable and policed by the community"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "By adding reputation to the game, it becomes a repeated game, and the rest of the community becomes relevant. Reputation is a future-oriented commodity, which pays off profits with the promise of future contracts. Now the game is a repeated game which is positive-sum.",
      "text_sha256": "9e2915642049de3dbb1b567b19af9538fccafbc68d744ce645729207006eb795",
      "source_sha256": "74df9cc9a19a098bdacd0424a4174795f6e184f7a31c8ee7541195186701ebd2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782193-033",
      "text": "Reputation permits business with any member of a network regardless of personal acquaintance, but only if the network is closed and its size is limited by the ability to police reputation with the available information technology.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation-based networks",
        "network must be closed",
        "size bounded by available information technology"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "First, reputation allows business dealings with any member of the network, regard- less of personal acquaintance. This requires the network to be closed, however, with a size limited by the ability to police reputation using the information technology available.",
      "text_sha256": "c7b661e468f520cb30a945629817eb4c4f59da898dbbb4dfb0bd8d56b287e895",
      "source_sha256": "74df9cc9a19a098bdacd0424a4174795f6e184f7a31c8ee7541195186701ebd2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782193-034",
      "text": "Focusing rewards on reputation rather than on immediately fungible cash encourages decentralized organization because it disperses power fairly: anyone with equivalent talent is equally acceptable, those already employed are unavailable, and the exponential rich-get-richer concentration of power is diminished.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "networks that reward members with reputation rather than immediate cash"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Finally, a focus on reputation instead of immediately fungible cash rewards encour- ages decentralized organization because it disperses power, and it does so fairly.",
      "text_sha256": "24aaaa3279e5ba9ca7e93c49b6ef53365d8d106147407a92504f85a93e0af794",
      "source_sha256": "74df9cc9a19a098bdacd0424a4174795f6e184f7a31c8ee7541195186701ebd2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782193-039",
      "text": "The authors stipulate that functioning democracies are decentralized autonomous organizations: the United States government is a DAO, as are Norway, Mauritius, Uruguay, and South Korea, and every functioning democracy is more akin to a DAO than to a centralized corporation.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "functioning democracies"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The United States government is a decentralized organization, a DAO. Norway is a DAO\u2014the best DAO according to the democracy index.38 Mauritius, Uruguay, and South Korea are also DAOs. Every functioning democracy is more akin to a DAO than to a centralized corporation.",
      "text_sha256": "c04c88d8348237d1802ad446709978deb8866bdfba99379b368baf7856388a29",
      "source_sha256": "74df9cc9a19a098bdacd0424a4174795f6e184f7a31c8ee7541195186701ebd2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-004",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782198-004",
      "text": "Rating systems on centralized marketplaces are actively gamed: new Amazon sellers are solicited by sock puppet operators offering to inflate their ratings and attack competitors.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "regulatory-failure",
        "economics",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "observed on major centralized e-commerce platforms"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "For example, one of the first things that will hap- pen if you open a shop on Amazon is that you will receive several messages from ma- licious sock-puppet wranglers offering to game the rating system to improve your company's ratings while attacking your major competitor.",
      "text_sha256": "8d838eb89a53186b67f2f103338df3e8b37fca5e15df4f435858497ed9b82713",
      "source_sha256": "e7e1378e3eed06cace6534e7792a7307d607d18bc6beb4ac45896476280728e4",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-005",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782198-005",
      "text": "Social networks grow exponentially more powerful through the network effect, but they are stifled by the centralized ownership and governance of the Web 2.0 companies that run them; governing decentralized information flow requires decentralized incentive designs.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "decentralization",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to networks whose value comes from member interaction"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "But these networks are stifled by the centralized ownership and governance of the Web ).5 companies that run them. Governing decentralized information flow ne- cessitates decentralized incentive designs.",
      "text_sha256": "f5f6b223cb5f103b6fae878c2921b0c8c2c5a62d0cf1f3e99d3498909f889873",
      "source_sha256": "e7e1378e3eed06cace6534e7792a7307d607d18bc6beb4ac45896476280728e4",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782198-007",
      "text": "If a peer to peer network were decentrally owned by its users, its algorithms could be open source and still remain safe, because the network could reward members for policing exploitation instead of relying on a centralized company to keep the algorithm opaque.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "open-source-and-code",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "requires an incentive design that rewards members for defending the algorithm they own"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "if the P)P network were decentrally owned by the users them- selves, the algorithms can be open source and still remain safe.",
      "text_sha256": "30283ee0e49ca6a2b16909a05a36b83e63a0fe1749c0615ab14e9a4febfd13f9",
      "source_sha256": "e7e1378e3eed06cace6534e7792a7307d607d18bc6beb4ac45896476280728e4",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-014",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782198-014",
      "text": "A truly decentralized organization requires that its rules be transparently available to all members; otherwise the keepers of the knowledge acquire higher status and a hierarchy forms.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "decentralization",
        "institutional-design",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to organizations that claim to be decentralized"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-014:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In order to have a truly decentralized organization, the rules must be transpar- ently available to all members. Otherwise the keepers of the knowledge have a higher status, creating a hierarchy.",
      "text_sha256": "e9d21cc4d87b9004a7cddff29778832e4a58e6c3751f00a455206933b689ffca",
      "source_sha256": "e7e1378e3eed06cace6534e7792a7307d607d18bc6beb4ac45896476280728e4",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-020",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782198-020",
      "text": "The goal of the Web3 movement is to foster radical bureaucratic transparency through open source design, to advance individual autonomy and privacy through cryptography, and to level access to information and computing resources through decentralized networks.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "citation-and-knowledge"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-020:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The goal of the WebG movement is to foster radical bureaucratic transparency using open source design, to further individual au- tonomy and privacy using cryptography, and to level the access to information and computing resources with decentralized networks.",
      "text_sha256": "996ecf7e9a3bf068de822405454264849ded38c09acf8372de1ea33b970f8645",
      "source_sha256": "e7e1378e3eed06cace6534e7792a7307d607d18bc6beb4ac45896476280728e4",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782198-024",
      "text": "Bitcoin proved that a decentralized peer to peer network can manage valuable assets without a central authority, but the centralizing force of competition concentrated power anyway, as economies of scale produced large mining farms in place of millions of individual members maintaining the ledger.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "decentralization",
        "economics",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to proof of work networks where mining rewards create economies of scale"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "But the centralizing forces of competition led to concentration of power in the Bitcoin network, as econo- mies of scale led to large computer farms devoted to mining for bitcoins, instead of millions of individual network members maintaining the ledger on their laptops.",
      "text_sha256": "adb6ef796f801074746548347b648718dc54a2725badcba49f3e44fe07723f2c",
      "source_sha256": "e7e1378e3eed06cace6534e7792a7307d607d18bc6beb4ac45896476280728e4",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-025",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782198-025",
      "text": "Bitcoin and Ethereum have no formal binding governance framework declaring how consensus protocols may be changed in the future, which the authors identify as a deep flaw that weakens the networks and will lead to instability.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "governance-design",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to major blockchains lacking on chain governance"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In Bitcoin and Ethereum, there is no formal binding governance framework de- claring how the protocols for consensus might be changed in the future. This is a deep flaw which weakens these networks and will lead to instability.",
      "text_sha256": "67a7b7c29e7c163d80068060fc6c7cc0b05856503783e62af0e145bb88ba845d",
      "source_sha256": "e7e1378e3eed06cace6534e7792a7307d607d18bc6beb4ac45896476280728e4",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782198-028",
      "text": "Hash functions let a leaderless network reach consensus on identity and ordering, because every node independently hashes a transaction's data and deterministically arrives at the same unique identifier that everyone recognizes.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "tokenomics",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "requires all nodes to run the same deterministic hash protocol"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Thanks to the hash function, every node in the network hashes the transaction's data and independently arrives at the same an- swer, giving the transaction a unique ID that everyone recognizes.",
      "text_sha256": "5b300edde4894b7504eb8c64d0bb341a388aeb0a84fa8018c36c55b944be7a99",
      "source_sha256": "e7e1378e3eed06cace6534e7792a7307d607d18bc6beb4ac45896476280728e4",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782198-035",
      "text": "Anonymity can exacerbate second and third order discrimination because it makes such discrimination more difficult to detect, so other governance mechanisms in a decentralized organization must be used to combat it.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies where members infer protected characteristics from behavior, and to systemic discrimination"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-035:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In fact, anonymity can exacerbate )nd and Grd-order effects, as it makes it more difficult to detect. To combat such effects, different mechanisms in the governance of a decentralized organization must be employed.",
      "text_sha256": "641b8a8fad87c53270cfe8ce939fa82b414e6afa6fd030e422f6f80a332b9ccb",
      "source_sha256": "e7e1378e3eed06cace6534e7792a7307d607d18bc6beb4ac45896476280728e4",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782198-037",
      "text": "Anonymity should be balanced rather than absolute: a member's power to broadcast should be tied to a pseudonymous account carrying meaningful and valuable reputation that is lost when the broadcasting power is abused.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to decentralized networks that permit anonymous participation"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782198-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Therefore, anonymity should be balanced. Your power to broadcast your voice should be tempered by hav- ing that voice tied with a pseudonymous36 account with meaningful and valuable rep- utation. If you abuse your broadcasting power, then you should lose your reputation.",
      "text_sha256": "5c76f2e35cb3c48852f5961f5ca81fb59ca1cf11d63e5e638aaaedb5cc58e3b0",
      "source_sha256": "e7e1378e3eed06cace6534e7792a7307d607d18bc6beb4ac45896476280728e4",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782201-002",
      "text": "Effective decentralized DAO governance necessitates reputation verification systems.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "reputation",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "We believe that effective decentralized DAO governance necessitates reputation verification systems.",
      "text_sha256": "f3bdf5bba45a0b6e57d007b6cd94915cba7e978358a66eea65b31e7e7a7f07df",
      "source_sha256": "bedf7bcfbb7a9b0112b5848cb0d941b1d41f330dafeee0143a30ff5e8aa53700",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782201-003",
      "text": "A DAO that is internally well governed by a reputation verification engine lets other entities clone its governance for their own purposes and run with the same governance metrics, so mastery of internal decentralization becomes transplantable infrastructure governance.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "open-source-and-code"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to IoT infrastructure entities seeking governance and interoperability"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "DAOs that are internally well-governed by a reputation verification engine allow other IoT infrastructure entities to simply clone the DAO governance for their own purposes and run a DAO with the same gov- ernance metrics.",
      "text_sha256": "96a5f486c20e91a06e44fa93b1c9da6ef0575c27ebbffe4a2c4dd1b4f33b27e9",
      "source_sha256": "bedf7bcfbb7a9b0112b5848cb0d941b1d41f330dafeee0143a30ff5e8aa53700",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-004",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782201-004",
      "text": "Self policing is more effective when the members themselves hold the power, because a centralized hierarchy in which each member holds distinct powers and responsibilities is more prone to structural corruption.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where members hold the best domain knowledge about their own processes"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 44
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The power of decentralization is individual autonomy. Self-policing their own members is more effective when the members have the power, unlike a centralized hierarchy which is more prone to structural corruption when each member holds distinct powers and responsibilities.",
      "text_sha256": "546cb40128fb61b71b3ca91075d7b327203db4c6518b93c8b905d62d847dd918",
      "source_sha256": "bedf7bcfbb7a9b0112b5848cb0d941b1d41f330dafeee0143a30ff5e8aa53700",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782201-007",
      "text": "Code based trust in decentralized applications lowers transaction costs and simultaneously raises consumer and market confidence and certainty, which facilitates economies of scale that are only occasionally and temporarily possible in centralized structures.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "economics",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "holds despite the cybersecurity issues associated with cryptocurrencies"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "code-based trust can help lower trans- action costs, but it also increases consumer and overall market confidence and cer- tainty, which facilitate economies of scale that are only occasionally and temporarily possible in centralized structures.",
      "text_sha256": "57a9aa2e215a2a3d7c069ed79d53c23dbd93ddc44900d661aa7881e2e4054820",
      "source_sha256": "bedf7bcfbb7a9b0112b5848cb0d941b1d41f330dafeee0143a30ff5e8aa53700",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782201-009",
      "text": "Keeping a decentralized organization aligned in pursuit of its goals requires providing something more valuable than money, namely reputation, following the Maghribi traders' example.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "politically decentralized networks devoted to profit"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In order to keep a decentralized organization aligned in the pursuit of their goals, you must provide something more valuable than money: reputation.",
      "text_sha256": "2d9fedf4c73d082f99d56100476f5c13e314f60c95d10ed74c50746d37ea87be",
      "source_sha256": "bedf7bcfbb7a9b0112b5848cb0d941b1d41f330dafeee0143a30ff5e8aa53700",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782201-010",
      "text": "Centralized authorities have a long record of using crises to justify the introduction of monitoring tools that outlast their original purpose.",
