      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "New DAO proposals appear almost quarterly in the RWRWs. Most fail because of a lack of decentralized governance solutions.",
      "text_sha256": "06ade7ae1264a68f388f192e6876233bccb0cfa8283f42d8be107267548d5db5",
      "source_sha256": "bedf7bcfbb7a9b0112b5848cb0d941b1d41f330dafeee0143a30ff5e8aa53700",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-026",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782201-026",
      "text": "Aragon's refusal to use its own protocol to arbitrate an internal dispute is testimony to the lack of trust its own system designers place in their system's capabilities, and its reputation and legislative and judicial governance protocols remain trivial.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "systemic-risk",
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 67
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-026:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In RWRW, Aragon declined to use their own protocol to arbitrate an internal dispute, which is testimony to the lack of trust of their system designers in their own system capabilities.",
      "text_sha256": "1a1e0e5f681e1d7c5c69cf41725c391ebc47375974bc017fd1c33682f9d0c598",
      "source_sha256": "bedf7bcfbb7a9b0112b5848cb0d941b1d41f330dafeee0143a30ff5e8aa53700",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-027",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782201-027",
      "text": "Because DAO performance assessment is based on optimizing fungible token value rather than on hierarchical or political processes, the focus on token value enhancement can lead to short termism and may cause ethical and governance issues to be ignored.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "DAO designs inheriting the path dependencies of the 2016 DAO",
        "fungible token based membership"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782201-027:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Yet, the focus on the value en- hancement of fungible tokens can lead to short-termism and may ignore ethical and governance issues.",
      "text_sha256": "0ebf1fed85f499fe57bc0de2a71d4d306e898876053ed3d2c34b699f4c41239a",
      "source_sha256": "bedf7bcfbb7a9b0112b5848cb0d941b1d41f330dafeee0143a30ff5e8aa53700",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782203-001",
      "text": "Any set process or set of rules that can ever be designed will ultimately fail to secure a network for all time, so no static rule set can serve as the permanent foundation of a DAO.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized networks",
        "open global membership",
        "anonymous participation"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 41
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "A core precept for the creation of DAOs is the recognition that any set process or set of rules that can ever be designed will ultimately fail to secure a network for all time.",
      "text_sha256": "8756428b20acfd6100fb44bb2fd9aa483440a791af2cf5b85aebb75737373c43",
      "source_sha256": "ab8a22d0dbb026a09212a4c85963f3c05787cf80775e8613ae3724e3883e7a56",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782203-002",
      "text": "Building effective and efficient DAOs requires three things together: a secure and meaningful reputation system, maximum bureaucratic transparency through a dynamic governance structure, and coherent transcendental values for long-term stability.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "reputation",
        "disclosure",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "DAOs with open membership to anonymous individuals worldwide"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In this chapter we argue that building effective and efficient DAOs requires a secure and meaningful reputation system, maximum bureaucratic transparency through a dynamic govern- ance structure, and coherent transcendental values for long-term stability.",
      "text_sha256": "d252561c50cca6648d24136ed4ceb3ef0627f2c1e5994943b6f2091094e35b60",
      "source_sha256": "ab8a22d0dbb026a09212a4c85963f3c05787cf80775e8613ae3724e3883e7a56",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-004",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782203-004",
      "text": "Protocol centralization, meaning rigid and immediately enforced rules such as those executed by smart contracts, leads to instability unless it is implemented wisely.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "smart-contracts",
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "smart contract enforced protocols",
        "politically decentralized networks"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, protocol centralization leads to instability if it is not implemented wisely.",
      "text_sha256": "19cf14032577b86425327ada574d12209c9dcafe8746ca5ab473d19e020e3d7d",
      "source_sha256": "ab8a22d0dbb026a09212a4c85963f3c05787cf80775e8613ae3724e3883e7a56",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782203-010",
      "text": "Because a group sometimes genuinely has no consensus to be discovered, network forking is at times inevitable rather than a governance failure that better rules could prevent.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "blockchain",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "cyclic or irreconcilable group preferences",
        "decentralized networks whose members can exit"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "First, that is a major problem for democracy. Sometimes there is no consensus to be had. This leads to the second conclusion that sometimes network forking is inevitable.",
      "text_sha256": "ac0a81bf5c85c50703653d7b29bed0ffdb830ed94b8c61334ed29edf8bba5c22",
      "source_sha256": "ab8a22d0dbb026a09212a4c85963f3c05787cf80775e8613ae3724e3883e7a56",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782203-013",
      "text": "Across all the alternative polling methods explored in the literature, changes both help and hurt: new approaches solve old problems while creating new opportunities for manipulation, a pattern the authors identify with increasing the attack surface.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "alternative voting and polling mechanisms",
        "continuous or weighted voting technologies"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In all the methods dis- cussed the answer has always been that changes both help and hurt. New approaches solve old problems, but they create new opportunities for manipulation.",
      "text_sha256": "a8b13b2c7332e960c6f4a9adf23c4c83eaa7e58161d6ff1393ae0d814c6aa0c7",
      "source_sha256": "ab8a22d0dbb026a09212a4c85963f3c05787cf80775e8613ae3724e3883e7a56",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782203-028",
      "text": "Since no algorithm can be perfectly secure in all circumstances, protocol developers should redirect effort from proving algorithms correct to building a governance process that updates the algorithm as network circumstances change, rewarding protocol improvement with meaningful reputation instead of leaving attack as the profitable option.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "governance-design",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "proof of stake and other consensus protocols",
        "networks facing evolving adversaries"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 71
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Given the impossibility of creating an algorithm that will be perfectly secure in all circumstances, we should instead focus on developing a governance process that al- lows us to update our algorithm to adapt to the changing network circumstances to the security level required",
      "text_sha256": "ef2c8fc26ba4ebf2017074eddef96f4c733972aa44ea065237457431aba35250",
      "source_sha256": "ab8a22d0dbb026a09212a4c85963f3c05787cf80775e8613ae3724e3883e7a56",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782203-032",
      "text": "Cooperation is sustained only when the promise of future profits outweighs the present value of defecting, so a discount factor that is too low, or a game known to be ending soon, makes defection the rational choice.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "repeated games with end periods",
        "impatient players or high discounting"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Therefore, the promise of future profits must outweigh the present value to en- sure cooperation.",
      "text_sha256": "96f5d15dd67b7b8d737c2d8e912fe4b58e1f80350c6b5a406e339add090d07b3",
      "source_sha256": "ab8a22d0dbb026a09212a4c85963f3c05787cf80775e8613ae3724e3883e7a56",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782203-033",
      "text": "Anonymity increases rather than decreases the value of reputation tokens, because when potential business partners have less knowledge of a counterparty's identity, the number of reputation tokens held becomes the more important signal.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "anonymous or pseudonymous networks",
        "incomplete information about counterparties"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "When potential business partners have less knowledge of your identity, the knowledge from the number of reputation tokens you hold becomes more important.",
      "text_sha256": "7e28b32b470a4606943c51901eacdda93b70109ed594df1e4d3502244f9ad2eb",
      "source_sha256": "ab8a22d0dbb026a09212a4c85963f3c05787cf80775e8613ae3724e3883e7a56",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782203-034",
      "text": "The deterrent power of reputation tokens grows with network size, because the loss of opportunity from having reputation slashed increases as the network gets larger.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "open global networks",
        "digital reputation tokens"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Another advantage to digital tokens in open global networks is that the loss of opportunity from having your reputation slashed grows as the size of the network in- creases.",
      "text_sha256": "e400d0fdb68346798070044945c2e05701f51001fc3b3286a0e3c098e68b1783",
      "source_sha256": "ab8a22d0dbb026a09212a4c85963f3c05787cf80775e8613ae3724e3883e7a56",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782203-036",
      "text": "Paying contributors in reputation tokens rather than fees, and then distributing all fees as a periodic reputation weighted salary, defeats the sockpuppet attack because splitting a holding across many accounts yields exactly the same share of fees.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "dao",
        "tokenomics",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "anonymous DAOs with multiple accounts per member",
        "all DAO fees pooled and shared"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 76
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782203-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "A periodic reputation-weighted salary will distribute all fees the DAO earns to all members. Individuals who perform tasks that bring fees to the DAO will be rewarded with reputation tokens, not the fees. Members who own more reputation tokens share in a larger percentage of the fees.",
      "text_sha256": "f65d01ac9dfe1967825a43c502a30d3e50748cc708a500d3441b297fd7e60f6b",
      "source_sha256": "ab8a22d0dbb026a09212a4c85963f3c05787cf80775e8613ae3724e3883e7a56",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782205-004",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782205-004",
      "text": "A DAO will not be a genuinely profitable addition to the economy until decentralized versions of the legal system, the political system, the media, banking, and other services exist to support it.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "institutional-design",
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "systemic-risk"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "profit-seeking DAOs competing in the contemporary economy"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782205-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The legal system, the political system, the media, banking, and other services are all needed before the first DAO will be a genuinely profitable addition to our economy.",
      "text_sha256": "bb0b5ac9373f1886db8b2a1d72ba808605d8284c7868ccfb3830f33a1950b771",
      "source_sha256": "5ba52c63e81019b6867fb29c4a50821ff574e510d79b31b8ce9f4c726a0ebc71",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782205-008",
      "type": "Claim",
