    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782205-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "News services (oracles) and information repositories need to be decentralized.",
      "text_sha256": "4476e4e624e1459f4de1700d8b5492551523d9f02a35ca445a76c462f809bebb",
      "source_sha256": "5ba52c63e81019b6867fb29c4a50821ff574e510d79b31b8ce9f4c726a0ebc71",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782210-008",
      "text": "A Web of Trust style reputation ledger, in which each party rates each transaction and reputation is summed with weightings by rater reputation, will have all of its value drained by the sockpuppet attack, because an attacker can build reputation through transactions between their own fake accounts and then use it to cheat.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation",
        "regulatory-failure"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "open networks that permit account creation",
        "self-reported transaction ratings"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Unfortunately, the sockpuppet attack will suck all value from the network. Setting up fake accounts, an attacker can build their reputation by making transactions be- tween their own accounts. Once their reputation is sufficiently large to trick a mem- ber, they can use it to cheat the system.",
      "text_sha256": "3842ccea55d1a414727b927f9c61efbc21a2e13e6bb1d4e6578461c7dd396443",
      "source_sha256": "9cc531ab239f6266c8aeddcc8e54f4c06029c44e825444bee137bbcc0c9d0a8e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-011",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782210-011",
      "text": "The Web of Trust works acceptably for low-value information transmission but should not be used for transactions involving larger wealth in the general economy, which is part of why the scheme it originated in is called pretty good privacy rather than good privacy.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "high value economic transactions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-011:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "It works well for low-value infor- mation transmission, but it should not be used for transactions involving larger wealth in the general economy.",
      "text_sha256": "618b13fdda09d5c33ffbb81df9593bc6caa24075164a81b6d1b545a967d87701",
      "source_sha256": "9cc531ab239f6266c8aeddcc8e54f4c06029c44e825444bee137bbcc0c9d0a8e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-025",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782210-025",
      "text": "Sockpuppet attacks are inevitable in any organization that wants open membership and anonymous members, and since those properties are essential to the autonomy that makes a global decentralized organization efficient, reputation must be weighted every time it is used.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "open membership",
        "anonymous or pseudonymous members"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Sockpuppet attacks are inevitable if you want the membership to be open and to allow anonymous members. These properties are essential for fostering the individual autonomy that makes a global decentralized organization efficient and powerful.",
      "text_sha256": "81b558526e63926203453bdae15996e5e48797fb15f9d930121a0289ea6b2667",
      "source_sha256": "9cc531ab239f6266c8aeddcc8e54f4c06029c44e825444bee137bbcc0c9d0a8e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-026",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782210-026",
      "text": "Every single reputational implementation the authors have audited in the blockchain DAO space carries the flaw of vulnerability to the sockpuppet attack on the Web of Trust model.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "compliance",
        "dao",
        "blockchain",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "blockchain DAO reputation systems audited by the authors as of writing"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 61
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-026:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This is the flaw in every single reputational implementation we've audited in the blockchain DAO",
      "text_sha256": "a57c1a7cdb315f174bb0d9124742fca4f3c2577004286b61caf8492e9334ec4f",
      "source_sha256": "9cc531ab239f6266c8aeddcc8e54f4c06029c44e825444bee137bbcc0c9d0a8e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-027",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782210-027",
      "text": "SingularityNet's reputation system, which tracks self-reported transaction quality, transaction value, duration of satisfaction, and prior reputation weights, will have its value eroded by the sockpuppet attack once the system becomes valuable enough to merit attack, because it does not implement the other necessities.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "systems implementing only a subset of the seven necessities",
        "once the reputation becomes valuable enough to merit attack"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-027:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Without implementing the other necessities, the sockpuppet attack will eventually erode their value, once it becomes valuable enough to merit the attack.",
      "text_sha256": "83f242d3f10fd8319cb62d2ed6b68d4d7032b52697dec2fe38fd6bcc71a207c6",
      "source_sha256": "9cc531ab239f6266c8aeddcc8e54f4c06029c44e825444bee137bbcc0c9d0a8e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782210-028",
      "text": "With the balanced staking and fee-sharing necessities implemented, the cost of faking reputation is at an absolute minimum double the value of that reputation, which is how reputation is made more valuable than money.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "both the balanced staking necessity and the shared salary necessity are implemented"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "With #e and #j implemented, the cost of faking your reputation is (at an absolute minimum) double the value of the reputation.",
      "text_sha256": "80751f81789a51b29f62f275b38e3dc017e4eecf326fbaee2499415ac969eca4",
      "source_sha256": "9cc531ab239f6266c8aeddcc8e54f4c06029c44e825444bee137bbcc0c9d0a8e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782210-029",
      "text": "Concentration of power is the greatest threat to any decentralized organization, because a single member or sub-coalition that gains a majority of power in an inherently democratic organization will eventually control it no matter what safeguards are in place, at which point the organization is no longer decentralized.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "democratic decentralized organizations",
        "especially profit-devoted and therefore competitive ones"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The idea is that if a single member, or even a sub-coalition, gains j\\% of the power in an inherently dem- ocratic organization, they will eventually control it, no matter what the safeguards are.",
      "text_sha256": "a5daf7da5678a9d4c69b3802e079464db6a759ced53e417406e542bb722f1d0e",
      "source_sha256": "9cc531ab239f6266c8aeddcc8e54f4c06029c44e825444bee137bbcc0c9d0a8e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782210-035",
      "text": "Reputation-based governance faces a chicken and egg problem: voting becomes more efficient once reputation is valuable, but reputation cannot become valuable without meaningful voting.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "economics",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "bootstrapping a reputation system on existing infrastructure"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-035:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This is another chicken and egg problem. Voting will be more efficient with valu- able reputation. Reputation can't be valuable without meaningful voting.",
      "text_sha256": "d3c8d52f5191e6778a3982e9b742482f5724853e5a534a552f89de4768bed7b1",
      "source_sha256": "9cc531ab239f6266c8aeddcc8e54f4c06029c44e825444bee137bbcc0c9d0a8e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782210-036",
      "text": "A meaningful reputational system with the potential for retrospective review would let a network rely on fewer nodes, since randomly selected nodes staking their reputation can do the polling work and be reviewed and punished later, which is one reason proof of stake is more efficient than proof of work.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "consensus is near unanimous nearly all the time",
        "Byzantine behavior is detectable on later review"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "But if we had a meaningful reputa- tional system with the potential for review, we could rely on fewer nodes. This mech- anism is one reason proof of stake is more efficient than proof of work.",
      "text_sha256": "574b37a651d49a29cb5617fae189a12ef2f41100043259d07539be7f75af002c",
      "source_sha256": "9cc531ab239f6266c8aeddcc8e54f4c06029c44e825444bee137bbcc0c9d0a8e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-040",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782210-040",
      "text": "The Maghribi traders show that reputation alone can sustain a decentralized network under extreme information asymmetry: using only handwritten letters, Jewish merchants built a reputational system spanning the Silk Road in which nothing but the promise of better reputation deterred agents from cheating.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "empirical-evidence",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "historical trading networks with communication latency on the order of months",
        "agents with complete control of assets"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 61
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782210-040:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Nothing incentivized the agents from cheating except the promise of building better reputation.",
      "text_sha256": "b432820ff54b507fe28c6e57b2407ff16caa02b7cd1999992e641ddf93b695b2",
      "source_sha256": "9cc531ab239f6266c8aeddcc8e54f4c06029c44e825444bee137bbcc0c9d0a8e",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782214-001",
      "text": "Reputation changes the incentive structure of a decentralized organization from a single stage, zero sum game into a repeated positive sum game, which is why the authors treat reputation as the key to effective decentralized governance.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "economics",
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "the reputation system is formally linked to the organization's profits"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 60
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Reputation changes the incentive structure from a single-stage, zero-sum game to a repeated positive-sum game.",
      "text_sha256": "a66010ed32626d40407a41ad16b6e43bf2f60d582aadced384fa078b88c99615",
      "source_sha256": "ba892bb200c1455447c0014f5067a501a93ea9ec413c31942d95952eb3bdfd9d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782214-024",
      "text": "Reputation can be objectively valued by estimating the probability of future business deals, taking the expected value of that probability, and computing the present value of those deals, which is what makes reputation function as a promise of future rewards.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "economics",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation is tied to a stream of future business opportunities"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Reputation gives the promise of future rewards. Reputation can be objectively valued, by estimating the probability of future business deals, taking the expected value of that probability, and calculating the present value of those business deals.",
      "text_sha256": "c6e74d3a34086edb0154bdf9c037d9921ffb7fdecc15b832ddd283cb93249401",
      "source_sha256": "ba892bb200c1455447c0014f5067a501a93ea9ec413c31942d95952eb3bdfd9d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-025",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782214-025",
      "text": "No centralized platform such as Amazon or eBay has been able to create meaningful and secure online reputation, because central ownership and control prevent them from giving members the power and incentives needed to police their own reputation.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "centrally owned and controlled platforms"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "No centralized platform, such as Amazon or eBay, has been able to create mean- ingful and secure online reputation. Because they are centrally owned and controlled they cannot give members the power and incentives they need to police their own reputation,",
      "text_sha256": "7962ae42c170bfde90adfcaa35be2d7974242442a75f7df86f771334321a31b1",
      "source_sha256": "ba892bb200c1455447c0014f5067a501a93ea9ec413c31942d95952eb3bdfd9d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-026",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782214-026",
      "text": "The alternatives to a reputational system for countering profit driven instability, namely external stabilizing forces such as governmental fiat and rapidly expanding profit opportunities, are inadequate because expansion driven stability lasts only as long as the expansion does.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "organizations destabilized by profit competition"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-026:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Alternatives to reputational systems for countering the instability generated by profit competition include external stabilizing forces (such as governmental fiat) or rapidly expanding profit opportunities (which will only stabilize a group until the ex- pansion stops).",
      "text_sha256": "2a86281ccb082bd8b644c75d25b6185834ceac24a329af64267b5602ea184233",
      "source_sha256": "ba892bb200c1455447c0014f5067a501a93ea9ec413c31942d95952eb3bdfd9d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-027",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782214-027",
      "text": "The two sources of instability require different remedies and must not be swapped: dynamic rules are a mismatch for instability caused by the profit motive, and a reputational system is not an efficient method for attenuating instability caused by a group's diverse values.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-027:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Trying to institute dynamic rules to attenuate the instability due to a for-profit motive is a mismatch. Similarly instituting a reputational system is not an efficient method for attenuating the instability due to a group's diverse values.",
      "text_sha256": "38105508757a992d760e85cf1e7d736d473043acc7855b99f259130cd0b2af38",
      "source_sha256": "ba892bb200c1455447c0014f5067a501a93ea9ec413c31942d95952eb3bdfd9d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782214-029",
      "text": "If unanimous consensus is strongly incentivized in every validation pool, a DAO will degenerate quickly, because members holding minority opinions will not raise alternatives for fear of losing all their reputation tokens; this is why loosely coupled votes are needed.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "contentious protocol development",
        "validation pools that penalize minority positions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "If unanimous consen- sus is strongly incentivized by every validation pool, our DAOs will degenerate quickly, as alternative options will not be raised by members with minority opinions for fear they will lose all reputation tokens.",
      "text_sha256": "658876c1a54284d8321ad894d618593319c76c2af8a6d4b166706bd41a22276d",
      "source_sha256": "ba892bb200c1455447c0014f5067a501a93ea9ec413c31942d95952eb3bdfd9d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782214-030",
      "text": "Loosely coupled voting, in which staked reputation cannot be lost, encourages dissenting opinions, while tightly coupled voting, in which losing stakes are redistributed, guarantees consensus; a DAO steers deliberation by moving between the two.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation weighted validation pools"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 55
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Loosely-coupled voting encourages dissenting opinions. Tightly-coupled voting guarantees consensus.",
      "text_sha256": "5687fd56df92bd0a94bb4cdb93a62a6b793e7a770a85a47316cf6e7911b47ba9",
      "source_sha256": "ba892bb200c1455447c0014f5067a501a93ea9ec413c31942d95952eb3bdfd9d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782214-036",
      "text": "Equal distribution of output, where every member receives an equal share regardless of contribution, is impossible to maintain under current technology in a system with open access and privacy, because sockpuppet accounts would be abused.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "citation-and-knowledge"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "open access membership",
        "privacy or pseudonymity preserved",
        "current identity technology"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This is impossible to maintain under the current technology with open access and privacy, since sockpuppet accounts would be abused. Improvements in ZK proofs and identity protocols, however, will soon make it possible to efficiently and securely com- bat such sockpuppet attacks.",
      "text_sha256": "577cabe7678008e491b48f56edfe4ae2ad644ae306ac6a16b0277b0c82f6e72f",
      "source_sha256": "ba892bb200c1455447c0014f5067a501a93ea9ec413c31942d95952eb3bdfd9d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782214-039",
      "text": "Because major social media platforms are privately and centrally owned, their governance processes and reputation distribution algorithms are necessarily opaque, since their users' incentives are not aligned to police reputation against gaming.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "decentralization",
        "disclosure",
        "regulatory-failure"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "privately owned centralized platforms",
        "users hold no financial stake in the system"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Since Stack Overflow and Reddit and Facebook and Twitter and all the other successful social media sites are privately, centrally owned, their governance processes\u2014their algorithms for distributing reputation\u2014are necessarily opaque.",
      "text_sha256": "afaa4628f79824b19ede7d37d805605ba42772f63ecd691813e202aee42efc5a",
      "source_sha256": "ba892bb200c1455447c0014f5067a501a93ea9ec413c31942d95952eb3bdfd9d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-040",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782214-040",
      "text": "Against Eric Raymond's argument that love does not scale, the authors hold that reputation does: weighted democracy, properly measured and aggregated, can scale from valuing local expertise to valuing expertise on global issues.",
      "claim_type": "normative",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation valuations across DAOs reach equilibrium through market freedom"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782214-040:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Love doesn't scale, but reputation does. Weighted democracy, properly meas- ured and aggregated, can scale from valuating expertise on a local level to expertise on global issues.",
      "text_sha256": "d8647248d917560dc40d427496bbd192cd6f7611e3071b4e2461f2a5620ad650",
      "source_sha256": "ba892bb200c1455447c0014f5067a501a93ea9ec413c31942d95952eb3bdfd9d",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782216-001",
      "text": "The decentralized economy cannot fully proliferate until it acquires the institutions ordinary commerce depends on, above all a secure and meaningful reputation system for anonymous supranational partners and an effective, dynamic governance system.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "defi",
        "decentralization",
        "economics",
        "reputation",
        "governance-design",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "the decentralized economy as of the early 2020s"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 57
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "the decentralized economy is missing the major institutions that our society relies on to conduct profitable business, especially a secure and meaningful system for evaluating reputation for anonymous supranational partners, and an effective and dynamic governance system",
      "text_sha256": "56a6b403ffb7f848d37d2d15e6096f21bbabd080aa877b9ffb439e1219a4fc9f",
      "source_sha256": "f1739743aa06bbc1641cd65da790d531b69d8628ea3f5cc3fcad1bf5a1242373",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-006",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782216-006",
      "text": "Maintaining consensus without a central authority forces a reputation system to verify members' votes extremely redundantly, which imposes serious computational overhead.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized networks with no central authority"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 48
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-006:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In order to maintain consensus in a decentralized network, with no central authority to check in with, a reputational system needs to verify each others' votes extremely redundantly, which leads to serious overhead costs in computation.",
      "text_sha256": "c27ca4f3696b3c3bfcb2774e6ca83f18838a067da3f23870524fd476c831b8a7",
      "source_sha256": "f1739743aa06bbc1641cd65da790d531b69d8628ea3f5cc3fcad1bf5a1242373",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782216-008",
      "text": "Liquidity has always been a problem on decentralized exchanges because meaningful history and reputation cannot form where there is little or no governance structure, no insurance, no appeals process and no reputable decentralized news service.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "defi",
        "reputation",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "But liquidity has always been a problem in decentralized exchanges, as meaning- ful history and reputation are difficult to achieve when there is little to no governance structure, no insurance, no appeals process, and no reputable decentralized news ser- vice",
      "text_sha256": "42819340d9972fd1cdf4eb210eb9600727c367493632e7ff7dfac92dfb75d947",
      "source_sha256": "f1739743aa06bbc1641cd65da790d531b69d8628ea3f5cc3fcad1bf5a1242373",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-014",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782216-014",
      "text": "Reputation must be grounded to be meaningful, so reputation tokens should be minted only when policy premia enter the group, reputation should dictate power, and fees should be shared through reputation weighted salaries.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics",
        "dao",
        "defi",
        "governance-design",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "design for an Underwriting DAO"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 65
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-014:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Reputation needs to be grounded to be meaningful, so reputation tokens should only be minted when fees (policy premia) enter the group. Reputation should dictate power in the group. So, reputation should determine how the fees are shared, through reputation-weighted salaries.",
      "text_sha256": "45efd083b74acbe6db69c0cffd060f8b755c7bd6f8233c28a9574806c5613c25",
      "source_sha256": "f1739743aa06bbc1641cd65da790d531b69d8628ea3f5cc3fcad1bf5a1242373",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782216-015",
      "text": "Because underwriting mints new reputation tokens, passive holders see their proportional ownership in the DAO fall over time, which is designed to incentivize agents to underwrite actively while still allowing passive investors to earn income.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "defi",
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Underwriting DAO that rewards underwriting with newly minted tokens"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Thus, the total number of tokens grows over time. This implies that \"passive\" agents who hold the tokens purely to receive a share of future premia will find their proportional ownership in the DAO decrease over time.",
      "text_sha256": "425d64237c4c8f25efeb5709327c67dc647099a0f8f62ecc66f263df21433fbb",
      "source_sha256": "f1739743aa06bbc1641cd65da790d531b69d8628ea3f5cc3fcad1bf5a1242373",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782216-016",
      "text": "Underwriters encumber reputation tokens against each policy under a preset formula, and if the insured event occurs they lose control of those tokens, which are auctioned to meet the claim, with new tokens minted and sold if the auction falls short.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "defi",
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Underwriting DAO design"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In case the insured event were to occur during the life of the policy, the agents who underwrote the policy would lose control of their encumbered tokens, which would be sold at auction to meet the claim.",
      "text_sha256": "5d1f3d6fc73aa14c2ff318a571b2b8782695d637134849f5a7937ee740e7a246",
      "source_sha256": "f1739743aa06bbc1641cd65da790d531b69d8628ea3f5cc3fcad1bf5a1242373",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782216-017",
      "text": "In the Underwriting DAO a breach occurs only when the market values the encumbered reputation tokens at less than the payout, which requires minting additional tokens to meet the claim.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "defi",
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Underwriting DAO with encumbered reputation tokens"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "We would consider the need to mint more reputation tokens to meet a policy claim to be a breach. Under what circumstances would a breach occur? It would occur only if the market values the encumbered reputation tokens as less than the payout.",
      "text_sha256": "2c9176bae6ffab87022ac193a41c690f7115833409657e2523d387fcbc6a9d99",
      "source_sha256": "f1739743aa06bbc1641cd65da790d531b69d8628ea3f5cc3fcad1bf5a1242373",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782216-018",
      "text": "From the viewpoint of consumers and regulators, encumbered reputation tokens serve as a substitute for capital, because they derive their value from the DAO's future cash flows.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "defi",
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Underwriting DAO whose tokens are claims on future cash flows"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The key point is this: from the viewpoint of consumers and regulators, the encumbered tokens (which as we know derive their value from the DAO's future cash flows) essentially serve as a substitute for capital.",
      "text_sha256": "d77753f1e9ed0fe64ba632e839d17c50dee0aa31794ac09b194fd1906978b70f",
      "source_sha256": "f1739743aa06bbc1641cd65da790d531b69d8628ea3f5cc3fcad1bf5a1242373",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782216-037",
      "text": "Once secure and meaningful reputation is incorporated into Web3, the collateral imbalance will reverse, and because reputation tokens are more meaningful than identity and easier to value, less collateralization will be required than in traditional protocols.",
      "claim_type": "predictive",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics",
        "defi"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "requires a coherent system that securely tracks the value of a reputation token"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, once secure and meaningful reputation is incorporated into the WebT environment, this imbalance will be reversed. Since reputation tokens are more mean- ingful than identity, and much easier to valuate, even less collateralization will be re- quired than traditional protocols",
      "text_sha256": "1c15b221968e033a48d8f14751d2e8cde404ed62bb264b37079074a92e8e1b21",
      "source_sha256": "f1739743aa06bbc1641cd65da790d531b69d8628ea3f5cc3fcad1bf5a1242373",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-040",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782216-040",
      "text": "The decentralized economy still lacks trustworthy open source decentralized institutions for recording and parsing history, reporting news and guiding attention, without which the average person cannot judge which networks to join or what to invest in.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "institutional-design",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782216-040:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "We need trustworthy open source decentralized institutions for recording and parsing history, for investigating and reporting the news, for guiding our attention to the future.",
      "text_sha256": "7908f684f595d24074dd1f21ddc668759a1c25128a52a406721c422556dc2cb3",
      "source_sha256": "f1739743aa06bbc1641cd65da790d531b69d8628ea3f5cc3fcad1bf5a1242373",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782217-001",
      "text": "Market liquidity depends on trustworthiness, and trustworthiness depends on observed momentum: isolated instances of motion are insufficient, because the observations must be collected into a history before they carry weight and meaning.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "defi",
        "reputation",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "marketplaces seeking liquidity"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "To achieve liquidity, marketplaces must be trustworthy. They need momen- tum. It's not enough to achieve motion in any particular instance. Momentum must be observed to give trust to the marketplace. These observations need to be collected in a history to give them weight and meaning.",
      "text_sha256": "29386d89e633821666564ae4bd1ba64cd0b86af10a2bfff16ae9a66011179de5",
      "source_sha256": "358779557d8e7dcd101720ca0fad90b9146d24f1c7c03909eb431fcf1fb7e103",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782217-002",
      "text": "Governance in a decentralized organization depends on meaningful reputation, and the meaning of any reputation is determined by its history and by how that history is analyzed and presented, which makes historiography a governance variable rather than a neutral record.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "reputation",
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized organizations"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 57
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Governance relies on meaningful reputation to de- cide who or what to focus on. The meaning of reputation is determined by its history and how that history is analyzed and presented.",
      "text_sha256": "b0032c23a86412d40945b81a3bdf24756c71b7ecf5c611241eb606e4aacdf573",
      "source_sha256": "358779557d8e7dcd101720ca0fad90b9146d24f1c7c03909eb431fcf1fb7e103",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-011",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782217-011",
      "text": "In the SchellingCoin approach to oracle design, members stake reputation tokens on their answer to the question a DApp is asking and are rewarded according to how close they came to the resulting median value, which functions as the game theoretic Schelling point.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "smart-contracts",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "questions with a verifiable focal answer"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-011:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The idea is to have your Oracle DAO members stake their reputation tokens on their answer to a question a DApp is asking. Then you reward those closer to the resulting median value",
      "text_sha256": "99f34dc4fc4eff73a4d0e17c4a5f7aaa246a94af3b2fa972227b578221245bf6",
      "source_sha256": "358779557d8e7dcd101720ca0fad90b9146d24f1c7c03909eb431fcf1fb7e103",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782217-012",
      "text": "The protocols governing how a particular oracle question is answered should be set by the subject matter experts themselves rather than by a static centralized hierarchy, because the experts know best how their own system can be gamed and how to prevent that gaming to protect their hard earned reputation.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "smart-contracts",
        "regulatory-failure",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "domain specific oracle questions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 53
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Giving the experts, them- selves, control of their own organization is better than relying on a static centralized hierarchy. The experts know best how to game their own system, and how to prevent gaming to protect their hard-earned reputation.",
      "text_sha256": "5d482bb9e7bff12d93b672e2f6c921677f5350a0c8995799c6e21aa2cc4d03ee",
      "source_sha256": "358779557d8e7dcd101720ca0fad90b9146d24f1c7c03909eb431fcf1fb7e103",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782217-013",
      "text": "Robust decentralized oracles do not yet exist despite well funded proposals, because decentralized oracles are themselves DAOs and therefore inherit the same missing incentive structure, governance processes, and history that all DAOs suffer from.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "smart-contracts",
        "dao",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "state of the technology at the time of writing"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Put simply, decentralized oracles are DAOs, so they still lack the proper incentive structure and governance processes and history that all DAOs suffer from.",
      "text_sha256": "791fc2592b28a99b6a021318bbef7bc6a86b4105b34d0d9a67c31dd02875b2d1",
      "source_sha256": "358779557d8e7dcd101720ca0fad90b9146d24f1c7c03909eb431fcf1fb7e103",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782217-028",
      "text": "Reputation in a news DAO must be anchored in fungible currency: new reputation should be minted only when articles connect to profitable endeavors such as advertising, paid analyses, or protocols relied upon for decentralized business contracts.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "news DAOs building meaningful reputation"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "articles must have a foun- dational meaning in fungible currency. New reputation should only be minted when the articles are connected to profitable endeavors\u2014advertising, paid analyses, new protocols that are relied upon for decentralized business contracts.",
      "text_sha256": "889eb53e0a465969850c25eae9e8a8162f12123306be2f7d57141e900db5f292",
      "source_sha256": "358779557d8e7dcd101720ca0fad90b9146d24f1c7c03909eb431fcf1fb7e103",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782217-029",
      "text": "Reviewers in a news review DAO will give honest reviews despite being paid fees, because the reputational system rewards members mostly on the basis of future fees rather than present ones.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation systems weighted toward future fee streams"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Reviewers will be incentivized to give honest reviews despite fees, because the reputational system rewards members mostly based on future fees.",
      "text_sha256": "537ee9c71ec4e65809b40cb570ae81f3aa47676ecc1ef73b24d56737494fc324",
      "source_sha256": "358779557d8e7dcd101720ca0fad90b9146d24f1c7c03909eb431fcf1fb7e103",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782217-030",
      "text": "Tracking and aggregating reputations across DAOs can build a more accurate picture of a person's expertise and experiential gaps than traditional educational institutions provide, which would quickly reveal meaningless certification and licensure programs as worthless.",
      "claim_type": "predictive",
      "topics": [
        "education-and-practice",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation systems anchored in profitable endeavor"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Tracking and aggregating our reputations in various DAOs can build a more accurate picture of our expertise and experiential gaps than our tra- ditional educational institutions have.",
      "text_sha256": "7add60023c9d3859376319cf7a402e9a924dfdb4a6bcc14f1341e49a76af454a",
      "source_sha256": "358779557d8e7dcd101720ca0fad90b9146d24f1c7c03909eb431fcf1fb7e103",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782217-031",
      "text": "Transparency in a decentralized network is not optional: every function needs to be publicly auditable for people to trust it, because without a central authority to approve code, unexpected malicious behavior can be built into any opaque code.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "disclosure",
        "compliance",
        "open-source-and-code",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized networks without a central approving authority"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782217-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Transparency is crucial in a decentralized net- work. Every function needs to be publicly auditable for people to trust it. Without a central authority to approve it, unexpected malicious behavior can be built into any opaque code.",
      "text_sha256": "7cd9b46406340a6a414c8d49459a379e57e90bdc9e11d24c47647d910ddf98f9",
      "source_sha256": "358779557d8e7dcd101720ca0fad90b9146d24f1c7c03909eb431fcf1fb7e103",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
