    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782220-001",
      "text": "Strong unifying values are the institution most essential to the long-term stability of a decentralized organization, and they demand continual reevaluation rather than one-time specification.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "institutional-design",
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized organizations",
        "long time horizons"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This final essential institution is the most important for long-term stability, and demands eternal reevaluation. Decentralized organizations require strong unifying values to remain coherent.",
      "text_sha256": "e8056fea4b7cc341692d552d3b24d7159ff978d503e44fb7abca33416797f747",
      "source_sha256": "f0bf1e80c6da60a6f8ba20630562bdf1dab171ccb5267f497dc0b815113cde99",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782220-002",
      "text": "Because a single global society is emerging in which everyone is densely interconnected, the more efficient and stable arrangement is power decentralization giving individuals and subgroup DAOs autonomous power, not a single power-centralized hierarchy controlling the whole.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "globally interconnected society"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "the better, more efficient, more stable state of this global society is an organi- zation that is power decentralized, giving individuals and subgroup DAOs more auton- omous power to contribute to the health and wealth and happiness of all.",
      "text_sha256": "dd4ce928bba845bb4c20cc3affbff904f51129987604b1c948f42061afcb3d4f",
      "source_sha256": "f0bf1e80c6da60a6f8ba20630562bdf1dab171ccb5267f497dc0b815113cde99",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782220-015",
      "text": "Overhead institutions that protect or promote essentials should be governed and borne by the group, while those protecting nonessentials should be governed and borne privately, with each DAO deciding for itself what is essential to its function.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "per DAO determination",
        "democratic decision within the DAO's own system"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Overhead institutions to protect or promote essentials should be governed and borne by the group, protecting and promoting non- essentials should be governed and borne privately. Each DAO must decide what is es- sential to its function;",
      "text_sha256": "2e4c7823d3ddfda9f0174368069bff9eae93e30e707792aa951923537a0a68f6",
      "source_sha256": "f0bf1e80c6da60a6f8ba20630562bdf1dab171ccb5267f497dc0b815113cde99",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782220-017",
      "text": "Demand for insurance and reputation policing runs counter to prosperity: when the system runs well and everyone profits there is less need for insurance, and when profits fall and competition intensifies cheating becomes more attractive and more policing is needed.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "competitive market conditions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "If the system is running well and everyone is profiting, there is less need for insurance. When the profits decrease and the system becomes more competitive, cheating becomes more attractive, and more insurance and reputation policing is needed.",
      "text_sha256": "254b38c2f8429dbc65b185053b90142c9155baf2c9ac76ca98d125fb84d7b9a3",
      "source_sha256": "f0bf1e80c6da60a6f8ba20630562bdf1dab171ccb5267f497dc0b815113cde99",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782220-019",
      "text": "Where the line between public and private information falls is a function of a society's values, as the divergence between American, German, and Chinese practice shows.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "cross-national comparison"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The line between what is public information and private information is a function of a society's values.",
      "text_sha256": "b288bc78b9365b96683b6dab429b6c3675215f1e201cf31a2fdd6e9f31549415",
      "source_sha256": "f0bf1e80c6da60a6f8ba20630562bdf1dab171ccb5267f497dc0b815113cde99",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782220-024",
      "text": "Individual autonomy and group cohesion reinforce rather than substitute for each other: the network effect is achieved only when individuals subsume their freedom to act in concert with the group, and diminishing one quality diminishes the other.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "network organizations"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The network effect is only achieved when individuals subsume their freedom to act in concert with the group. Again, both individual autonomy and group cohesion need to be balanced to increase both qualities. Diminishing one diminishes the other.",
      "text_sha256": "e8bfbe3544eb91588357de5435e0ef0c75af6dd50b54c0dda45200c792fac339",
      "source_sha256": "f0bf1e80c6da60a6f8ba20630562bdf1dab171ccb5267f497dc0b815113cde99",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782220-027",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782220-027",
      "text": "A long-term successful network requires a dynamic and responsive governance system that keeps the organization in the decentralized democratic realm and prevents it from moving to the next natural stage of centralized governance with a static hierarchy.",
