      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808859-040:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Without such basic infrastructure products, on-chain governance of blockchains may not be or may only limitedly be possible.",
      "text_sha256": "9c08103c0a89dbc8abd93e84aa30399972937d73bb40772fec91917e7ea18afc",
      "source_sha256": "304ad25d43b5ecea3158e3a2ca04e6e1e3bd2958e2134e2dcefbfedf3b6f3ab7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808867-009",
      "text": "Decentralism holds that trust in a system should not be controlled by corruptible human constructs and institutions run by a limited number of fallible humans; instead trust rests on technology enhanced individualism and technology facilitated collective human action.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "contrast with capitalist trusted intermediaries and socialist belief in government infallibility"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "decentralism posits that trust in the system should not be controlled by corruptible human constructs and institutions that are controlled by a limited number of fallible and corruptible humans. Rather, trust in decentralism is based on technology-enhanced individualism.",
      "text_sha256": "822743d48cafb441f54d0975f86a14e809076c778c85febef5ac2a16a48aec1a",
      "source_sha256": "eeccf6d0587bd278a96ce6ac8ec5003e26d161c245f6c94b4144d84f374802eb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808867-010",
      "text": "Legally created trust is limited because it is only indirectly democratically legitimized, and is therefore arbitrary, inflexible, untimely, resistant to change, dependent on fallible human centric decision processes, and confined to human speed.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "law-and-legal-systems"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "trust created by legal guarantees and judicial enforcement in capitalist and socialist systems"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Legally created trust is often limited as it can be arbitrary because it is only indirectly democratically legitimized, inflexible, untimely, resistant to change, with fallible human-centric decision processes, and human speed.",
      "text_sha256": "adcd8d16970001df9c5ad4b3a1aef9dcc02333a8bc9b55d11e1d6ac9b4c967ff",
      "source_sha256": "eeccf6d0587bd278a96ce6ac8ec5003e26d161c245f6c94b4144d84f374802eb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808867-012",
      "text": "Delegating one's vote to a third party whose ethics and belief system the voter does not truly know produces suboptimal outcomes, and delegated voting on issues that cannot be foreseen is corrupting.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "representative democracies in the 21st century"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The very notion of delegating one's vote to a third party without true knowledge of the ethics and belief system of such a third party creates suboptimal outcomes. Delegated voting on issues one cannot foresee corrupts.",
      "text_sha256": "35ed58d9130edbe87fef3534fd1057b7edadf60b3f9578ccb22ab9d88e956ee2",
      "source_sha256": "eeccf6d0587bd278a96ce6ac8ec5003e26d161c245f6c94b4144d84f374802eb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808867-013",
      "text": "Elected representatives are incentivized to maintain their own power of office rather than to vote for outcomes reflecting the presumptive wishes and needs of their constituents.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "representative democracies"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Voted representatives are not incentivized to vote for outcomes that reflect the presumptive wishes and needs of their constituents but for maintaining their own power of office.",
      "text_sha256": "d06dc3fc32dc119f96633c9db2cb6ef2bc1b0b79bd9f98972afef2796a7a95a5",
      "source_sha256": "eeccf6d0587bd278a96ce6ac8ec5003e26d161c245f6c94b4144d84f374802eb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808867-015",
      "text": "Microdemocratic vote allocation improves voting outcomes because the proportion of votes a voter allocates to an issue evidences that voter's higher level of knowledge on the issue, and voters are unlikely to give top priority to issues they know little about.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "citation-and-knowledge"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "voting systems that allocate a maximum number of votes per voter across issues",
        "quadratic voting style designs"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Moreover, part of the power of this microdemocratic approach derives from the higher levels of knowledge a given voter has on a particular issue that is evidenced by the voters' proportional allocation of votes on such issue.",
      "text_sha256": "5f64454d6bb39509ba57599a94d7e361922a97f19c02477c4f50003cf7a4183d",
      "source_sha256": "eeccf6d0587bd278a96ce6ac8ec5003e26d161c245f6c94b4144d84f374802eb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808867-016",
      "text": "Microdemocratic systems must solve the tragedy of the commons, because without controls self interested voters acting independently of the totality of voters may deplete or spoil shared resources such as the environment and public goods.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "microdemocratic shared-resource systems",
        "absence of controls"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Without controls, some self-interested voters may be depleting or spoiling resources they share with the rest of society, such as the environment, public goods, among others.",
      "text_sha256": "3b6ce0032fa459d21aa1ed01db065ca83a3c32ab371a43d5fee1d61314a68534",
      "source_sha256": "eeccf6d0587bd278a96ce6ac8ec5003e26d161c245f6c94b4144d84f374802eb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808867-019",
      "text": "Unlike their centralized predecessors, decentralized technologies enable, for the first time in history, improved incentive designs that help overcome the insufficiencies in the voting outcomes of representative democracies.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
