    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-023",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808867-023",
      "text": "The conveniences and benefits of centralized algorithmic automation carry risks to humanity that cannot be fully quantified, and decentralized systems can counteract those downsides and threats.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-023:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "At the same time, the conveniences and benefits that derive from centralized algorithmic automation bring with them risks to humanity that cannot be fully quantified. Decentralized systems can counteract the downsides and threats of algorithmic automation",
      "text_sha256": "cadc5166761cf07523956fe21fc8bfd5e9c3866720c31337d042176d241c5f36",
      "source_sha256": "eeccf6d0587bd278a96ce6ac8ec5003e26d161c245f6c94b4144d84f374802eb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808867-030",
      "text": "Because a decentralized system has a blockchain based quasi precedent nature with a human backstop, it enables built in checks and balances capable of supporting resistance even to apocalyptic takeovers of algorithmic systems that would remove human presence to optimize efficiency.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "blockchain based systems with accumulated human voting records"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Because of its blockchain-based quasi- precedent nature with a human backstop, the decentralized system enables built-in checks and balances that can support resistance to even the most apocalyptic applications and takeover of algorithmic systems",
      "text_sha256": "a78a49a5d2e8c5f4196ca4f6214c0baf021169b60dac43846109ca7385b6e3df",
      "source_sha256": "eeccf6d0587bd278a96ce6ac8ec5003e26d161c245f6c94b4144d84f374802eb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808867-033",
      "text": "Code based trust lowers transaction costs and simultaneously raises consumer and market confidence and certainty, which facilitates economies of scale that are rarely possible in centralized structures, despite the cybersecurity problems associated with cryptocurrencies.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "code based decentralized applications",
        "presence of cybersecurity issues in cryptocurrency markets"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808867-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "code-based trust can help lower transaction costs, but it also increases consumer and overall market confidence and certainty, which facilitate economies of scale that are rarely possible in centralized structures",
      "text_sha256": "ccd594b86e417e6a48d3ddcb46f0cd822d74c1ac47b9df57fb5e37dc5cc79c52",
      "source_sha256": "eeccf6d0587bd278a96ce6ac8ec5003e26d161c245f6c94b4144d84f374802eb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808873-013",
      "text": "Applying decentralized technology to optimize a legacy system, for example using blockchain to improve the malfunctioning shareholder proxy voting process, perpetuates the outdated and malfunctioning centralized system rather than replacing it with a better performing decentralized one.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized technology deployed as an optimization layer on centralized legacy processes"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In the process, the outdated and malfunctioning centralized legacy systems are being perpetuated rather than being replaced with better performing decentralized systems.",
      "text_sha256": "bad5d332c9bef120555aab6b9eb3d1974c085b24bec8762ec4b7531511edbd20",
      "source_sha256": "f11493915e6b8c266d421510b5546816e33defb5650aac9d09b20d78549da727",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808873-018",
      "text": "Overreliance on the design of constitutional democracies limits experimentation with decentralized solutions for organizing society, because exclusive reliance on a single legal document combined with widespread voter apathy makes the constitutional model appear to be the only lasting form of organization.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "constitutional democracies as the dominant form of organizing society"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Overreliance on the design of constitutional democracies limits experimentation with decentralized solutions for the organization of society.",
      "text_sha256": "cf58294e724b79f4016382bcfa92bef1d876c615a65ee2e6839370399eb61f5e",
      "source_sha256": "f11493915e6b8c266d421510b5546816e33defb5650aac9d09b20d78549da727",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-020",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808873-020",
      "text": "Experimentation with decentralized organizational forms of society is curtailed by the principle of territorial integrity of nation states, a foundational principle of international law under which forced border change justifies war and which sustains a permanent national military presence.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "international legal order built on Article 2(4) of the UN Charter"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-020:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Experimentation with decentralized organizational forms of society is curtailed by the principle of territorial integrity of nation states.",
      "text_sha256": "a2c1913268fd7675f654d5002de1d52b2219f9868a8a202b7022049a5565a523",
      "source_sha256": "f11493915e6b8c266d421510b5546816e33defb5650aac9d09b20d78549da727",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-026",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808873-026",
      "text": "Regulatory solutions tracked the characteristics of issuers, so the more decentralized, censorship resistant and autonomous products that regulators could not control were left in a regulatory vacuum that limited their expansion, reach and evolution.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "jurisdiction specific regulatory frameworks of the early 2020s"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-026:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As a result, the more decentralized products that were more censorship resistant, autonomous, and could not be controlled by regulatory agencies, were largely left in a regulatory vacuum that limited their expansion, reach, and evolution.",
      "text_sha256": "993669f2b5bfbb3d7244a687352b7d6bc340b8d9c9e353b634937b3301d3f23a",
      "source_sha256": "f11493915e6b8c266d421510b5546816e33defb5650aac9d09b20d78549da727",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808873-033",
      "text": "Decentralized networks depend on dynamic governance because evolving blockchain protocols require updates, and the practice of hardforking that remained prevalent in the early 2020s created significant economic loss for such blockchains.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "governance-design",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "blockchain protocols requiring upgrades in the early 2020s"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As blockchains protocols evolve in a given market, they require updates. The practice of hardforking, that was still prevalent in the early 2020s, created significant economic loss for such blockchains.",
      "text_sha256": "80e1368ec96e8f9b6980156227efe415f97655079b43647712a36b68c28ed5a0",
      "source_sha256": "f11493915e6b8c266d421510b5546816e33defb5650aac9d09b20d78549da727",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808873-034",
      "text": "Because basic standards for the governance of digital assets were still missing at the beginning of the 2020s, the digital asset market stagnated and decentralized finance remained in its infancy; without standards and governance, certainty and market confidence cannot develop.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "defi",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "digital asset markets at the beginning of the 2020s"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "At the beginning of the 2020s, basic standards for the governance of digital assets were still missing. As a result, the digital asset market stagnated and DeFi (decentralized finance) remained in its infancy.",
      "text_sha256": "d26dcd4facedca7e9365b5463969be9927501ee47e19a8869d607a0de2cfeb73",
      "source_sha256": "f11493915e6b8c266d421510b5546816e33defb5650aac9d09b20d78549da727",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808873-035",
      "text": "DAO governance designs of the early 2020s failed to take account of the historical precedent on governance, and most DAOs used centralized master nodes to institute blockchain protocol and DAO upgrades.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized autonomous organizations at the beginning of the 2020s"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-035:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "At the beginning of the 2020s, the then existing DAO governance design structures failed to take into account the historical precedent on governance. Most DAOs utilized centralized forms of master nodes to institute blockchain protocol and DAO upgrades.",
      "text_sha256": "1f6561d251728fc2c5beeb1f666ec60e5ca936ec1fbf2a2f52767e1ae2c05fb6",
      "source_sha256": "f11493915e6b8c266d421510b5546816e33defb5650aac9d09b20d78549da727",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808873-037",
      "text": "Effective institutional governance, human or machine, requires a duality of incentives in which actors improve their own utility while their actions benefit the whole institution over the long run, and without that duality rational and opportunistic constituents will game the governance design.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "DAO governance designs facing internal and external opportunistic actors"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Human nature and any effective machine derivates of human engagements in institutional form require a duality of incentives in order to overcome attempts of rational and opportunistic internal and external constituents to game the governance design of a given DAO.",
      "text_sha256": "a500b370ac38d3cc92c826f69fdbf249cc9f4b5cb2f174b0efcebafd6345554a",
      "source_sha256": "f11493915e6b8c266d421510b5546816e33defb5650aac9d09b20d78549da727",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808873-038",
      "text": "When fungible assets are the dominant incentive design in the governance of DAOs with identifiable actors, rational and opportunistic internal and external participants will typically attempt to corrupt the governance design for their own gain; merit identifiers other than individual identity remove the most corruptive influences.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "DAO governance using fungible assets and identifiable actors"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "When fungible assets are used as the dominant incentive design in the governance of DAOs with identifiable actors, rational and opportunistic internal constituents and external participants will typically attempt to corrupt the governance design of the DAO for their own gain.",
      "text_sha256": "76c989d3d95c36827fde8063a4176e2af63928b16467b151dd7e2c5d0db34ebe",
      "source_sha256": "f11493915e6b8c266d421510b5546816e33defb5650aac9d09b20d78549da727",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-042",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3808873-042",
      "text": "A decentralized human backstop to code is a core and often overlooked infrastructure requirement, because without it the immutability of the blockchain and its cryptographic security may not create genuine transactional guarantees or trust between principals and agents in the integrity of their contractual relationship.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "smart-contracts",
        "reputation",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized algorithmic systems mediating principal agent contractual relationships"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 74
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3808873-042:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Without a decentralized human backstop to code, the immutability of the blockchain and its cryptographic security systems may not be able to create truly transactional guarantees and trust between principals and agents in the integrity of their contractual relationship.",
      "text_sha256": "60e41a7c2a30c69fc6e5ab3bd236f7c13f3625cb73022f99cbe1744cffd4d2b9",
      "source_sha256": "f11493915e6b8c266d421510b5546816e33defb5650aac9d09b20d78549da727",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3931933-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3931933-002",
      "text": "The core proposal of Hybrid Secure Proof of Stake is to separate block consensus from block rewards, making the reward a function of the node's reputation rather than of stake alone.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3931933-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The main concept in Hybrid Secure Proof of Stake (HSPoS) is to separate the block consensus from the block rewards. HSPoS proposes that the rewards become a function in the reputation of the node.",
      "text_sha256": "854bfbffdf071320f2dc75f997821ff9c2db4099f06814e758b4732edfbc25b3",
      "source_sha256": "55a71cdfceb96fadefba1f2fed9563b588825378c91aff644ee7faaccdf31204",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3931933-022",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3931933-022",
      "text": "Shasper governance is funded in a hardcoded way: each validator that succeeds in propagating a block allocates a fixed percentage of its block reward, denominated in SHAS, into a separate SDAO wallet, in addition to the ordinary Casper PoS allocation.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "tokenomics",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Shasper Network validators producing blocks under the Casper PoS consensus algorithm"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 58
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3931933-022:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, in addition to the Casper PoS Consensus algorithm allocation, each validator who succeeds in propagating a block allocates [__]% of the block reward, denominated in SHAS, into a separate SDAO wallet.",
      "text_sha256": "930b9ab323dd82708ffe19fe773d3f201f59c593e611bdc7a80c23dab56470d8",
