      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-011",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3936876-011",
      "text": "Hot storage buys easy access and quick transferability of digital assets at the cost of exposure to cyber attacks and to the difficulty of keeping private keys safe.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "defi"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "wallets stored and accessible online"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-011:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Hot storage ensures the easy access and quick transferability of digital assets but is also subject to possible asset security issues in the form of cyber attacks or issues with keeping private keys safe.",
      "text_sha256": "ad1ea54b2f94e9ea0a999ffa29eddb1c7ae35601b28562869cee9e3b9a422691",
      "source_sha256": "9bc0903d01910460298e754c451f027df4324367359800a98ee8e638d94aff55",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-014",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3936876-014",
      "text": "Because a wallet provider or exchange that has custody of a digital asset gains full control over transactions, hacking a digital asset exchange is equivalent to robbing a bank: the attacker obtains valuable cryptocurrency that can be cashed out.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "defi",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "exchanges holding pooled customer assets in hot storage"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-014:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As such, a hack of a digital asset exchange is akin to robbing a bank-- getting hold of valuable cryptocurrencies that they can cash out of.",
      "text_sha256": "f54dc3c07ecbdf5414152434df468e2a9819c04c645adc99d62cf42ecc80e429",
      "source_sha256": "9bc0903d01910460298e754c451f027df4324367359800a98ee8e638d94aff55",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3936876-017",
      "text": "Custodial exchanges are largely unprepared for breach: only 53 percent of small custodial exchanges and 78 percent of large custodial exchanges have a written policy setting out what happens to customer funds if a security breach causes loss.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "defi",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "custodial cryptocurrency exchanges surveyed in the 2017 benchmarking study"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Just 53% of small custodial exchanges and 78% of large custodial exchanges have a written policy outlining what happens to customer funds in the event of a security breach resulting in the loss of customer funds.",
      "text_sha256": "da9db0595786c183dcfd2fb25ed9dc7755e196724cde40a5ca4aea534ce2990f",
      "source_sha256": "9bc0903d01910460298e754c451f027df4324367359800a98ee8e638d94aff55",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3936876-024",
      "text": "Applying the trust label to digital asset firms without an accompanying fiduciary duty is problematic, because the typical legal obligation of a trust company is to place customers' interests above its own.",
      "claim_type": "normative",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "governance-design",
        "corporate-governance",
        "regulatory-failure"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "state trust charters used by digital asset firms"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 53
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The applicability of the trust label to digital asset firms, without a fiduciary duty, can be problematic. A typical legal obligation for trust companies is a fiduciary duty \u2013 to place customers' interests above the company's own.",
      "text_sha256": "e802871ef9e3ded0f9e2c6309440fccf73e0f3814ff7890a014dc02281010aa0",
      "source_sha256": "9bc0903d01910460298e754c451f027df4324367359800a98ee8e638d94aff55",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3936876-028",
      "text": "Information security infrastructure and controls to mitigate hacking, theft, and fraud must be enhanced when maintaining custody of digital assets, because digital assets have unique technical characteristics.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "defi",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "banks and custodians holding digital assets"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Information security infrastructure and controls to mitigate hacking, theft, and fraud need to be enhanced when maintaining custody of digital assets due to their unique technical characteristics.",
      "text_sha256": "0c8addd8f9185885f97d0084804d6aefdf16da3420d6f58cb53b6a5717290c06",
      "source_sha256": "9bc0903d01910460298e754c451f027df4324367359800a98ee8e638d94aff55",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3936876-030",
      "text": "Every risk in a digital custody operation should carry both a preventative and a detective control, layered so that if some controls fail others remain to reduce the risk.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "defi",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "digital asset custody risk management programs"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Every risk should have a preventative and detective control and there should be appropriate layers of controls so that if some fail, others will still be there to reduce the risk.",
      "text_sha256": "7919c583b3d76ab78066eab4baf8f58e301acf7c17033c41ec94b547a90cda33",
      "source_sha256": "9bc0903d01910460298e754c451f027df4324367359800a98ee8e638d94aff55",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3936876-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3936876-031",
      "text": "Specialized digital custody audit procedures for verifying that a bank maintains access controls over a cryptographic key differ from the audit procedures used for physical assets, so some risk management processes must be tailored for digital custody.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
