    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3962614-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3962614-035",
      "text": "The hybrid smart contracting model is defective because VCs are partially incentivized to fund and stake only the best deals while staking on less optimal deals that the market mostly funds, which undermines their long term reputation accumulation.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation",
        "regulatory-failure",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "models where VCs can stake reputation without proportionate capital commitment"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 74
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3962614-035:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The problem with this model is that VCs are incentivized partially to fund and stake only on the best deals and stake on the less optimal deals that are mostly funded by the market. This undermines their long-term reputation accumulation",
      "text_sha256": "3a8f7f6a937216caaec6a2ff8fdbc042fbc2cde6cf94b86196d699a0fa4a3aab",
      "source_sha256": "c6e202e77fd08db801f932774026458b94e5d103abf30cb1189fe6a1c5edf391",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3962614-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3962614-036",
      "text": "The incentives that undermine long term success of the hybrid model can be mitigated by mandating that staking on deals requires capital commitments, while allowing VCs to lower their capital commitments and increase their staking over time.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "hybrid VC DAO models transitioning away from capital"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3962614-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "It is possible to mitigate these incentives that undermine the long-term success of the system. For example, it is conceivable that staking on deals by VCs mandates capital commitments to the deals but that VCs can over time lower their capital commitments and increase their staking.",
      "text_sha256": "3895665454338484d3956c601f535f9bbd91d7ae7a98549d621ce139591899ba",
      "source_sha256": "c6e202e77fd08db801f932774026458b94e5d103abf30cb1189fe6a1c5edf391",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3962614-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3962614-037",
      "text": "A better system emphasizes reputation by prohibiting capital investment into portfolio companies after an initial minting of reputation in proportion to incoming capital.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "the incentive optimized reputation model with smart contracts"
