    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3981021-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Similar to how centralized institutions rely on the vetting of candidates from other centralized institutions, the CHARITYxDAO may serve as a decentralized oracle for philanthropic endeavors.",
      "text_sha256": "1abac0edc701017b640bfecc00d15d9bc346055f07fab9d46387f4c405fd1a25",
      "source_sha256": "9d8bc78d119c780c96c89ce3e820f4ac8b037d39b3ade59feb4e40d46b048288",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3995709-002",
      "text": "The benefit of a code review is negatively correlated with the size of the code under review: the larger the number of files in a single review, the lower the rate of beneficial feedback from reviewers.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "open-source-and-code"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "single review submissions of increasing size"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Therefore, the benefit of attaining a code review is negatively correlated with the size of the code under review. In particular, the larger the amount of files in a single review, the lower the rate of beneficial feedback from the reviewers.",
      "text_sha256": "84b4d37d5bfcc6d2d6c6ce6a6b06c88a271213a5207f4dcae71eae4293d46c2a",
      "source_sha256": "6d77dbfb15ee86080bfde0b98089180cabafeb6defdf0f05eaaeb3cb99871e89",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3995709-009",
      "text": "Feedback in modern code review is deficient in both timeliness and substance: receiving feedback in a timely manner is developers' number one reported challenge, and the feedback that arrives is often not insightful because reviewers focus on insignificant details rather than larger issues.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "surveyed developer populations in industry code review"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Moreover, even when developers finally receive feedback on their code change, it is often not insightful or helpful. For example, the study also found that some reviewers focus on \"insignificant details rather than larger issues.\"43",
      "text_sha256": "ed64eace5a5f8c9fa1bd3bb2f083c8f59cbf00465c32058c80e78ce288ea2f56",
      "source_sha256": "6d77dbfb15ee86080bfde0b98089180cabafeb6defdf0f05eaaeb3cb99871e89",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3995709-010",
      "text": "Organizational metrics, such as the number of developers working on a component, organizational distance between developers, and organizational code ownership, are better predictors of defect proneness than traditional metrics like churn, complexity, coverage, dependencies, and pre release bug measures.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "open-source-and-code"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "large organization software development"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "including the number of developers working on a component, organizational distance between developers, and organizational code ownership, are \"better predictors of defect-proneness than traditional metrics like churn, complexity, coverage, dependencies, and pre-release bug measures.\"45",
      "text_sha256": "861d49e68d55384932b583b3854d848a56080dc1f3ca5f18a423c630613478c6",
      "source_sha256": "6d77dbfb15ee86080bfde0b98089180cabafeb6defdf0f05eaaeb3cb99871e89",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-011",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3995709-011",
      "text": "Organizational identity and structure affect the time and effectiveness of the code review process, as shown by a statistically significant difference in how quickly Apple accepts its own patches versus Google patches.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "open-source-and-code"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "cross organization patch submission"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-011:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "treats their own patches differently from external patches.\"48 Therefore, organizational identity and structure may have impacts on the time and effectiveness of the code review process.",
      "text_sha256": "9396732e9f122ace3b4e3cde1fc86bdf62d1c3523f76cf06231085ca0c178973",
      "source_sha256": "6d77dbfb15ee86080bfde0b98089180cabafeb6defdf0f05eaaeb3cb99871e89",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3995709-012",
      "text": "The more hierarchical the code review process and the more barriers to entry it imposes, the lower the quality of the resulting code.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "open-source-and-code",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "legacy code review firms with hierarchical reviewer selection"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In other words, the more hierarchical the code review process and the more barriers to entry, the lower the quality of code.",
      "text_sha256": "a4d1e6c6f97489a7ce6b63554c5bc660b7fe0d8827e7b262429c184c97a505e3",
      "source_sha256": "6d77dbfb15ee86080bfde0b98089180cabafeb6defdf0f05eaaeb3cb99871e89",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3995709-013",
      "text": "In hierarchical legacy review processes the first reviewer's output gets the highest priority and follow on reviewers add only minor upgrades, so the collective of reviewers is not incentivized to find flaws and optimize the code as a collective work product.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "legacy code review firms",
        "hierarchical ordering of reviewers"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "often gets the highest priority and is often merely followed with minor upgrades by follow-on reviewers. The collective of reviewers is also not incentivized to find flaws in the code to optimize code as a work product of the collective.",
      "text_sha256": "7486d6d8c2fc13824a1af790c29008a1c74e8eef5a0b381e3754a9a997b8c95b",
      "source_sha256": "6d77dbfb15ee86080bfde0b98089180cabafeb6defdf0f05eaaeb3cb99871e89",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3995709-029",
      "text": "The CRDAO governance model enables a community policing and audit methodology for code reviews, and those governance and policing functions ensure less duplication of code reviews.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "open-source-and-code"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "DAO based governance over a reviewer community"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The CRDAO also uses a community policing and audit methodology for code reviews. This is enabled by the CRDAO governance model. Moreover, the CRDAO governance and policing functions ensure less duplication of code reviews.",
      "text_sha256": "c902dd736b87e07dbc74f6c814b7f9134df3c1d58fea340c88647a6ad9c8009b",
      "source_sha256": "6d77dbfb15ee86080bfde0b98089180cabafeb6defdf0f05eaaeb3cb99871e89",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3995709-030",
      "text": "Crowd review and policing votes by the CRDAO collective filter out idiosyncratic reviewer preferences, because reviewers who submit highly idiosyncratic reviews would have to fear slashing and loss of standing in the community.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "mandatory crowd review of each code review",
        "slashing and reputation stakes in place"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Instead, the CRDAO mandates that reviews are subject to crowd review and policing votes by the CRDAO collective. Accordingly, code reviewers are less likely to engage in highly idiosyncratic reviews as they would need to fear slashing and loss of standing in the community.",
      "text_sha256": "b945e1995250ce25e8e8b9355b6464954b8d7428df1f0ecffeedb4faa5471d69",
      "source_sha256": "6d77dbfb15ee86080bfde0b98089180cabafeb6defdf0f05eaaeb3cb99871e89",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3995709-032",
      "text": "Lower cost early feedback from the CRDAO enables risk taking by development teams that wish to move quickly through governance and upgrade processes, which in turn enables accelerated growth and scaling of experimentation.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "dev teams operating with fast governance and upgrade cycles"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The feedback provided by the CRDAO for the developer community enables risk-taking for dev teams who wish to move quickly through their governance and upgrade process, which in turn enables accelerated growth and scaling of experimentation.",
      "text_sha256": "d5bc0a973fd8b986b2bb3e4fb0cb32a261f5dd9daf8a155ea7e04998cfaed711",
      "source_sha256": "6d77dbfb15ee86080bfde0b98089180cabafeb6defdf0f05eaaeb3cb99871e89",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3995709-036",
      "text": "The CRDAO governance framework is the decentralized governance framework developed by Craig Calcaterra and Wulf Kaal, further enhanced and implemented by the code review DAO, and CRDAO members get paid to participate in that governance.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "CRDAO network governance participation"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 58
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3995709-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The CRDAO follows a decentralized framework of governance that was developed by Craig Calcaterra and Wulf Kaal50",
      "text_sha256": "cd68cba3b846572d42ca2ae7e7ea4ac0c91ebf5d8d3c78ea5e550a1a6afd338c",
      "source_sha256": "6d77dbfb15ee86080bfde0b98089180cabafeb6defdf0f05eaaeb3cb99871e89",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4015908-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4015908-003",
      "text": "The foundation model for token issuance is a core form of centralized top-down governance, and most ICO projects were governed by a small group of individuals rather than by the community at large or a DAO.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "securities-law",
        "governance-design",
        "decentralization",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "ICO era token issuance"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4015908-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The foundation model for token issuance is a core form of centralized top-down governance in the context of token offerings.",
      "text_sha256": "ad4b733761f8a8a82153b393c81c99964620bb2b1fc4c49db9eea4e62edcc030",
      "source_sha256": "e0925afde0c42a16cd5310983789fae3eb3d1f121e2954a72afa64191d00fe37",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4015908-014",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4015908-014",
      "text": "The larger the market capitalization controlled by the DAO, the less likely it becomes that whales and insiders can purchase inexpensive tokens on the market.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "defi",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "DAO governance over project liquidity"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4015908-014:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The larger the market capitalization that is controlled by the DAO, the less likely it becomes that whales and insiders can purchase inexpensive tokens on the market.",
      "text_sha256": "0e2991d93e9da5d2153c0864d143c6b863d700b84c5a7885fdd6261500e6ed0a",
      "source_sha256": "e0925afde0c42a16cd5310983789fae3eb3d1f121e2954a72afa64191d00fe37",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4015908-022",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4015908-022",
      "text": "The more decentralized the governance of a fair launch protocol, the less likely the project will be seen as treating public users unfairly, which makes a decentralized autonomous organization design advisable for fair launch projects.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design",
        "disclosure"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "governance design is transparent and decentralized"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4015908-022:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The more decentralized the governance of a fair launch protocol, the less likely the project will be seen as not treating the public users unfairly. In this context, it may be advisable for fair launch projects to be launched in a decentralized autonomous organization (DAO) design.",
      "text_sha256": "ce969a82c29d4638a10af99d50ab35d08b24adb6e1222e60ed62248bdf9ed6d7",
      "source_sha256": "e0925afde0c42a16cd5310983789fae3eb3d1f121e2954a72afa64191d00fe37",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4015908-023",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4015908-023",
      "text": "If the DAO governing a fair launch is controlled by a handful of people in a foundation setting, decentralized governance metrics are less likely to take hold and the public is correspondingly less likely to benefit from decentralized community governance over the launch.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design",
        "regulatory-failure"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "DAO controlled by a small group in a foundation setting"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4015908-023:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "controlled by a handful of people in a foundation setting, it is less likely that decentralized governance metrics take hold in the DAO. Accordingly, it is less likely that the public can benefit from the decentralized community governance over the fair launch.",
      "text_sha256": "a14cfe00474832399f45d2ad9c46cff099ecdfe0d154abf8f3cfb76e459da0b3",
      "source_sha256": "e0925afde0c42a16cd5310983789fae3eb3d1f121e2954a72afa64191d00fe37",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4015908-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4015908-024",
      "text": "DAO governance built on fungible governance tokens is disfavored and dangerous because governance rights can be bought on open exchanges, whereas non-fungible reputation governance assures the highest levels of decentralization.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "tokenomics",
        "reputation",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "DAO governance rights are tradeable on open exchanges"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 57
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4015908-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "DAO governance that revolves around fungible governance tokens is disfavored and dangerous in this context as governance rights can be bought on open exchanges. By contrast, non-fungible reputation governance of the DAO assures highest levels of decentralization.",
      "text_sha256": "935ba2a9b3c9e2dde0a474095fe94a9282677f0050338e0f61176f7a6df697fe",
      "source_sha256": "e0925afde0c42a16cd5310983789fae3eb3d1f121e2954a72afa64191d00fe37",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4015908-025",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4015908-025",
      "text": "Community DAO governance makes any form of rug pull much less likely, because rug pulls typically benefit only a few select individuals who retained control over the project code or liquidity.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "defi"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "community DAO oversees project code and liquidity"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
