    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The six factors considered are: Decentralization, Work to Earn, Attack Resistance, Regulatory Compliance, Governance, and Organizational Communication. Each DAO was given a score between zero (0) and ten (10) by the analyzing teams",
      "text_sha256": "f1e273932cab4d80ce01434c7971848c1c471b54ff0bf851a914b2b87f4c0de4",
      "source_sha256": "2d71961e8c449afbeaf45ca4f53de8a575d45c77d6960b767d3d1d0874f296b5",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4529715-012",
      "text": "There is no consistent standard for DAO governance, which pushes each DAO to invent its own structure, and because decentralized governance is complex many of those structures fail to become truly decentralized, autonomous, or organized.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "decentralization",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "absence of a governance standard",
        "novelty of decentralized governance"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 58
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "There is no consistent standard for DAO governance. This leads many DAOs to develop their own governance structure. However, because of the complex nature of decentralized governance, many DAO governance structures fail to become truly decentralized, autonomous, or organized.",
      "text_sha256": "f5eb95142bafd1493528f57631bf224f41b6719043f8853e9b2b960ec2863346",
      "source_sha256": "2d71961e8c449afbeaf45ca4f53de8a575d45c77d6960b767d3d1d0874f296b5",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4529715-028",
      "text": "Where a founder retains access to the smart contract behind the governance token, as with 3OH DAO, an internal attack by that founder would be remarkably easy.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "smart-contracts"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "founder has not renounced ownership of the token smart contract"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "If a DAO could have negative attack resistance, 3OH would be the DAO. With the founder having access to the smart contract, an internal attack by the founder would be remarkably easy.",
      "text_sha256": "304e7f9e57ef5a18b146b4cdd2690e9bb70337978af4d07f4ce0067d860a2be1",
      "source_sha256": "2d71961e8c449afbeaf45ca4f53de8a575d45c77d6960b767d3d1d0874f296b5",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4529715-032",
      "text": "A reputation system that rewards voting with the majority, as Bridge Mutual uses, can be manipulated by users who create multiple wallets and always vote with the majority.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation derived solely from voting outcomes"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 71
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "reliance solely on voting outcomes may present some vulnerability, as it could potentially be manipulated by users creating multiple wallets and voting with the majority.",
      "text_sha256": "be499c6c5209948bdb8d857ebf175bd0cf2687b2bfb4df0dc5fb2260fd745a1a",
      "source_sha256": "2d71961e8c449afbeaf45ca4f53de8a575d45c77d6960b767d3d1d0874f296b5",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4529715-033",
      "text": "Locking voted tokens for a period after a vote, as Nexus Mutual does for three days, prevents an attacker from using a flashloan to borrow a large amount of wrapped tokens and swing a vote with significant voting weight.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "token weighted voting with freely traded wrapped token"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This prevents anyone from using a flashloan to borrow a large amount of wNXM and unwrap the wNXM to NXM to sway a vote with a significant voting weight.",
      "text_sha256": "76f014512866416a75454507a18c665df8521193548ebfc03babf60eb93e2408",
      "source_sha256": "2d71961e8c449afbeaf45ca4f53de8a575d45c77d6960b767d3d1d0874f296b5",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4529715-034",
      "text": "Short-term incentives in a decentralized insurance mutual would motivate decision-makers never to pay a claim in order to maximize current profit; incentivizing long-term alignment instead motivates them to pay genuine claims because of the value of the resulting reputation.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "discretionary mutual where members decide claims"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Short-term focus would motivate decision-makers to never pay out any claim to maximize current profit. However, incentivizing long-term alignment motivates decision-makers to pay out genuine claims because of the significant value of the resulting positive reputation.",
      "text_sha256": "03b800a607ff388b2a99d729a282211548750a259b69b8ee4409bd4a42988ceb",
      "source_sha256": "2d71961e8c449afbeaf45ca4f53de8a575d45c77d6960b767d3d1d0874f296b5",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4529715-036",
      "text": "Requiring governance tokens to be earned through contribution rather than purchased, as GDN DAO does, leaves only minimal risk of 51 percent and sock puppet attacks even under a one token one vote structure.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "tokenomics",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "one token one vote with non purchasable tokens"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While the voting structure of the DAO is a 1 token = 1 vote, tokens are not available for purchase. All governance tokens must be earned through contributions to the community.",
      "text_sha256": "53c584497bb191175cdaa4de98d9b51dc19a1ea2036443c94d0fc8963c1a52cc",
      "source_sha256": "2d71961e8c449afbeaf45ca4f53de8a575d45c77d6960b767d3d1d0874f296b5",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4529715-037",
      "text": "A DAO built on reputation rather than a fungible token, as CRDAO is, makes the 51 percent attack nearly impossible and renders sock puppet attacks technically possible but of little influence.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "reputation",
        "governance-design",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation based governance",
        "no fungible governance token"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 69
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "CRDAO is fairly attack resistant because of its use of reputation. As a result, sock puppet attacks are technically possible, but would have little influence. CRDAO does not appear to have a fungible token, so the 51 percent attack is nearly impossible.",
      "text_sha256": "8d302173760edbaf517c8938bb0dbbca7d6184c6c6b09772e5f772885c22a4c7",
      "source_sha256": "2d71961e8c449afbeaf45ca4f53de8a575d45c77d6960b767d3d1d0874f296b5",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4529715-038",
      "text": "Kleros has weak attack resistance because juror selection is proportional to staked fungible tokens; staking reputation rather than tokens to select jurors would remedy this.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "systemic-risk",
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "token staked juror selection"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As such, Kleros has weak attack resistance. This could be changed by utilizing a reputation system to stake rather than tokens in order to select the jurors.",
      "text_sha256": "85578c0a0ede570b330ef4aab1794d989b806f61bf4a788610bc803e84b7f6a2",
      "source_sha256": "2d71961e8c449afbeaf45ca4f53de8a575d45c77d6960b767d3d1d0874f296b5",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4529715-039",
      "text": "Big Green DAO's committee unanimity and closed membership make attacks unlikely, but these same protections come at the expense of the decentralized organization the founders were trying to create.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "decentralization",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "vetted membership and unanimous committee approval"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4529715-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, these principles really limit what a DAO is supposed to be so in a way it is secure, but also at the expense of the organization they were trying to create.",
      "text_sha256": "43089b594e62776e0e72ba309687170a2d242f9663b87b9ac8bed8af1b849c89",
      "source_sha256": "2d71961e8c449afbeaf45ca4f53de8a575d45c77d6960b767d3d1d0874f296b5",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4685567-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4685567-003",
      "text": "Impact 1.0 foundations developed plutocratic power structures because their leaders and trustees were never democratically elected, and Impact 3.0 addresses this by adding WEB3 collaborative democratic measures on top of the existing foundation structures.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "private foundation governance",
        "Impact 3.0 still relies on foundation structures"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4685567-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "further improve Impact 1.0 private foundations by adding collaborative WEB3 democratic measures that address plutocratic power structures in Impact 1.0 foundations that originated in the lack of democratic elections of Impact 1.0 foundations' organizations' leaders or trustees.",
      "text_sha256": "c3ef3e1f76d0b378525855d44b468b5b88f8c1153f9cd4802daa4b6ec1fa2437",
      "source_sha256": "87fb1be89d2661967ed2b0b673fe26448ded3bc3119b122177a4fc13ae5c085c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4685567-004",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4685567-004",
      "text": "Because Impact 1.0 entrusted individual donors rather than donor collectives with identifying which problems to solve, individual philanthropists can reshape underfunded causes according to their own ideals without meaningful checks and balances or crowd wisdom.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Impact 1.0 and 2.0 philanthropic strategies",
        "high net worth individual and corporate donors"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4685567-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Individual philanthropists can leverage underfunded causes and reshape them according to their ideals without significant checks and balances or crowd wisdom considerations.",
      "text_sha256": "29910e9ae0b1a09f5fa2228c820b958589e5750fad34cac1d702cd9f5c855f99",
      "source_sha256": "87fb1be89d2661967ed2b0b673fe26448ded3bc3119b122177a4fc13ae5c085c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4685567-020",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4685567-020",
      "text": "The two stage vote is the mechanism that produces consensus: a non binding test vote reveals how every donor assesses a project, after which donors can change their minds in the formal vote where their reputation tokens are at stake, and in practice decisions are made with unanimity.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "reputation",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation tokens are staked in the formal vote",
        "the chosen WEB3 decentralized governance design"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 56
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4685567-020:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Once every donor sees how all other donors assess the given project, they can jointly change their minds during the \"formal vote\" in which their respective reputation tokens are at stake. Typically, in this form of decentralized governance, all decisions are made with unanimity.",
      "text_sha256": "ba6928186653139e002c712e0694150f17c8245d269d94833cf38124b3f14ef7",
      "source_sha256": "87fb1be89d2661967ed2b0b673fe26448ded3bc3119b122177a4fc13ae5c085c",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4685567-021",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4685567-021",
      "text": "Retroactive public goods funding via results oracles in DAO format fails at the governance layer: even where the core resource distribution concept works, the project remains exposed to decentralized governance attack vectors because the governance design lacks attack resistance.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design",
        "dao",
        "smart-contracts"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "results oracle operating as a DAO",
        "retroactive public goods funding designs"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
