      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 56
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Alas, hackers often sell the bug or exploit them when they discover them.",
      "text_sha256": "a180a8094116e697de126f06e56b0f540e553d60380e7bb70497429fdce298eb",
      "source_sha256": "60eadf91c0913468505afc664c8d8d1e1673d6c5326d031ca7060addb8ab2eda",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-021",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4734750-021",
      "text": "The Code Review DAO drives review prices down by running a decentralized, community driven review process built on a bidding process, combined with open access for any qualified reviewer rather than membership in a few firms.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "economics",
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-021:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "which facilitates a decentralized community-driven code review process that utilizes a bidding process on code reviews to drive prices down",
      "text_sha256": "bb653432617eee615cb900ec0b2efeae08b89878c1f01cb6f85f4b9bd4fd83b9",
      "source_sha256": "60eadf91c0913468505afc664c8d8d1e1673d6c5326d031ca7060addb8ab2eda",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4734750-024",
      "text": "Subjecting every review to crowd review and policing votes makes reviewers less likely to produce idiosyncratic reviews, because they would face slashing and loss of standing in the community.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reviewers holding stakeable reputation within the DAO"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Accordingly, code reviewers are less likely to engage in highly idiosyncratic reviews as they would need to fear slashing and loss of standing in the community.",
      "text_sha256": "b2896ec2e65bd73ce931d096a8f260c51332513e5f3aced6a300dee023569057",
      "source_sha256": "60eadf91c0913468505afc664c8d8d1e1673d6c5326d031ca7060addb8ab2eda",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4734750-028",
      "text": "Fast community feedback enables development teams to take risks and move quickly through their governance and upgrade processes, which in turn accelerates growth and the scaling of experimentation.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design",
        "open-source-and-code"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "enables risk-taking for dev teams who wish to move quickly through their governance and upgrade process, which in turn enables accelerated growth and scaling of experimentation.",
      "text_sha256": "a010d561fd99054fb81f88611a50ff1814c09029f560bdf7623ecb7b0c7e162a",
      "source_sha256": "60eadf91c0913468505afc664c8d8d1e1673d6c5326d031ca7060addb8ab2eda",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4734750-029",
      "text": "The community audit should proceed in two stages: an informal vote that reveals collective wisdom to all members, followed by a formal vote in which staked reputation tokens are at risk, and this sequence gives job posters significant quality assurances.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "reputation",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Once the entire community knows how each member feels about the code review examined, the CRDAO now votes in a formal vote in which the reputation tokens staked are at risk.",
      "text_sha256": "1b8ad8658884601b6a1e5312d9c6deb5c8733d62ec3a027a55c17fcca02964df",
      "source_sha256": "60eadf91c0913468505afc664c8d8d1e1673d6c5326d031ca7060addb8ab2eda",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4734750-036",
      "text": "A reliable reputation score substitutes for redundant labor: if a high reputation worker completes a task, required duplication can fall from fifteen workers to five or fewer, which is what allows micro task work to scale.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized platforms with portable, wallet linked reputation scores"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 44
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "If a reliable and high reputation score worker completes the tasks, the duplication may be brought from 15 to 5 or less in the decentralized CRDAO setup. This enables unprecedented scaling of micro task work.",
      "text_sha256": "80805bd622808c575a5e7cf10182e62bd18e118f84665451d3444548ec369496",
      "source_sha256": "60eadf91c0913468505afc664c8d8d1e1673d6c5326d031ca7060addb8ab2eda",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4734750-037",
      "text": "Two sided reputation scores discipline both sides of the micro task market: workers become less likely to accept offers from low reputation requesters, and low reputation workers are less likely to be retained.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "If requesters have a lower reputation score, workers become less likely to accept requesters",
      "text_sha256": "d9ca42a11c002878c62387533059f6ec8ec4e92adf1725661f6a1970cee65377",
      "source_sha256": "60eadf91c0913468505afc664c8d8d1e1673d6c5326d031ca7060addb8ab2eda",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-040",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4734750-040",
      "text": "Reputation token staking substitutes for identity verification: because staking makes the network attack resistant, workers can complete micro tasks without verifying identity, which removes the cost, delay, and privacy surrender of centralized approval and enlarges the available labor pool.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 72
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4734750-040:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The CRDAO architecture, and specifically its reputation token staking mechanism, make the CRDAO attack resistant.",
      "text_sha256": "bcdd89c762b465c33ca6ea7e3d9d1faca8e9edd3c877bd8df2d9fb09cccdfb0d",
      "source_sha256": "60eadf91c0913468505afc664c8d8d1e1673d6c5326d031ca7060addb8ab2eda",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4755632-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4755632-016",
      "text": "Gamification supplies quality control by making workers review and rate each other's contributions for points or recognition, which surfaces and resolves discrepancies through consensus-based voting or peer review rather than through duplicated independent work.",
