    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4796714-004",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4796714-004",
      "text": "Ex-post governance, which applies regulation only after AI systems are developed and deployed or after large language models have been pretrained on existing proprietary datasets, fails to address risks and biases preemptively.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to regulation imposed after model development or pretraining",
        "concerns risk and bias formation during development"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4796714-004:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The traditional ex-post governance methods, where regulations are applied after AI systems are developed and deployed, or were pretrained LLMs models were trained on existing proprietary datasets, often fall short in preemptively addressing risks and biases.",
      "text_sha256": "84ecf1ee87210f6fc6b112f8a0fc89189045dd4fdbb3aa735bd26a4d9472dc97",
      "source_sha256": "59fa63bae179e8f9b6b8efbdf90cee28400276512a1b04f9f579a48641305c93",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4796714-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4796714-013",
      "text": "Blockchain can only deliver decentralized AI governance if the blockchain trilemma is first overcome, since decentralization, security, and scalability cannot readily be achieved simultaneously within one network.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to blockchain networks used as governance infrastructure",
        "necessary condition, not sufficient"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 60
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4796714-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The effectiveness of blockchain in achieving the goal of decentralized AI governance is contingent upon overcoming the fundamental blockchain trilemma: the challenge of balancing decentralization, security, and scalability.",
      "text_sha256": "b0d2fd8fefa95a6492bcec46ad8b36294b93ec701bd6140aea4dd124a9d52094",
      "source_sha256": "59fa63bae179e8f9b6b8efbdf90cee28400276512a1b04f9f579a48641305c93",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4796714-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4796714-015",
      "text": "When decentralization at the Layer 1 level is compromised, the autonomy of the smart contracts deployed on that chain is compromised by affiliation, so smart contracts are corruptible in the current design and cannot reliably serve as neutral instruments of ethical AI governance.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "smart-contracts",
        "decentralization",
        "compliance",
        "governance-design",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies where a few dominant parties influence the underlying Layer 1",
        "holds under current blockchain design as of 2024"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4796714-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "When the decentralization of Layer 1 blockchains is compromised, the autonomy of smart contracts is inherently jeopardized, undermining their effectiveness as tools for ethical AI governance.",
      "text_sha256": "c05cc329d81e3939b314c2580a42d5ed075b350bfd54359214ece19849af9702",
      "source_sha256": "59fa63bae179e8f9b6b8efbdf90cee28400276512a1b04f9f579a48641305c93",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4796714-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4796714-016",
      "text": "Decentralized governance structures impose their own costs: with no central authority to coordinate diverse stakeholders, consensus is difficult to reach, negotiations are prolonged, and enforcement of agreements is weak because no single entity is responsible for compliance.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "institutional-design",
        "compliance",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "applies to decentralized structures without a coordinating authority",
        "evidenced in the paper by the environmental agreement domain"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 50
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4796714-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In decentralized systems, the lack of a central authority often leads to difficulties in coordinating and achieving consensus among diverse stakeholders, each with their own priorities and objectives. This can result in prolonged negotiations or weak enforcement of agreements",
      "text_sha256": "fb0e1c46bcc6ae68f077ababece3b5cef53fa854ed70b154a4f5ee334e2228b1",
      "source_sha256": "59fa63bae179e8f9b6b8efbdf90cee28400276512a1b04f9f579a48641305c93",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4796714-021",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4796714-021",
      "text": "Until the known attack vectors on decentralized autonomous organizations are solved, DAO based AI governance solutions remain suboptimal; these include Sybil attacks, tyranny of the majority, Arrow's impossibility theorem, sockpuppet attacks, and tragedy of the commons.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "describes DAOs as set up and governed in the majority of cases in 2024",
        "conditional on the attack vectors remaining unsolved"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 71
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4796714-021:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Without solving these attack vectors, DAO related AI governance solutions remain suboptimal.",
      "text_sha256": "9cc5c77e19d0bc01a46731963fec7293340a4f29dc0e788ca872c79af6dd6a26",
      "source_sha256": "59fa63bae179e8f9b6b8efbdf90cee28400276512a1b04f9f579a48641305c93",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4796714-022",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4796714-022",
      "text": "AI powered DAOs that autonomously generate revenue are especially hard to regulate or dismantle, because the same blockchain security features that protect the organization also make it difficult to intervene once it is operational.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
