      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 59
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4855607-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "with validation pools that are smart contract coordinated to dispense rewards pro rata to the reputation scores a node may have accumulated through productive work. This mechanism ensures that nodes are incentivized based on their actual input to the AI model's learning.",
      "text_sha256": "fc602a73b15e5b4e5d6527b94758718d9bc759609b56a246ae923bbe14b70d48",
      "source_sha256": "eb0b3e62374b45a8fa888c6bde9725e606bcb46cf4b5e74a6e851d9f25099113",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4855607-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4855607-032",
      "text": "GNNs and web3 systems optimize each other through mutual feedback effects, and it is this bidirectional learning, rather than one system merely serving the other, that produces an evolutionary dynamic optimization process.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "GNNs deployed inside the web3 systems they analyze"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4855607-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The integration and optimization of AI models such as GNNs and web3 systems happens in feedback effects between the two systems. Through these feedback effects both systems learn constantly from and with each other which results in an evolutionary dynamic optimization process.",
      "text_sha256": "e6de58abf3fcae7778939e5078eb5e0e03a204dd2f41357360090c39e670d8a1",
      "source_sha256": "eb0b3e62374b45a8fa888c6bde9725e606bcb46cf4b5e74a6e851d9f25099113",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4855607-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4855607-033",
      "text": "The RLHF process is exposed to failure because participants may hold potentially adversarial and misaligned interests, so the vulnerability lies in the incentive structure of feedback provision rather than in the learning algorithm.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "RLHF systems where feedback providers have divergent stakes"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 53
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4855607-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Currently, the RLHF process, which involves training AI models based on human preferences and feedback, can face challenges due to the potentially adversarial and misaligned interests of participants.",
      "text_sha256": "8d740de31a4f6d8b0a5c27e84c02967c1e913134a82f8f5e5aa06630411cfc50",
      "source_sha256": "eb0b3e62374b45a8fa888c6bde9725e606bcb46cf4b5e74a6e851d9f25099113",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4855607-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4855607-034",
      "text": "Distributing governance across all participants prevents any single entity from dominating decision making, and because model or training changes then require consensus, the resulting decisions reflect collective rather than individual interest.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "regulatory-failure",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "governance systems where change requires consensus among distributed participants"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 56
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4855607-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "By distributing governance across all participants, the proposed web3 community governance system ensures that no single entity can dominate the decision-making process. This structure promotes the alignment of incentives since changes to the model or the training process require consensus",
      "text_sha256": "a76a87920a4024d907c07eb66a54c20c8fe8aa91f0178479b83b3d5d493bab44",
      "source_sha256": "eb0b3e62374b45a8fa888c6bde9725e606bcb46cf4b5e74a6e851d9f25099113",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4855607-035",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4855607-035",
      "text": "Applying decentralized voting and consensus to RLHF permits human feedback to be verified before it is used to calibrate the Reward Model, which raises the integrity and reliability of the feedback data entering the model.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "RLHF pipelines where feedback can be verified prior to reward model training"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 48
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4855607-035:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Applying these mechanisms to RLHF allows for the decentralized verification of human feedback before it's used to calibrate the RM, enhancing the integrity and reliability of the feedback data.",
      "text_sha256": "8a3e623ef2586ac88acdd9c5abe9c5d05ab90770055c2c1b2de9d60a521ca6c8",
      "source_sha256": "eb0b3e62374b45a8fa888c6bde9725e606bcb46cf4b5e74a6e851d9f25099113",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4855607-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4855607-037",
      "text": "Issuing non fungible reputation tokens that represent voting power, access rights, or entitlement to a share of the project's success creates an economic structure in which participants are directly invested in the success of the RLHF process.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "RLHF communities where retention and sustained participation matter"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4855607-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The web3 system as proposed herein can issue non-fungible reputation tokens that represent voting power, access rights, or entitlement to a share of the project's success. This creates an economic structure where participants are directly invested in the success of the RLHF process",
