      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4900878-022:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "By carefully designing these incentives, token economies can balance supply and demand, ensuring stable and sustainable growth.",
      "text_sha256": "de11c19078232f4e2dc8bfd9afbdcd9efb2b22a52cd0dc2aeccf09521a77e8d7",
      "source_sha256": "75bf96d3b751b4ad0a6ca4a32591cf026094f113e3a372aa6c61790941b391f7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4900878-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4900878-024",
      "text": "Because quantum economics models probabilities rather than certainties, it is better suited than deterministic models to capturing cryptocurrency price dynamics, and probabilistic models let economists better anticipate price movements and market behavior in decentralized markets.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "economics",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized and volatile cryptocurrency markets"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4900878-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, quantum economics, with its focus on probabilities rather than certainties, offers a framework that is more suited to capturing these dynamics.",
      "text_sha256": "a3ef71451bfb84f2cffc2cd3cecde5189e1e943dac4a0c0d7c0feeea2c6fa96f",
      "source_sha256": "75bf96d3b751b4ad0a6ca4a32591cf026094f113e3a372aa6c61790941b391f7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4900878-025",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4900878-025",
      "text": "Decentralized blockchain networks display an economic analogue of entanglement: a single participant's action, such as a large transaction, immediately propagates into token prices, network congestion, and the behavior of other participants.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design",
        "blockchain",
        "systemic-risk",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized blockchain networks"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4900878-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "For example, a large transaction by a single user can influence token prices, network congestion, and even the behavior of other participants.",
      "text_sha256": "d7df830242b7c12cfc0707e95a188acfb4c0616c28ca6d0d533eca5d85f74bf6",
      "source_sha256": "75bf96d3b751b4ad0a6ca4a32591cf026094f113e3a372aa6c61790941b391f7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4900878-026",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4900878-026",
      "text": "Tokens solve the quantification problem in quantum economics by serving as measurable units of value and governance: token denominated voting power in a DAO makes social influence and decision making power countable, supplying the consistent set of units the framework lacked.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "dao",
        "governance-design",
        "research-methods"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "token based systems with on chain governance such as DAOs"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4900878-026:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Tokenomics offers a practical solution through the use of tokens as quantifiable units of value and governance.",
      "text_sha256": "e966a12865cb32208cafaa4e1a1f232121260bcb7806b1466dea991c919b34d1",
      "source_sha256": "75bf96d3b751b4ad0a6ca4a32591cf026094f113e3a372aa6c61790941b391f7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4900878-027",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4900878-027",
      "text": "Decentralized governance models such as DAOs answer the criticism that micro level quantum properties do not scale to the macro level, because DAOs demonstrate participatory governance structures that operate effectively in large, complex economies.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "large scale decentralized economies with DAO governance"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4900878-027:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Additionally, the use of decentralized governance models in tokenomics, such as DAOs, can address the criticism that quantum properties observed at the micro level do not scale up to the macro level.",
      "text_sha256": "8b529b5e684b2a2d5da7322e19f0b5bf71db809869fb7b7f324a93ca991a02ed",
      "source_sha256": "75bf96d3b751b4ad0a6ca4a32591cf026094f113e3a372aa6c61790941b391f7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4900878-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4900878-031",
      "text": "In blockchain transactions the signing function, performed by wallets holding cryptographic keys, is separate from execution, which occurs inside the smart contract, so tokens are never physically held in the same locality as the keys and the smart contract acts as the intermediary executing predefined rules.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "smart-contracts",
        "defi"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "smart contract based blockchain transactions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4900878-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This separation ensures that the tokens themselves are not physically held in the same locality as the keys.",
      "text_sha256": "d0aac91d894a74f44bf1498ff71ab1bf53a02a3c65cf45ee181556e504078771",
      "source_sha256": "75bf96d3b751b4ad0a6ca4a32591cf026094f113e3a372aa6c61790941b391f7",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4900878-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4900878-034",
      "text": "Quantum computing cuts both ways for blockchain: it can raise the efficiency and security of blockchain networks, but safeguarding those systems against the threats it also creates depends on research into quantum resistant cryptographic algorithms.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "as quantum computing capability advances"
