      "relevance_score": 59
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This opacity can obstruct the debugging process, obscure bias detection and mitigation, and hinder comprehension of AI decision-making.",
      "text_sha256": "dbe5fec10920af00e1ff02eeb77e415c81d94186faa0b8d905ade79aa182edaf",
      "source_sha256": "ab66c1e99a88da1fa36b0c6b536df5184231fe6aa427f3dd53287a4e0ac79853",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4941807-012",
      "text": "Federated learning does not eliminate privacy risk, because although the data stays decentralized the protocol still exchanges model parameters, and those parameters can expose sensitive information if intercepted or improperly handled.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "decentralization",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "in federated learning deployments that exchange model parameters",
        "where parameters can be intercepted or mishandled"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 67
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "These challenges arise because, while FL keeps data decentralized, it still involves the exchange of model parameters, which could potentially expose sensitive information if intercepted or improperly handled.",
      "text_sha256": "1b9a51b9ccc3f77decf465ff3c98171d1d4c7fc0e6bf327ad319fb8a929afe9a",
      "source_sha256": "ab66c1e99a88da1fa36b0c6b536df5184231fe6aa427f3dd53287a4e0ac79853",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4941807-017",
      "text": "As AI systems come to depend on vast data, personal information is converted from a resource the individual could control and deploy at discretion into a fundamental operational input for AI systems, which increases the potential for misuse and makes it harder for individuals to manage how their data is used.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where AI operation requires large volumes of personal data"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 64
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As AI technologies evolve, they rely heavily on vast amounts of data, transforming personal information from a resource that individuals could control and use at their discretion into a fundamental operational tool for AI systems.",
      "text_sha256": "5a5f5e78d25afae3591907ceff0fd16e464e2dc8118fe45362b506a1441f3725",
      "source_sha256": "ab66c1e99a88da1fa36b0c6b536df5184231fe6aa427f3dd53287a4e0ac79853",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4941807-019",
      "text": "Smart contracts can automate compliance with regulatory requirements and ethical guidelines: for example, a smart contract can enforce privacy law directly by controlling an AI system's access to personal data according to predefined rules.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "smart-contracts",
        "compliance",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "blockchain",
        "governance-design",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where compliance rules can be expressed as predefined, codified conditions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 67
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "They can be used to automate compliance with regulatory requirements and ethical guidelines. For instance, smart contracts can automatically enforce privacy laws by controlling AI's access to personal data based on predefined rules.",
      "text_sha256": "843bda6ae982cef70547d0afb48d52b73ab382e60fe4c6eb9969b7c9c522a388",
      "source_sha256": "ab66c1e99a88da1fa36b0c6b536df5184231fe6aa427f3dd53287a4e0ac79853",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-021",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4941807-021",
      "text": "In the federated model of AI governance many challenges cannot easily be decentralized, because distinct entities maintain their own AI systems and datasets, producing variation in standards, protocols, and formats that obstructs a unified governance framework.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where separate organizations maintain independent AI systems and datasets"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-021:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In the federated model of AI governance, many challenges cannot be easily decentralized. For example, different entities or organizations maintain their own AI systems and datasets. This can lead to variations in standards, protocols, and formats used",
      "text_sha256": "6bf15153a6ad763fbb363bb5cb050230f3c65b7f71719c7b8c4848b6c6d34dae",
      "source_sha256": "ab66c1e99a88da1fa36b0c6b536df5184231fe6aa427f3dd53287a4e0ac79853",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-022",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4941807-022",
      "text": "When decision making power is distributed across multiple entities in a federated model, consensus and cooperation become harder to reach, which makes cohesive AI governance mechanisms difficult to establish.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "institutional-design",
        "decentralization",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where governance authority is distributed across multiple independent entities"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 70
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-022:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In a federated model, where decision-making power is distributed across multiple entities, it becomes harder to achieve consensus and cooperation, making it challenging to establish cohesive AI governance mechanisms.",
      "text_sha256": "e9949bb35bd398818ef9f04919f83f9e38d1ec72d630f03510399fd5786b94a1",
      "source_sha256": "ab66c1e99a88da1fa36b0c6b536df5184231fe6aa427f3dd53287a4e0ac79853",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-025",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4941807-025",
      "text": "Kaal proposes that a more decentralized Web3 model of AI governance can address the failures of the federated model by distributing governance more equitably across network participants, so that no single entity dominates decision making.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where governance rights are distributed across network participants"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "A more decentralized web3 model of AI governance as proposed here could ostensibly address these challenges in a federated AI governance model by distributing governance more equitably across network participants.",
      "text_sha256": "81f64357494b277d0a8b20d6b4e90424316d231024aeb5ac576cc493b4ea36c3",
      "source_sha256": "ab66c1e99a88da1fa36b0c6b536df5184231fe6aa427f3dd53287a4e0ac79853",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4941807-028",
      "text": "Kaal's proposed answer to the decentralized governance needs of AI is to implement Decentralized Autonomous Organizations that govern AI through expert community consensus.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where an expert community can be assembled and its consensus recorded on chain"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 75
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "One promising way to address the decentralized governance needs of AI pertains to the implementation of Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (DAOs) for the governance of AI through expert community consensus.",
      "text_sha256": "d0843df7b67bb76957f30961da96230b4d7a06c6ff6eda30d2b3d0015154bce0",
      "source_sha256": "ab66c1e99a88da1fa36b0c6b536df5184231fe6aa427f3dd53287a4e0ac79853",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4941807-030",
      "text": "Validation Pools are the consensus mechanism of the proposed system: an author's stakes are pooled to evaluate a specific forum post, and the outcome of the pool can mint new reputation tokens that reflect community consensus on that contribution.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where participants stake against specific forum posts"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 60
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Validation Pool (VP) form a crucial mechanism where an author's stakes are pooled to evaluate specific posts within the forum. The outcome of a VP can lead to the minting of new REP tokens, reflecting the consensus on a given issue or contribution.",
      "text_sha256": "e08976fdab6bbc47247006a5c9a767bb7a7a79801f79cd2a5d086ee2d8820cfd",
      "source_sha256": "ab66c1e99a88da1fa36b0c6b536df5184231fe6aa427f3dd53287a4e0ac79853",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4941807-033",
      "text": "Under the proposed model the input parameters and learning data of AI systems are themselves governed by expert community consensus, through submission of proposals to the Forum and review by Validation Pool, so that only vetted and consensus backed data and parameters enter AI development.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "education-and-practice",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "dao"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where training data and parameters are submitted as forum proposals subject to validation pool review"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 69
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4941807-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "the input parameters and learning data for AI systems can be governed through expert community consensus. This process involves submitting proposals to the Forum and undergoing Validation Pool review,",
      "text_sha256": "8a9e731a007d6815ab136ad59cf6a347f9cbc6af55ef2c7d38469dbdd38e7e95",
      "source_sha256": "ab66c1e99a88da1fa36b0c6b536df5184231fe6aa427f3dd53287a4e0ac79853",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-005",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4957318-005",
      "text": "Inconsistent application of a proliferating body of law by different judges and regulatory bodies produces unpredictable legal outcomes, which increases litigation as parties seek judicial clarification and in turn undermines public confidence in the legal system.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where statutes and regulations multiply faster than interpretive doctrine consolidates"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-005:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Inconsistencies in the application of laws by different judges or regulatory bodies can result in unpredictable legal outcomes, thereby increasing litigation as parties seek judicial clarification. This inconsistency further undermines public confidence in the legal",
      "text_sha256": "c2790a3f3c1d2fdc4bcdb96438994a8f3a88f9460871f6dce57c36c3f172c23d",
      "source_sha256": "137fb77eb82111a85f0ab5581926f762a7414ae84aaf3d56e8299db670e0e0c1",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-006",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4957318-006",
      "text": "As law becomes more detailed and specialized it becomes less accessible to the general public, which complicates citizens' ability to understand the rules governing them and discourages engagement and participation in democratic processes.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "disclosure",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where legal complexity outpaces lay comprehension"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-006:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "less accessible to the general public, complicating citizens' ability to understand and engage with the rules that govern their lives. This lack of accessibility and transparency can discourage public engagement and participation in democratic processes",
      "text_sha256": "b86bcb463cc88cfc1fe2b47fe3e44d00f6490c38ce934f7dc752f5d7afb81654",
      "source_sha256": "137fb77eb82111a85f0ab5581926f762a7414ae84aaf3d56e8299db670e0e0c1",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-007",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4957318-007",
      "text": "Web2 platform architecture is a causal contributor to distrust in legal institutions: centralized models driven by engagement metrics prioritize sensationalism over nuanced discourse, which accelerates misinformation and echo chambers and magnifies public distrust.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "centralized, engagement optimized social media platforms",
        "where citizens use social media as a substitute for formal legal channels"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 53
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-007:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This design incentivizes the rapid spread of both information and misinformation, often amplifying extreme viewpoints and fostering echo chambers. As a result, these platforms can magnify public distrust in legal institutions",
      "text_sha256": "1c2ab761af09fb86891df3eacac14fd151e7b18f481079990c0c4e703a5b7d55",
      "source_sha256": "137fb77eb82111a85f0ab5581926f762a7414ae84aaf3d56e8299db670e0e0c1",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-011",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4957318-011",
      "text": "Sunset provisions likely increase rents extracted by interest groups and entrench current majoritarian preferences, and they can create planning problems for both public and private actors.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "politically salient statutes subject to periodic renewal"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-011:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "rather than genuine policy improvement. Sunset provisions also likely increase rents from interest groups, entrench current majoritarian preferences, which can at times produce planning conundrums for public and private actors.",
      "text_sha256": "c5662daaff778cc23a504f6cb9cc7b76669e0c78d2d23948d853e8eddbc4e749",
      "source_sha256": "137fb77eb82111a85f0ab5581926f762a7414ae84aaf3d56e8299db670e0e0c1",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4957318-016",
      "text": "Sunset provisions in tax law do not deliver fiscal restraint, because shifting baselines, exceptions to budget rules, and the difficulty of accurately costing temporary legislation undermine their theoretical benefits.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "tax legislation subject to budget scoring rules"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Complexities such as shifting baselines, exceptions to budget rules, and the challenges of accurately assessing the costs of temporary legislation undermine the theoretical benefits of sunset provisions in promoting fiscal restraint.",
      "text_sha256": "b07bdf45a949a2224ab5f1d5a4ec9aac44d8a0ea4e37cafed71d14c56a29f96b",
      "source_sha256": "137fb77eb82111a85f0ab5581926f762a7414ae84aaf3d56e8299db670e0e0c1",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4957318-029",
      "text": "Web3 systems answer the web2 pathology at the architectural level rather than the content level: decentralized, transparent, community governed designs eliminate the centralized control that drives misinformation and echo chambers, and substitute transparency, decentralization, and user control.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "reputation",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "decentralized and community governed platform architectures"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Unlike Web2 platforms, Web3 systems aim to eliminate the centralized control that exacerbates the spread of misinformation and the creation of echo chambers. Instead, they prioritize transparency, decentralization, and user control,",
      "text_sha256": "5dc41c1e55ee355ce01769941e78f2b1f16f6bc8e764bac42874f66c869ef85d",
      "source_sha256": "137fb77eb82111a85f0ab5581926f762a7414ae84aaf3d56e8299db670e0e0c1",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4957318-030",
      "text": "The proposed system stipulates a forum as an on chain collection of uniquely identified posts that may cite prior contributions, and this citation structure is what constitutes the Weighted Directed Acyclic Graph.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "on chain forums where posts and citations are recorded immutably"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The web3 community as proposed herein operates a forum as an on-chain collection of posts, each uniquely identified and possibly citing previous contributions. This forum forms a Weighted Directed Acyclic Graph (WDAG), facilitating organized discussion and citation among participants.",
      "text_sha256": "5f57316c38bead962b3246394241ae26904a330a3985002bffe52351b17eec56",
      "source_sha256": "137fb77eb82111a85f0ab5581926f762a7414ae84aaf3d56e8299db670e0e0c1",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4957318-031",
      "text": "Validation pools are the consensus mechanism of the proposed system: author stakes are pooled to evaluate specific forum posts, and the outcome can mint new reputation tokens that record the community's consensus on a contribution.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where participants stake reputation on the evaluation of specific posts"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 61
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Validation Pool (VP) form a crucial mechanism where author stakes are pooled to evaluate specific posts within the forum. The outcome of a VP can lead to the minting of new REP tokens, reflecting the consensus on a given issue or contribution.",
      "text_sha256": "67a76f7386c40989c05582005a8eacff17998e1c026c36ea42a9fa95cd1dd25f",
      "source_sha256": "137fb77eb82111a85f0ab5581926f762a7414ae84aaf3d56e8299db670e0e0c1",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4957318-033",
      "text": "In the WDAG system a legal precedent or rule that gains favor because it is effective automatically receives a higher weight, and that weight is set by user preferences and citations rather than by any legislative act.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where citation and user preference data are recorded on chain",
        "where effectiveness is revealed through use"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In the WDAG system, when a new legal precedent or rule gains favor due to its effectiveness, it automatically receives a higher weight in the system based on user preferences and citations.",
      "text_sha256": "6a927915ace2b2ea7006fd1714f7ef5883f7535fb3fd0421c400a5cabe9b59f1",
      "source_sha256": "137fb77eb82111a85f0ab5581926f762a7414ae84aaf3d56e8299db670e0e0c1",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/4957318-038",
      "text": "Political resistance to repeal dissolves under the WDAG model because a rule that loses substantial backing simply diminishes in relevance through the citation mechanism, with no external legislative act of repeal to contest.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "law-and-legal-systems"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "where support and opposition are expressed through citation behavior"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:4957318-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "dynamically reflecting evolving support or opposition to legal precedents through a citation mechanism. If a legal rule loses substantial backing, its relevance diminishes organically within the WDAG framework, without the need for external legislative intervention.",
      "text_sha256": "eba6d6e1f951e87553fb197eda5bfe3dd7051e2fbaaca36ba125396e942f0c20",
      "source_sha256": "137fb77eb82111a85f0ab5581926f762a7414ae84aaf3d56e8299db670e0e0c1",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5095633-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5095633-012",
      "text": "The governance protocols required for GDPR and AI Act compliance, including anonymization, data minimization, and explicit consent, themselves complicate the assembly of robust AI training datasets.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "compliance",
        "governance-design",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "jurisdictions with GDPR-style data protection mandates"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 59
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5095633-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "which may include anonymization, data minimization, and explicit consent where applicable. These measures can, however, complicate the collection and curation of robust datasets for AI training.",
      "text_sha256": "069b81c4fcf538404ad7da7fc098f95824d49de5b313bd57dba411251e08e526",
      "source_sha256": "cbb484711f89bcefc9fc6a5730a1ed0a3f764d7999ad9b6f7d8ea05634c26c63",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5095633-022",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5095633-022",
      "text": "Centralizing annotation data inside a small number of vendor firms creates a standing risk of breach or misuse that can produce legal liability and loss of trust in AI technologies.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "data aggregated and held by centralized annotation vendors"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 58
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5095633-022:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As data is centralized in these companies, there's always a risk of data breaches or misuse, which could lead to legal issues or loss of trust in AI technologies.",
      "text_sha256": "fd66d14e5ffc65d4de98fa21ad8a9a513b9aa9446e2accf0ea6d1895e694f117",
      "source_sha256": "cbb484711f89bcefc9fc6a5730a1ed0a3f764d7999ad9b6f7d8ea05634c26c63",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5095633-025",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5095633-025",
      "text": "Transparent DAO governance lets platforms compensate contributors according to demonstrated expertise and reputation, which mitigates the exploitative labor practices associated with centralized annotation services.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "governance is genuinely transparent and reputation is verifiable"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 63
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5095633-025:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "By implementing transparent governance mechanisms\u2014often in the form of Decentralized Autonomous Organizations (\"DAOs\")\u2014these ventures can equitably compensate data contributors based on demonstrated expertise and reputation, thus mitigating exploitative labor practices",
      "text_sha256": "99a4dad2cf3c6a887ede237557e5bc6c0c311174771f240b017319a54acfbd42",
      "source_sha256": "cbb484711f89bcefc9fc6a5730a1ed0a3f764d7999ad9b6f7d8ea05634c26c63",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5095633-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5095633-031",
      "text": "The reputation systems of SingularityNET, Fetch.ai, Ocean Protocol, Numeraire, and DcentAI are structurally insufficient for a fully decentralized Mechanical Turk model of large-scale AI dataset creation, offering only incremental innovation.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "decentralization",
        "governance-design",
        "empirical-evidence"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "highly contextual, iterative, and ethically sensitive dataset tasks",
        "continuous compliance with evolving legal standards"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 71
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5095633-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "While these platforms offer incremental innovations in how contributors are evaluated and rewarded, they remain structurally insufficient for a fully decentralized \"Mechanical Turk\" model of large-scale AI dataset creation.",
      "text_sha256": "35f647818b65a9c8b5edd38fe4635a2464ae885e3556e8d59c315f3efba790c7",
      "source_sha256": "cbb484711f89bcefc9fc6a5730a1ed0a3f764d7999ad9b6f7d8ea05634c26c63",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5095633-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5095633-032",
      "text": "Linking every contributor action and every piece of data to on-chain governance elements within a structured graph is what enables real-time community oversight, iterative updates, and granular reputation tracking in the WDAG model.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "contributions and governance elements are recorded on chain"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 58
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5095633-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "By enabling every contributor action and piece of data to be linked to on-chain governance elements in a structured graph, the WDAG model supports real-time community oversight, iterative updates, and granular reputation tracking.",
      "text_sha256": "f5e932676708ce962ec8cf7c0d1feb15237c5078396ee537cf8f45b9f1028383",
      "source_sha256": "cbb484711f89bcefc9fc6a5730a1ed0a3f764d7999ad9b6f7d8ea05634c26c63",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5095633-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5095633-033",
      "text": "Reputation for AI dataset governance must be multi-dimensional rather than a single numeric score, which the author operationalizes as weighted nodes and directed edges in a WDAG.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "AI dataset governance requiring traceability and flexibility"
