      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "LER employs a bifurcated architecture: voucher-based rewards for brokerage-held equities and programmable, on-chain reward units for tokenized equities.",
      "text_sha256": "33026eb675d4df3a1398a88e6dd3f1475481b1788f4fc8b3b384d742363a1721",
      "source_sha256": "9f53a865e6f0e5424640779df8f9b50923cd7d05649301dd4cc727144749b6e6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5454054-003",
      "text": "Retailer-issued stablecoins operate as an onchain Eurodollar play: they decentralize the creation of dollar-denominated liquidity, which reduces transaction costs and disintermediates traditional banks and their fees.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "merchant issues a dollar-pegged token backed by reserves"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Retailer-issued stablecoins function as an onchain Eurodollar play that enables the decentralized creation of dollar-denominated liquidity, thus reducing transaction costs, and disintermediating traditional banking systems and their fees.",
      "text_sha256": "6a78f9c7bd922c0e13c9fd25ce5e53b7a6d72635e3a63255766511f4c3b1b158",
      "source_sha256": "9f53a865e6f0e5424640779df8f9b50923cd7d05649301dd4cc727144749b6e6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-006",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5454054-006",
      "text": "Because LER requires no lock-up of the underlying equity or token, it increases liquidity and reduces sell pressure on the underlying asset, unlike conventional staking-style loyalty schemes.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "defi"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "rewards accrue on the basis of verified holding duration rather than escrowed assets"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-006:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "But, LER does not require lock-ups for the underlying equity or token assets, thus increasing liquidity and reducing sell pressure on the underlying equity or token assets.",
      "text_sha256": "1a18f6fe45b0ac2792d950fbe9d63c14fe5689657c2995421b60cd9152f3e92b",
      "source_sha256": "9f53a865e6f0e5424640779df8f9b50923cd7d05649301dd4cc727144749b6e6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5454054-017",
      "text": "Verification of off-chain equities held in brokerage accounts is a core implementation obstacle for LER, and before tokenized listings it required comparatively complex hybrid pipelines using off-chain attestations and zero-knowledge proofs.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "citation-and-knowledge"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "equities held in traditional brokerage accounts rather than on-chain"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As such, it addresses a core implementation challenge for LER, that is, the verification of off-chain equities held in brokerage accounts. Previously that verification required comparatively complex hybrid pipelines involving off-chain attestations and privacy-preserving technologies like ZKPs.",
      "text_sha256": "904f47655092b344e83c5175e30f65a8e58002602606e9a0ef574dfb7dc085c6",
      "source_sha256": "9f53a865e6f0e5424640779df8f9b50923cd7d05649301dd4cc727144749b6e6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-021",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5454054-021",
      "text": "Making LER rewards utility-only and non-transferable, in the manner of soulbound tokens, is what keeps them functioning as loyalty incentives rather than speculative assets and is what aligns them with MiCA and SEC exemptions.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "securities-law"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "rewards issued as non-transferable credits or soulbound tokens"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-021:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Second, LER voucher rewards are utility-only and non-transferable, similar to soulbound tokens (SBTs). This ensures they function as voucher loyalty incentives rather than speculative assets, thus aligning with regulatory exemptions under MiCA and SEC frameworks.",
      "text_sha256": "2f96de3356bff52491d5aebf3d3666f540c44989e8462d44e2b9a10d82e60fc7",
      "source_sha256": "9f53a865e6f0e5424640779df8f9b50923cd7d05649301dd4cc727144749b6e6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-027",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5454054-027",
      "text": "A disciplined, jurisdiction-specific controls framework should be treated as a condition precedent to launching LER, not as a matter to be resolved after deployment.",
      "claim_type": "normative",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "compliance",
        "law-and-legal-systems"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "cross-border LER deployments"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-027:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "A disciplined, jurisdiction-specific controls framework should therefore be treated as a condition precedent to LER launch.",
      "text_sha256": "dc5e5e2df97db3f2dce455a5c63f38173ad3c3691be8807ee1fab127c02d699d",
      "source_sha256": "9f53a865e6f0e5424640779df8f9b50923cd7d05649301dd4cc727144749b6e6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5454054-031",
      "text": "LER must maintain a visible separation between equity tenure verification and reward attribution, so that vouchers operate as loyalty entitlements and do not represent equities, dividends, or profit shares.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "securities-law",
        "systemic-risk"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "holding period used only as a trigger, not as a claim on returns"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-031:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "A key legal compliance strategy for LER is maintaining an obvious separation between equity tenure verification and reward attribution. This separation ensures voucher loyalty rewards function as loyalty entitlements without representing equities, dividends, or profit shares.",
      "text_sha256": "ede0e2553bde993c918fcfd2dc96f9347a5021e121ded31f4aaae229dc13576e",
      "source_sha256": "9f53a865e6f0e5424640779df8f9b50923cd7d05649301dd4cc727144749b6e6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-032",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5454054-032",
      "text": "Because Landreth holds that instruments carrying equity attributes such as dividends or voting rights are securities, LER rewards cannot include any such features and must function as independent loyalty perks.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "securities-law",
        "systemic-risk",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "United States securities law"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-032:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This is reinforced by SEC v. Landreth Timber Co. (1985), where the court held that stock sales are securities if they carry equity attributes like dividends or voting rights. Therefore, LER rewards cannot include such features.",
      "text_sha256": "f247353b5c10783caca4f790944f38d3b9ec0c85b1339e37d05c8367106258f4",
      "source_sha256": "9f53a865e6f0e5424640779df8f9b50923cd7d05649301dd4cc727144749b6e6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5454054-033",
      "text": "AML obligations for LER should be right-sized: zero-knowledge proofs or anonymized attestations should minimize identity collection for non-transferable rewards, with VASP-grade measures applied only where transferability exists.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "compliance",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "citation-and-knowledge"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "non-transferable rewards versus transferable rewards",
        "GDPR privacy obligations apply"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "LER should employ ZKPs or anonymized attestations to minimize identity collection for non-transferable rewards, applying VASP-grade measures only where transferability exists, balancing compliance with GDPR privacy obligations.",
      "text_sha256": "b810a60cc6c486547835fdfc1b6552a6c10d47c674e9d5dcea62818473cf3d33",
      "source_sha256": "9f53a865e6f0e5424640779df8f9b50923cd7d05649301dd4cc727144749b6e6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5454054-036",
      "text": "Before launch, an LER program requires a defined governance package: classification memoranda, financial promotions review, data protection impact assessments, an MSB or EMI evaluation, and consumer terms and conditions.",
      "claim_type": "normative",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "systemic-risk"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "pre-launch stage of an LER program"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5454054-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This involves several key preparatory steps before launch: drafting classification memoranda, conducting reviews of financial promotions, performing data protection impact assessments (DPIAs),",
      "text_sha256": "7d5fd330ea8606620ed50953d47385fd70938f1091c43a8b9b1ac703b67ee8cd",
      "source_sha256": "9f53a865e6f0e5424640779df8f9b50923cd7d05649301dd4cc727144749b6e6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-010",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5541658-010",
      "text": "The Shenzhen courts illustrate a workable three step human-in-the-loop design for generative judicial AI: the judge decides first, the LLM generates the supporting reasoning, and the judge then revises that output to finalize the judgment.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Chinese courts using LLMs to draft judicial opinions"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-010:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "A notable case study from Shenzhen, China, illustrates a three-step interaction pattern: judges make initial decisions, LLMs generate reasoning based on these decisions, and judges revise the output to finalize judgments.",
      "text_sha256": "2ab83998bf62e9a0df48a5612d85e6c022ebbeaaa0e586ec7b76c7032ecf34f1",
      "source_sha256": "e543a2d698fcd522d4d02e034cc9ee1344d0015d2c824b40b9e05ab7c0728c60",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-011",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5541658-011",
      "text": "Accuracy alone is insufficient for legal AI: a model must also be explainable before its outputs can be trusted in judicial settings.",
      "claim_type": "normative",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "predictive AI used in legal and judicial applications"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 70
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-011:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Accuracy alone is insufficient without explainability.",
      "text_sha256": "bd4507bc04f4399dba9807d9e2423ae36a8208af7b1b24a7849c1560f3316443",
      "source_sha256": "e543a2d698fcd522d4d02e034cc9ee1344d0015d2c824b40b9e05ab7c0728c60",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5541658-012",
      "text": "Post hoc explainability techniques do not by themselves establish trustworthiness; the explanations they produce must additionally be verified against human knowledge.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "post hoc explainable AI methods such as the SHAP family of explainers"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 72
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, post-hoc explainers still need to be verified for trustworthiness, in that the explanations comport with human knowledge.",
      "text_sha256": "80309849fe451b30d52281bedeeac9459502e726a5ab2b902a6b137c5171214b",
      "source_sha256": "e543a2d698fcd522d4d02e034cc9ee1344d0015d2c824b40b9e05ab7c0728c60",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5541658-013",
      "text": "Bias in judicial AI arises because models are trained on historical data that reflect past inequities, and the standard remedy of fairness through unawareness, meaning the omission of protected characteristics such as race, fails because proxy variables continue to correlate with the omitted attribute.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "education-and-practice"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "machine learning models trained on historical judicial data"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This bias arises because AI models rely on historical data that reflect past inequities, and even attempts at \"fairness through unawareness\" (omitting protected characteristics like race) fail due to proxy variables that correlate with bias.",
      "text_sha256": "0a0a379f2a33d6b79e0acb27c929c39a73951c206e760798a372f1e5b6f068cf",
      "source_sha256": "e543a2d698fcd522d4d02e034cc9ee1344d0015d2c824b40b9e05ab7c0728c60",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5541658-015",
      "text": "Transparent, explainable models such as those built for the European Court of Human Rights, which paired 97% accuracy with digestible explanations, provide the design template for addressing legal AI's transparency problem.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "disclosure"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "systems using computational models of argument to generate legally grounded explanations"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Transparent, explainable AI models, such as those developed for the ECHR, which achieved 97% accuracy with digestible explanations, offer a model for addressing these concerns.",
      "text_sha256": "29d1835617112627969f5e5a5994a50aadaa2533ef2e74d115aa567c4115bfe3",
      "source_sha256": "e543a2d698fcd522d4d02e034cc9ee1344d0015d2c824b40b9e05ab7c0728c60",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5541658-016",
      "text": "Keeping judges ultimately accountable through a human-in-the-loop review of AI generated reasoning, as practiced in Shenzhen, does not fully resolve the accountability problem in AI assisted adjudication.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "law-and-legal-systems"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "judicial settings where AI drafts or supports reasoning that a human judge then reviews"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Shenzhen case study illustrates that judges retain ultimate accountability, revising AI-generated reasoning to ensure accurate judgments, but this human-in-the-loop approach does not fully resolve the issue.",
      "text_sha256": "2239e800ea72adc4f4aaf4a373b577023369ca7c3800835f382dcfe825ea1f74",
      "source_sha256": "e543a2d698fcd522d4d02e034cc9ee1344d0015d2c824b40b9e05ab7c0728c60",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5541658-019",
      "text": "Because AI cannot fully interpret cultural or socioeconomic factors that human judges naturally weigh, it can produce outputs that are technically accurate yet contextually deficient, and this degrades the quality of justice.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "cases where cultural or socioeconomic context bears on the outcome"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 46
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5541658-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As a result, AI may produce technically accurate but contextually deficient outputs, undermining the quality of justice.",
      "text_sha256": "dfe0475e91a5ddd832026de37bc2b3ecc2110cd494709c1344d3168198760483",
      "source_sha256": "e543a2d698fcd522d4d02e034cc9ee1344d0015d2c824b40b9e05ab7c0728c60",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
