      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5554218-023:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "We argue that the absence of accountability mechanisms in anonymous, automated smart contracts encourages a \"take the money and run\" mentality, necessitating a historical record of conduct and incentives for ethical behavior.",
      "text_sha256": "0027138c9f2a7962e11ebe30d9af7e47af085630a272f661f4372cc8942ad03a",
      "source_sha256": "55738b4035a91b70aa2ddaa127552fe4b373ec641afee2719fbdcabebdcbea44",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5554218-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5554218-024",
      "text": "The deterministic execution of smart contracts rigidly enforces coded terms and thereby incentivizes participants to exploit loopholes for immediate gain, because no mechanism exists to adapt the rules contextually.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "regulatory-failure",
        "smart-contracts",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "smart contracts without on chain amendment or human review mechanisms"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5554218-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Conversely, smart contracts' deterministic execution rigidly enforces coded terms, incentivizing participants to exploit loopholes for immediate gain, as there is no mechanism to adapt rules contextually.",
      "text_sha256": "808c1cdf1faa272bfe90b387b93429b7a3cb5327d9739951bd519f7d2a02b17e",
      "source_sha256": "55738b4035a91b70aa2ddaa127552fe4b373ec641afee2719fbdcabebdcbea44",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5554218-028",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5554218-028",
      "text": "Unilateral regulation of artificial intelligence by a single jurisdiction produces global ripple effects, but that approach reaches its limits because AI systems remain accessible worldwide over the internet.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "AI models distributed globally over the internet",
        "regulation by a single jurisdiction"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 54
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5554218-028:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "clear that unilateral regulation by one jurisdiction can have global ripple effects. However, this approach faces limitations when AI systems are accessible globally via the internet.",
      "text_sha256": "545eae0e7c0b93ac125460ba7c417f532e779b22935ea27f787cab44ab6c30f7",
      "source_sha256": "55738b4035a91b70aa2ddaa127552fe4b373ec641afee2719fbdcabebdcbea44",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5554218-036",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5554218-036",
      "text": "Allowing jurisdictions to tailor smart contract requirements to local statutory frameworks while adhering to a baseline of ethical principles preserves the innovative potential of blockchain by avoiding the homogenizing effects of harmonized legal standards.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "governance-design",
        "innovation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "hybrid governance combining a universal ethical baseline with localized adaptation"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5554218-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This flexibility preserves the innovative potential of blockchain by avoiding the homogenizing effects of harmonized legal standards, which could stifle jurisdictional experimentation.",
      "text_sha256": "747ede08d21aaa3142e37d832829d2c5a10e2e7817e494f294a9a1a2483ca863",
      "source_sha256": "55738b4035a91b70aa2ddaa127552fe4b373ec641afee2719fbdcabebdcbea44",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:5554218-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/5554218-037",
      "text": "A reputation system in which participants who act in good faith earn reputation credits and those acting opportunistically face penalties mitigates the take the money and run mentality that anonymity otherwise fosters.",
