    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/617681-003",
      "text": "The Societas Europaea has drawn a less than enthusiastic initial reaction, plausibly because its rules are the product of years of negotiation and political compromise rather than a response to market forces.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "the SE as of 2004, shortly before it entered into force"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 10
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "It has yet to be seen whether managers and investors view the SE as a viable alternative, but initial reaction has been less than enthusiastic, perhaps because the rules governing an SE are the product of years of negotiation and political compromise rather than a response to market forces.",
      "text_sha256": "ac475e77945ee6e195f4723eb0925d2019dcab51310124da4072a4d0efefe22d",
      "source_sha256": "e142130507ea2f5b025fd97b3f762d44ee3a7aaa82b155aab63434b85e8fd834",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/617681-008",
      "text": "Regulatory competition for a bundled product of statutes plus courts is only a realistic possibility if relatively high supply side hurdles can be overcome to induce states to enter the market for corporate law.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "markets for a bundled corporate law product"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 11
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In sum, regulatory competition for a bundled product is only a realistic possibility if relatively high supply side hurdles can be overcome to induce states to enter the market for corporate law.",
      "text_sha256": "2a761cc7c054cf02eec4f2badf4851c76de6ad9c58c2c6fd46959e35737a2f13",
      "source_sha256": "e142130507ea2f5b025fd97b3f762d44ee3a7aaa82b155aab63434b85e8fd834",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/617681-009",
      "text": "A jurisdiction supplying corporate law as an unbundled statutory product faces low fixed costs, principally statute drafting, and near zero marginal costs, because additional users impose no new adjudication costs and registration costs are insignificant.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "tokenomics",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "statutes offered without adjudication by the state of incorporation"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Fixed investment would be principally in drafting statutes. Each additional user of the jurisdiction's corporate law would not impose new adjudication costs, and the cost of registering additional corporate charters are relatively insignificant.",
      "text_sha256": "4ba3ce6a0b211e9d992dddd59e57fcc64fd6af9f8d66548561ff0769e2b52113",
      "source_sha256": "e142130507ea2f5b025fd97b3f762d44ee3a7aaa82b155aab63434b85e8fd834",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-013",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/617681-013",
      "text": "To the extent adjudication over U.K. corporate law is expected to take place outside the U.K., the U.K. has not in fact exported a bundled product; its users are demonstrating a preference for an unbundled package.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "small closely held enterprises incorporating in the U.K. after Inspire Art"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-013:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "To the extent adjudication over U.K. corporate law is expected to be carried out somewhere other than the U.K. the U.K. has not exported a bundled product at all.",
      "text_sha256": "b675f9befad80c80a032c194ae2af70b9a9061bba0ce9cd92960bf7b061e7604",
      "source_sha256": "e142130507ea2f5b025fd97b3f762d44ee3a7aaa82b155aab63434b85e8fd834",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/617681-015",
      "text": "Member States unwilling to incur the rule switching costs of conducting judicial proceedings in English could be precluded from marketing their corporate charters in other Member States that do not share their language.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "English being the only language widely understood throughout the EU"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Member States unwilling to incur the rule switching costs involved with using English in judicial proceedings could be precluded from marketing their corporate charters in other Member States that do not speak the same language.",
      "text_sha256": "49c6781df9963de032c958e259d786d79e3701cd55decd408bec33f36004da0b",
      "source_sha256": "e142130507ea2f5b025fd97b3f762d44ee3a7aaa82b155aab63434b85e8fd834",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-033",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/617681-033",
      "text": "Forum unbundling is the arrangement in which the incorporation jurisdiction's statutes and interpretive case law are unbundled only from the adjudication services of its courts, so corporations may choose a different adjudicator in their charters.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The second alternative is \"forum unbundling\" in which the incorporation jurisdiction's statutes and interpretive caselaw are unbundled from the adjudication services of its courts. Corporations may in their charters choose an adjudicator other than the courts of the state of incorporation.",
      "text_sha256": "c0627624702333bc2c3d225679ca11fa354116c586f902453ad26c96b935f252",
      "source_sha256": "e142130507ea2f5b025fd97b3f762d44ee3a7aaa82b155aab63434b85e8fd834",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-034",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/617681-034",
      "text": "None of the Delaware based solutions, whether importing bundled or unbundled Delaware law, is likely to be viable for Europe.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "the four options canvassed: Delaware charters, partial copying, wholesale statutory copying, and copying statutes plus case law"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-034:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "For all of the above mentioned reasons, it is likely that none of the \"Delaware based\" solutions, whether involving bundled or unbundled Delaware law, is viable for Europe.",
      "text_sha256": "5b22844d70f4ff18fc754951f479f61de56f9b585fae5f7dd081f87f86746c58",
      "source_sha256": "e142130507ea2f5b025fd97b3f762d44ee3a7aaa82b155aab63434b85e8fd834",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/617681-038",
      "text": "Arbitration of corporate governance disputes has not emerged in the United States because arbitration is at best the next best alternative to Delaware, and a second place finish does not justify the investment needed to design a workable arbitration framework.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "United States, where Delaware's adjudication system commands high confidence"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Arbitration of corporate law disputes may be the next best alternative to Delaware, but a second place finish in regulatory competition probably does not justify the investment needed to design an arbitration framework that overcomes many of Coffee's specific objections.",
      "text_sha256": "320e7e026ffdfd5e472e9f11bc59d26e7749ee4f0b1d8af058412bde630c07f6",
      "source_sha256": "e142130507ea2f5b025fd97b3f762d44ee3a7aaa82b155aab63434b85e8fd834",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-042",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/617681-042",
      "text": "Unless the Member State of incorporation specifically provides in its corporate statute that arbitration is permissible when allowed in the charter or a shareholders agreement, investors run the risk that courts refuse to enforce the arbitration provision.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "closely held corporations may rely on a shareholders agreement instead of the charter"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-042:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "specifically provide in its corporate statute that arbitration is permissible if allowed in either the corporate charter or (for a closely held corporation) in a shareholders' agreement. Otherwise, investors run the risk that courts refuse to enforce the arbitration provision.",
      "text_sha256": "d368a55735d7a36e58b29bc687bad3a3eec71a919ba4af0432501d2abaeea750",
      "source_sha256": "e142130507ea2f5b025fd97b3f762d44ee3a7aaa82b155aab63434b85e8fd834",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:617681-043",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/617681-043",
      "text": "Empirically, at least 48 companies with German names carrying the GmbH designation were formed as private limited companies under U.K. law in the ten months after the Inspire Art decision, indicating that charter migration accelerated after the ruling.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "governance-design",
        "empirical-evidence"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "some of these companies may also do business in the U.K. or be affiliated with a German GmbH"
