      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 57
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "First, the identity problem: Reputation systems built on persistent identity5 collapse when agents can costlessly create new identities. A poorly-performing agent simply abandons their account and starts fresh, a phenomenon known as whitewashing.6",
      "text_sha256": "006d94674b46b6bb7cad0bf110adbd201270a4f8cef66b1e33883a1b744c7c07",
      "source_sha256": "b04292561ee041e0c9eaa7eca28a410ed440e76a95743a539361a3f76c97f2b3",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-008",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6192998-008",
      "text": "Current agent platforms are inadequate on both horns: centralized rating systems defeat the purpose of agent autonomy, while primitive token staking mechanisms produce binary outcomes and fail to capture knowledge graphs.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "economics",
        "citation-and-knowledge"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "AI agent marketplaces and comparable decentralized collaboration platforms"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 53
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-008:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Current platforms either use centralized rating systems (defeating the purpose of agent autonomy) or primitive token-staking mechanisms (producing binary outcomes and failing to capture knowledge graphs).",
      "text_sha256": "3ffd08af95d47ee28bcdcffe9dc4810f387ce059f7ca04f13a4fb05ce4f8a67a",
      "source_sha256": "b04292561ee041e0c9eaa7eca28a410ed440e76a95743a539361a3f76c97f2b3",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-012",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6192998-012",
      "text": "Selecting a single agent per job by weighted random draw sacrifices quality assurance for efficiency, reflecting a broader pattern in DAO governance where efficiency optimization crowds out quality.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "economics",
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 58
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-012:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Problem 2: Single agent selection. The system randomly picks one agent per job, even if having multiple agents compete would improve quality. This reflects a broader pattern I have observed in DAO governance: efficiency optimization often sacrifices quality assurance.",
      "text_sha256": "866b1960136b3bc5789a984b71b756043794a09d4102a258e50fd1ac4369d9ca",
      "source_sha256": "b04292561ee041e0c9eaa7eca28a410ed440e76a95743a539361a3f76c97f2b3",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6192998-019",
      "text": "Multi agent competitive collaboration captures a diversity dividend worth more than half a standard deviation of quality improvement while enabling attribution through citation graphs.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "economics",
        "empirical-evidence",
        "citation-and-knowledge"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "quality approximately normally distributed across competing agents",
        "competition size of roughly three to seven agents"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 48
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Our multi-agent competitive collaboration protocol captures diversity dividends worth 0.5+ standard deviations of quality improvement while enabling attribution through citation graphs.",
      "text_sha256": "c848b9f410ce25f2199c838096676bac21ba7c73da5b8d5ef546aa07939b445e",
      "source_sha256": "b04292561ee041e0c9eaa7eca28a410ed440e76a95743a539361a3f76c97f2b3",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-020",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6192998-020",
      "text": "The real barrier to multi agent competition is not cost but the absence of an attribution mechanism: if only the best of several competing agents is paid, the others have no incentive to participate, so competition requires rewards proportional to each contributor's contribution.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "economics",
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "multiple agents competing on the same job"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-020:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The real barrier is the lack of attribution mechanism. If 5 agents compete but only the best gets paid, the other 4 have no incentive to participate. We need a framework where all contributors can be rewarded proportional to their contribution.",
      "text_sha256": "48ae1e3238264ec59c6a4335f8eee25f9c5fdb8ddfd88be8166aa7a215506ca2",
      "source_sha256": "b04292561ee041e0c9eaa7eca28a410ed440e76a95743a539361a3f76c97f2b3",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-023",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6192998-023",
      "text": "AI and DAO convergence requires machine readable governance structures that preserve semantic richness, and binary validation outcomes fail that requirement fundamentally.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "dao",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "AI agent ecosystems participating in organizational decision making"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 58
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-023:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "As I have argued,48 AI-DAO convergence requires machine-readable governance structures that preserve semantic richness. Binary outcomes fail this requirement fundamentally.",
      "text_sha256": "fcd2df78fa3d0431fe919d10c0de3b459e4ff3dba4e5556b53e99f255454af32",
      "source_sha256": "b04292561ee041e0c9eaa7eca28a410ed440e76a95743a539361a3f76c97f2b3",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-029",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6192998-029",
      "text": "Validators who align with the stake weighted consensus ranking gain reputation and those who deviate lose it, which carries the winner takes losers' stakes property of the original framework over to ranked voting.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "validator agreement measured by normalized Kendall tau distance from consensus"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 48
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-029:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Validators who align with consensus gain reputation. Those who deviate lose it. Thus, preserving the winner-takes-losers'-stakes property from the original framework (Calcaterra, Kaal, and Andrei 2018, 7) while extending it to ranked voting.",
      "text_sha256": "3905c9dbe34fe4f0380764b5270d89fb92cc501fc909e01e75b767fdadd8bcd8",
      "source_sha256": "b04292561ee041e0c9eaa7eca28a410ed440e76a95743a539361a3f76c97f2b3",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6192998-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6192998-031",
      "text": "Formal mechanism design alone is insufficient for decentralized systems; the security analysis depends on honest agents also detecting citation rings, downranking colluding submissions, and applying penalties, so formal mechanisms must be combined with emergent social enforcement.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
