    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6269518-001",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6269518-001",
      "text": "Under existing citation-weighted reputation formulations, rational agents face a direct financial disincentive to cite prior contributions, because PageRank-derived value allocation transfers economic reward from the citing agent to the cited agent.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation",
        "dao",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "citation-weighted value allocation through PageRank-derived mechanisms",
        "agents are rational and self interested"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 84
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6269518-001:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Under existing formulations, rational agents face a direct financial disincentive to cite prior contributions, as citation-weighted value allocation through PageRank-derived mechanisms transfers economic reward from the citing agent to the cited agent.",
      "text_sha256": "7018c81163dab747d40ec9ba9580ce6fbabdebdf4cfd069a01b1f7db32efff1e",
      "source_sha256": "f096ecf5b41bb9ae8642facd54b9149c7b594de53a1cc32718a4d806b772f88f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6269518-002",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6269518-002",
      "text": "Because citation integrity determines both economic reward and governance power in on-chain reputation systems, the citation mechanism is a load bearing structural element of the entire governance architecture rather than an academic courtesy.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "reputation",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation tokens are minted and allocated based on perceived value of contributions",
        "perceived value depends on how later work references prior work"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 53
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6269518-002:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "and when the perceived value of contributions is itself a function of how subsequent work references prior work, the integrity of the citation mechanism becomes a load-bearing structural element of the entire governance architecture.",
      "text_sha256": "b0cd3a6a10cad4a043331038f239bbdeed45eea91ca9c8537ec14b3eb2b91e15",
      "source_sha256": "f096ecf5b41bb9ae8642facd54b9149c7b594de53a1cc32718a4d806b772f88f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6269518-003",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6269518-003",
      "text": "Citation-weighted payment mechanisms as currently formulated will systematically erode the quality of knowledge attribution in any decentralized reputation system if the incentive misalignment is left unaddressed.",
      "claim_type": "predictive",
      "topics": [
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "decentralization"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "the incentive misalignment remains unaddressed"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 61
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6269518-003:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This paper demonstrates, however, that citation-weighted payment mechanisms as currently formulated contain a fundamental incentive misalignment that, if left unaddressed, will systematically erode the quality of knowledge attribution in any decentralized reputation system.",
      "text_sha256": "36ca06e7e01e576ff1eb0ad4ab63066af57278fe725f70d336858b988c3fd2c2",
      "source_sha256": "f096ecf5b41bb9ae8642facd54b9149c7b594de53a1cc32718a4d806b772f88f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6269518-011",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6269518-011",
      "text": "The citation-weighted payment mechanism in multi-agent settings effectively operates with an implicit leaching parameter of one, since every unit of citation-weighted value conferred on another agent is a unit lost to the citing agent, which is a maximally punitive setting.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "multi-agent citation-weighted payment settings"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6269518-011:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The citation-weighted payment mechanism in multi-agent settings effectively operates with an implicit q4 = 1: every unit of citation-weighted value conferred on another agent is a unit lost to the citing agent. This is a maximally punitive leaching parameter,",
      "text_sha256": "6fb54df6b5d69476a7a84b9e028a6b6f9bfa7a2367a9dc6dbcecb44cc2fbc4d3",
      "source_sha256": "f096ecf5b41bb9ae8642facd54b9149c7b594de53a1cc32718a4d806b772f88f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6269518-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/6269518-015",
      "text": "A PageRank-derived value distribution is only as honest as its inputs, and those inputs are generated by agents with a direct incentive to distort them, so relying entirely on the calculation to distribute value correctly fails.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "citation-and-knowledge",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:6269518-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The framework relies entirely on the PageRank calculation to \"correctly\" distribute value, but the PageRank calculation is only as honest as its inputs. And the inputs are generated by agents with a direct incentive to distort them.",
      "text_sha256": "81006b8b09c62a38ed6daccab21adad26a28682428a7489ddd7aa39ac3950a9b",
      "source_sha256": "f096ecf5b41bb9ae8642facd54b9149c7b594de53a1cc32718a4d806b772f88f",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
