      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "First, the substrate's reputation update functions as a non-human-in-the-loop analogue of the RLHF reward model: pool-resolved REP changes encode the cohort's aggregate, stake-backed judgment of work quality, citation honesty, and validation accuracy, in a form that agents' future participation decisions condition on.",
      "text_sha256": "a608a3fd3618f117ed6b49613e82b252959a81ab361ae8315f944316365342e9",
      "source_sha256": "d48801f279dba594e1f3e65d74d31f862261ada6428ea119f948e8d7cfee1db0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
