    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:7314479-033:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The permission model records that per-agent tool access and per-agent internet access are not yet implemented, and that consequently all tools are available to all agents. Granting an agent access to a single Vault box therefore grants it the ability to invoke every installed tool, whose union of declared domains defines the true outbound surface. The user approves permissions tool by tool and receives their composition without ever seeing it.",
      "text_sha256": "80d3c79d2ecc0256ce693e51a3f4a47c5f173a88c82a5b6c245e4c4bfad0f66d",
      "source_sha256": "debace24a155ae924a155b1fafe98856d98cf83689feff2f87a32f1c06171ce6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:7314479-040",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/7314479-040",
      "text": "Hash chaining each Chronicle entry to its predecessor with a persisted per-tool head digest makes any modification, deletion, or reordering of history break the chain at a determinable point, at the cost of one hash per append.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "open-source-and-code",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "a minimal delta against the Mosaic design at commit 2d920ce"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 52
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:7314479-040:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Give each entry a digest over its own content and its predecessor's digest, and persist the current head digest per tool. Append cost is one hash. Verification is a linear scan. Any modification, deletion, or reordering of history breaks the chain at a determinable point.",
      "text_sha256": "aa22e268b251320554b6d1593f8aafcbe06d508c02cf6a6996795406f5b9b541",
      "source_sha256": "debace24a155ae924a155b1fafe98856d98cf83689feff2f87a32f1c06171ce6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:7314479-041",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/7314479-041",
      "text": "Reputation standing should anchor to the SHA-256 of the tool artifact, paired with a publisher-level link and a controlled migration rule under which standing carries across versions only by an explicit, recorded act.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "introduction of a reputation layer into a sovereign runtime"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 67
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:7314479-041:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Hash-bound standing therefore needs a publisher-level link and a controlled migration rule, under which standing carries across versions only by an explicit, recorded act. The identity-cost precondition Part IX names is met by that pairing, not by the hash alone.",
      "text_sha256": "acaa8a73c198072afc9d6a9cac0db316d16176e2b3673af9b6e7f93590010378",
      "source_sha256": "debace24a155ae924a155b1fafe98856d98cf83689feff2f87a32f1c06171ce6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:7314479-043",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/7314479-043",
      "text": "Among institutions governing counterparty selection, contract, regulation, and brand each fail at machine speed, leaving reputation as the portable, cumulative, continuously updated summary of past conduct a counterparty can evaluate before transacting.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "economics",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "counterparty selection among autonomous software components"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 55
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:7314479-043:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Contract requires negotiation and enforcement, both of which are slow and expensive relative to the transaction sizes characteristic of agent interaction. Regulation requires jurisdiction, which is unavailable where the parties are software components of uncertain domicile. Brand requires an audience with memory and attention, neither of which an agent possesses. What remains is reputation: a portable, cumulative, and continuously updated summary of past conduct that a counterparty can evaluate in the time available before transacting.",
      "text_sha256": "c8839af32c533a3e15cf9db48852dda83b3bdb7339b481c07a92b03a0d32a301",
      "source_sha256": "debace24a155ae924a155b1fafe98856d98cf83689feff2f87a32f1c06171ce6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:7314479-047",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/7314479-047",
      "text": "In a sovereign runtime no operator is positioned to intervene, so the reputation layer is the institution of last resort and must be built to bear that weight from the beginning.",
      "claim_type": "normative",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "institutional-design",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "sovereign local agent runtimes without a platform operator"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 55
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:7314479-047:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In a sovereign runtime there is no operator positioned to intervene. The reputation layer is therefore not a convenience feature. It is the institution of last resort, and it must be built to bear that weight from the beginning.",
      "text_sha256": "23a61a791ebe21aa93b1cd385fb5c824dc4b16dfc464e5fb4e468571bd9ccd4f",
      "source_sha256": "debace24a155ae924a155b1fafe98856d98cf83689feff2f87a32f1c06171ce6",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
